 = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\"_combo_arc_utils\", ROOT / \"solvers\" / \"arc_utils.py\")\n+    _mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(_spec)\n+    assert _spec.loader is not None\n+    _spec.loader.exec_module(_mod)\n+    bbox_coords = _mod.bbox_coords\n+    components_mask = _mod.components_mask\n+    get_bg = _mod.get_bg\n+    paste = _mod.paste\n+    random_free_location = _mod.random_free_location\n \n # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n-# Design analysis for the fused D7/2 + D13/0 variant\n+# Design analysis for the combo variant\n #\n # a) Concrete behavior and trace:\n-#    - Keep the original large gray frame with solid-color placeholder blocks inside.\n-#    - Keep one outside sprite template per placeholder color; each sprite still uses the\n-#      placeholder color and has the same N x N bbox as the matching blocks inside the frame.\n-#    - Replace the old overlapping two-color legend with a top-left strip of monochrome\n-#      count codes. Each code is a compact 3x3 nested stencil whose area is the key and\n-#      whose color is the recolor target.\n-#    - Add 1-2 extra legend entries whose counts do not match any real sprite. Those entries\n-#      are visible in the same strip, so solver must count every sprite, compare that count\n-#      against all legend entries, and ignore the unmatched ones.\n-#    - Example: suppose a cyan external sprite occupies exactly 5 cells in a 4x4 bbox, while\n-#      the legend strip contains orange-5, red-7, yellow-3, and teal-8 entries. Cyan blocks\n-#      inside the frame become the 5-cell sprite recolored to orange. The 7/3/8 entries stay\n-#      unused if no sprite has those counts. In the original task, recoloring came from a\n-#      direct shape-color legend pair; here it comes from sprite area, and some legend items\n-#      are decoys.\n+#    - Keep the original backbone: one gray rectangular frame, solid placeholder blocks\n+#      inside the frame, and one source-colored sprite template outside the frame for each\n+#      placeholder color.\n+#    - Replace the original overlapping two-color legend with a fixed top-left legend strip.\n+#      Each legend entry is now a compact monochrome stencil whose area encodes a number.\n+#      The legend color is the output color, while the number of colored pixels is the key.\n+#    - Add mandatory distractor legend entries. These extra count codes are rendered exactly\n+#      like the real legend entries but their pixel counts do not match any real sprite area.\n+#    - Example: suppose blue placeholders correspond to a 4x4 outside sprite with exactly\n+#      5 colored cells, and green placeholders correspond to a 4x4 sprite with 3 cells.\n+#      The legend may show orange=5 cells, red=3 cells, and yellow=6 cells. The solver must\n+#      count the blue sprite, match 5 to orange, count the green sprite, match 3 to red,\n+#      and ignore the yellow 6-cell legend item. In the original task, recoloring came from\n+#      direct shape-color legend pairs; in this fusion, recoloring requires count matching\n+#      plus filtering unmatched legend counts.\n #\n # b) Complexity calibration:\n-#    - Real sprite counts are unique and chosen from a small visual vocabulary 2..8. This\n-#      keeps counting tractable while still giving enough room for distractors.\n-#    - There are 2-5 placeholder colors, so each sample has repeated evidence inside the frame\n-#      but not so many codes that the top legend becomes unreadable.\n-#    - Distractors are mandatory but capped at 1-2, which makes the extra filtering visible\n-#      without drowning out the true legend entries.\n+#    - Restrict real sprite areas to a small vocabulary {2,3,4,5,6,7}. This makes counting\n+#      observable, while still leaving room for 1-2 unmatched legend counts in the same band.\n+#    - Limit the number of placeholder colors to 2-4. That preserves repeated evidence inside\n+#      the frame and avoids exhausting the count vocabulary once distractors are added.\n+#    - Keep sprite boxes at 3x3 or 4x4. Larger boxes would make exact counting slower and add\n+#      clutter; smaller boxes would not support enough distinct counted patterns.\n #\n-# c) Implicit assumption audit against the original solver:\n-#    - Old legend parsing assumed overlapping two-color glyphs and source-color inference from\n-#      pair structure. That breaks completely; fused solver instead reads monochrome entries\n-#      anchored on the top row and uses component area as the code.\n-#    - Old sprite extraction only had to exclude legend components paired by overlap. That is\n-#      no longer valid because legend entries now have a single color and may share colors with\n-#      real sprites. The generator therefore reserves the whole top band for legends, and the\n-#      solver excludes all top-band components from sprite recovery.\n-#    - Count-based recoloring only works if different placeholder colors do not share the same\n-#      sprite area. The generator guarantees unique real counts, and solver asserts that.\n-#    - Distractors are only safe if their counts are distinct from all real counts. The\n-#      generator enforces that; solver checks that legend counts form a strict superset of\n-#      sprite counts rather than an arbitrary unrelated set.\n+# c) Implicit-assumption audit against the original solver:\n+#    - Original legend parsing assumed small overlapping two-color regions; that is no longer\n+#      true. The new solver instead assumes every outside component touching row 0 is part of\n+#      the top legend strip.\n+#    - Original source->target mapping was indexed by placeholder color. That assumption is\n+#      broken by D7/2: color now only selects which sprite to stamp, while legend lookup is\n+#      keyed by sprite area.\n+#    - Original code expected every parsed legend item to be relevant. D13/0 breaks that too:\n+#      the new solver must recover all real sprite areas first, then use only legend counts\n+#      that match those areas.\n+#    - Sparse counted sprites may be 4-disconnected, so extraction cannot rely on one single\n+#      connected component spanning the full bbox. The solver unions all non-legend components\n+#      of the same source color and checks the union bbox against the placeholder size.\n #\n # d) Placement legality:\n-#    - The top band is reserved before frame placement, so no sprite or frame cell can touch\n-#      the legend strip.\n-#    - Frame, external sprites, and legend entries are all placed with a one-cell padding gap\n-#      via `random_free_location`, preventing overlap or accidental touching.\n-#    - Sprite masks always include opposite corners of the N x N bbox, so the union bbox seen\n-#      by the solver exactly matches the placeholder block size even when the sprite is sparse\n-#      or disconnected.\n+#    - The generator reserves a top band for legends, preventing sprite/frame collisions with\n+#      legend entries and guaranteeing that row-0 colored components are legends only.\n+#    - `random_free_location` with one-cell padding separates the frame, legend strip, and\n+#      all outside sprites, so no objects touch or overlap.\n+#    - Sprite masks always include opposite corners of their NxN box, ensuring that the union\n+#      bbox exactly matches the placeholder block size even when the mask is disconnected.\n #\n # e) Visual observability:\n-#    - A human can recover the rule by counting cells in an outside sprite, then scanning the\n-#      top strip for the legend entry with the same count to get the output color.\n-#    - The extra legend items are not hidden metadata; they are visible unmatched counts in the\n-#      same legend family, so the added reasoning load is observable from the grids alone.\n+#    - A human can inspect the outside sprite for one placeholder color, count its colored\n+#      cells, and then look for the same count in the top-left legend to infer the recolor.\n+#    - The distractor dimension is visible because the legend contains more count entries than\n+#      there are actual sprite areas. These extras cannot be dismissed by shape alone; they\n+#      must be excluded by exact counting.\n #\n # f) Visual cleanliness:\n-#    - Legends live in one dedicated band, the frame occupies one compact rectangle elsewhere,\n-#      and sprites are separate free patches. This keeps object categories spatially separated.\n-#    - All legend entries share one simple 3x3 encoding template, reducing clutter compared with\n-#      arbitrary glyphs or mixed overlay patterns.\n+#    - All legend entries share one strip at the top. All sprites live below that strip.\n+#      The frame is placed away from both via the reserve mask, so the scene stays segmented.\n+#    - Each legend entry is monochrome and compact, with a single background gap between\n+#      entries. This keeps the distractors legible without introducing another border motif.\n #\n # g) Change inferability:\n-#    - Output colors are structurally indicated by the legend-entry colors, not by raw palette\n-#      ids. Because counts repeat via multiple placeholders of the same color, a few samples are\n-#      enough to show that equal source colors do not determine output colors on their own.\n-#    - Distractors do not affect placed objects, so the solver must infer that only counts seen\n-#      on real sprites are actionable.\n+#    - Output colors remain directly visible in the legend, but only after inferring which\n+#      count entries are live. Because placeholder colors repeat and each source color has\n+#      one repeated sprite template, 2-4 samples are enough to see that count equality, not\n+#      shape identity or legend order, drives the recoloring.\n #\n # h) Generator validation target:\n-#    - Every generated sample must contain at least one unused legend count.\n-#    - Every real sprite count must appear exactly once in the legend strip.\n-#    - `main(input)` must match the generator's output-frame oracle.\n+#    - Every generated sample must contain at least one unmatched legend count.\n+#    - Every real sprite area must appear exactly once in the legend.\n+#    - `main(input)` must equal the oracle output frame.\n #\n-# i) New solver assumptions that the generator explicitly guarantees:\n-#    - Every legend component touches row 0 because the strip is pasted at the top-left corner.\n-#    - No non-legend object touches row 0 because the entire top band is reserved.\n-#    - Each placeholder color has exactly one external sprite union with bbox equal to the\n-#      placeholder size.\n-#    - Sprite counts are pairwise distinct, and legend counts are pairwise distinct.\n+# i) New solver assumptions that the generator guarantees:\n+#    - Only legend entries occupy row 0 outside the frame.\n+#    - Real sprite areas are pairwise distinct.\n+#    - Distractor legend counts are distinct from all real sprite areas.\n+#    - For each placeholder color, the union of its non-legend outside components has the\n+#      same bbox as that color's placeholder blocks.\n # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n \n \n FRAME_COL = 5\n-SPRITE_N_RANGE = (3, 6)\n+SPRITE_N_RANGE = (3, 5)             # N in {3, 4}\n GRID_ROWS_RANGE = (2, 4)\n GRID_COLS_RANGE = (3, 5)\n TOTAL_BLOCKS_RANGE = (6, 10)\n MAX_EMPTY_SLOTS = 2\n-NUM_COLORS_RANGE = (2, 5)\n-SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES = (2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8)\n-DISTRACTOR_RANGE = (1, 2)\n+NUM_COLORS_RANGE = (2, 4)\n+SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES = (2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7)\n MIN_FRAME_H = 13\n MIN_FRAME_W = 18\n MAX_FRAME_DIM = 21\n@@ -110,22 +125,16 @@\n CANVAS_H_RANGE = (22, 31)\n CANVAS_W_RANGE = (23, 31)\n PATCH_PADDING = 1\n-GEN_RETRIES = 500\n+GEN_RETRIES = 400\n+DISTRACTOR_RANGE = (1, 2)\n \n-LEGEND_H = 3\n-LEGEND_ENTRY_W = 3\n+LEGEND_H = 2\n+LEGEND_ENTRY_W = 4\n LEGEND_GAP = 1\n TOP_BAND_H = LEGEND_H + 1\n LEGEND_ORDER = (\n-    (0, 0),\n-    (0, 1),\n-    (0, 2),\n-    (1, 0),\n-    (1, 1),\n-    (1, 2),\n-    (2, 0),\n-    (2, 1),\n-    (2, 2),\n+    (0, 0), (0, 1), (0, 2), (0, 3),\n+    (1, 0), (1, 1), (1, 2), (1, 3),\n )\n \n \n@@ -161,45 +170,6 @@\n \n def _bbox_hw(bbox: tuple[int, int, int, int]) -> tuple[int, int]:\n     return bbox[2] - bbox[0] + 1, bbox[3] - bbox[1] + 1\n-\n-\n-def _legend_entries(comps: list[dict]) -> list[tuple[int, int, int, int]]:\n-    \"\"\"Return legend entries as (x_pos, out_color, pixel_count, comp_id), sorted by x.\"\"\"\n-    entries = [\n-        (int(comp[\"bbox\"][1]), int(comp[\"col\"]), int(comp[\"area\"]), int(comp[\"id\"]))\n-        for comp in comps\n-        if comp[\"bbox\"][0] == 0 and comp[\"bbox\"][2] < LEGEND_H\n-    ]\n-    entries.sort(key=lambda item: item[0])\n-    return entries\n-\n-\n-def _extract_sprite_data(\n-    comps: list[dict],\n-    placeholder_colors: set[int],\n-    phw: dict[int, tuple[int, int]],\n-    legend_ids: set[int],\n-) -> dict[int, tuple[tuple[tuple[int, int], ...], int, int, int]]:\n-    sprite_data: dict[int, tuple[tuple[tuple[int, int], ...], int, int, int]] = {}\n-    for src_col in sorted(placeholder_colors):\n-        all_candidates = [c for c in comps if c[\"col\"] == src_col and c[\"id\"] not in legend_ids]\n-        assert all_candidates, f\"no sprite found for placeholder color {src_col}\"\n-\n-        pts_set = set()\n-        r0 = min(c[\"bbox\"][0] for c in all_candidates)\n-        c0 = min(c[\"bbox\"][1] for c in all_candidates)\n-        r1 = max(c[\"bbox\"][2] for c in all_candidates)\n-        c1 = max(c[\"bbox\"][3] for c in all_candidates)\n-        for comp in all_candidates:\n-            pts_set.update(comp[\"pts\"])\n-\n-        want_h, want_w = phw[src_col]\n-        assert (r1 - r0 + 1, c1 - c0 + 1) == (want_h, want_w), (\n-            f\"sprite union bbox does not match placeholder size for color {src_col}\"\n-        )\n-        coords = tuple(sorted((r - r0, c - c0) for r, c in pts_set))\n-        sprite_data[src_col] = (coords, want_h, want_w, len(coords))\n-    return sprite_data\n \n \n def _analyze_scene(grid: np.ndarray) -> dict:\n@@ -220,7 +190,7 @@\n     for col in sorted(placeholder_colors):\n         for pts in components_mask((crop == col) & inner_mask, connectivity=4):\n             r0, c0, r1, c1 = bbox_coords(pts)\n-            placeholders.append((col, (r0, c0, r1, c1)))\n+            placeholders.append((int(col), (r0, c0, r1, c1)))\n \n     phw: dict[int, tuple[int, int]] = {}\n     for col in placeholder_colors:\n@@ -228,7 +198,7 @@\n         assert dims, f\"no placeholder component found for color {col}\"\n         unique_dims = sorted(set(dims))\n         assert len(unique_dims) == 1, f\"ambiguous placeholder sizes for color {col}: {unique_dims}\"\n-        phw[col] = unique_dims[0]\n+        phw[int(col)] = unique_dims[0]\n \n     outside = np.ones(g.shape, dtype=bool)\n     outside[fr0 : fr1 + 1, fc0 : fc1 + 1] = False\n@@ -251,28 +221,58 @@\n             )\n             cid += 1\n \n-    legend = _legend_entries(comps)\n-    assert legend, \"count legend must occupy the top row\"\n-    legend_ids = {entry[3] for entry in legend}\n+    legend_entries = [\n+        {\n+            \"x\": int(comp[\"bbox\"][1]),\n+            \"color\": int(comp[\"col\"]),\n+            \"count\": int(comp[\"area\"]),\n+            \"id\": int(comp[\"id\"]),\n+        }\n+        for comp in comps\n+        if comp[\"bbox\"][0] == 0\n+    ]\n+    legend_entries.sort(key=lambda entry: entry[\"x\"])\n+    assert legend_entries, \"count legend must occupy the top row\"\n+\n+    legend_ids = {entry[\"id\"] for entry in legend_entries}\n+    count_to_color: dict[int, int] = {}\n+    for entry in legend_entries:\n+        count = entry[\"count\"]\n+        assert count not in count_to_color, f\"duplicate legend count {count}\"\n+        count_to_color[count] = int(entry[\"color\"])\n+\n+    sprite_data: dict[int, tuple[tuple[tuple[int, int], ...], int, int, int]] = {}\n+    for src_col in sorted(placeholder_colors):\n+        all_candidates = [c for c in comps if c[\"col\"] == src_col and c[\"id\"] not in legend_ids]\n+        assert all_candidates, f\"no sprite found for placeholder color {src_col}\"\n+\n+        r0 = min(c[\"bbox\"][0] for c in all_candidates)\n+        c0 = min(c[\"bbox\"][1] for c in all_candidates)\n+        r1 = max(c[\"bbox\"][2] for c in all_candidates)\n+        c1 = max(c[\"bbox\"][3] for c in all_candidates)\n+        pts_set = set()\n+        for comp in all_candidates:\n+            pts_set.update(comp[\"pts\"])\n+\n+        want_h, want_w = phw[int(src_col)]\n+        assert (r1 - r0 + 1, c1 - c0 + 1) == (want_h, want_w), (\n+            f\"sprite union bbox does not match placeholder size for color {src_col}\"\n+        )\n+        coords = tuple(sorted((r - r0, c - c0) for r, c in pts_set))\n+        area = len(coords)\n+        sprite_data[int(src_col)] = (coords, want_h, want_w, area)\n \n-    count_to_tgt: dict[int, int] = {}\n-    for _x, out_col, pixel_count, _cid in legend:\n-        assert pixel_count not in count_to_tgt, f\"duplicate legend count {pixel_count}\"\n-        count_to_tgt[pixel_count] = int(out_col)\n+    sprite_areas = [area for _coords, _sh, _sw, area in sprite_data.values()]\n+    assert len(set(sprite_areas)) == len(sprite_areas), f\"sprite areas must be unique, got {sprite_areas}\"\n \n-    sprite_data = _extract_sprite_data(comps, placeholder_colors, phw, legend_ids)\n-    sprite_counts = [area for _coords, _sh, _sw, area in sprite_data.values()]\n-    assert len(set(sprite_counts)) == len(sprite_counts), \"sprite counts must be unique in this variant\"\n-    sprite_count_set = set(sprite_counts)\n-    legend_count_set = set(count_to_tgt)\n-    assert sprite_count_set.issubset(legend_count_set), (\n-        f\"legend counts {sorted(legend_count_set)} do not cover sprite areas {sorted(sprite_count_set)}\"\n-    )\n+    color_map: dict[int, int] = {}\n+    for src_col, (_coords, _sh, _sw, area) in sprite_data.items():\n+        assert area in count_to_color, f\"no legend count matches sprite area {area}\"\n+        color_map[int(src_col)] = int(count_to_color[area])\n \n-    color_map = {src_col: int(count_to_tgt[area]) for src_col, (_coords, _sh, _sw, area) in sprite_data.items()}\n-    distractor_counts = sorted(legend_count_set - sprite_count_set)\n-    matched_counts = sorted(sprite_count_set)\n-    assert distractor_counts, \"legend must include at least one unused count\"\n+    matched_counts = {area for area in sprite_areas}\n+    distractor_counts = {entry[\"count\"] for entry in legend_entries if entry[\"count\"] not in matched_counts}\n+    assert distractor_counts, \"legend must contain at least one unmatched count\"\n \n     return {\n         \"bg\": bg,\n@@ -282,34 +282,29 @@\n         \"phw\": phw,\n         \"sprite_data\": sprite_data,\n         \"color_map\": color_map,\n-        \"legend_count_set\": legend_count_set,\n+        \"legend_entries\": legend_entries,\n         \"matched_counts\": matched_counts,\n         \"distractor_counts\": distractor_counts,\n+        \"legend_count_total\": len(legend_entries),\n     }\n \n \n def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n     \"\"\"\n-    Replace framed placeholders with outside sprites and recolor them through a count-coded legend strip.\n+    Fill the framed placeholders with external sprites, then recolor them using a counted legend with decoys.\n \n     Input structure:\n-    - A gray rectangular frame encloses a grid of solid-color placeholder blocks on a background field.\n-    - Outside the frame there is one source-colored sprite template for each placeholder color.\n-    - Along the top-left edge there is a legend strip of small monochrome count codes, and some of those\n-      legend entries are distractors whose counts do not match any real sprite.\n+    - A gray rectangular frame contains solid-color placeholder blocks on background cells.\n+    - Outside the frame there is one sprite template for each placeholder color, rendered in that same source color.\n+    - The top-left of the whole grid contains a legend strip of compact single-color entries whose pixel counts encode keys; some legend entries are extra and match no sprite.\n \n     Rule:\n-    - Recover each sprite by taking all non-legend outside components of the same color and matching their\n-      union bbox to the placeholder size.\n-    - Count the colored cells in that recovered sprite and use that count, not the sprite silhouette, as the\n-      lookup key into the top legend strip.\n-    - Ignore legend entries whose counts are never realized by any recovered sprite.\n-    - Stamp every recovered sprite into each matching placeholder slot and recolor it with the color of the\n-      legend entry that has the same pixel count.\n+    - Recover each source-colored sprite outside the frame and count how many colored cells it contains.\n+    - Read every top-row legend component as a candidate mapping from pixel count to output color.\n+    - Keep only the legend counts that actually occur among the recovered sprites, ignoring unmatched legend entries.\n+    - Replace every placeholder block with its sprite shape and recolor it to the output color associated with that sprite's pixel count.\n \n-    Key insight: The legend no longer tells you which shape to use; the outside sprite color still selects\n-    the shape, but the final recolor comes only from matching sprite area to a count legend that includes\n-    extra decoy counts.\n+    Key insight: The legend no longer names shapes or source colors. The only reliable key is the sprite's colored-cell count, and the extra legend counts must be filtered out by comparing them against the real sprites.\n     \"\"\"\n     info = _analyze_scene(grid)\n     crop = info[\"crop\"]\n@@ -337,7 +332,7 @@\n \n \n def _legend_patch(entries: list[tuple[int, int]], bg: int) -> np.ndarray:\n-    \"\"\"Build the top-left legend strip from (pixel_count, target_color) pairs.\"\"\"\n+    \"\"\"Build the top-left count legend from (pixel_count, target_color) pairs.\"\"\"\n     width = len(entries) * LEGEND_ENTRY_W + max(0, len(entries) - 1) * LEGEND_GAP\n     patch = np.full((LEGEND_H, width), bg, dtype=int)\n     for idx, (pixel_count, color) in enumerate(entries):\n@@ -349,7 +344,7 @@\n \n def _sprite_mask(n: int, area: int) -> np.ndarray:\n     \"\"\"Generate an NxN sparse mask with exact area and full NxN union bbox.\"\"\"\n-    assert 2 <= area <= min(len(LEGEND_ORDER) - 1, n * n - 1), f\"unsupported area {area} for n={n}\"\n+    assert 2 <= area <= min(len(LEGEND_ORDER), n * n), f\"unsupported area {area} for n={n}\"\n     mask = np.zeros((n, n), dtype=bool)\n \n     corner_pairs = [\n@@ -440,16 +435,18 @@\n     usable = [c for c in range(10) if c not in (bg, FRAME_COL)]\n \n     k = random.randint(*NUM_COLORS_RANGE)\n-    src_cols = random.sample(usable, k)\n-    tgt_cols = random.sample(usable, k)\n-    real_counts = random.sample(SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES, k)\n-    remaining_counts = [count for count in SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES if count not in real_counts]\n-    max_distractors = min(DISTRACTOR_RANGE[1], len(remaining_counts))\n+    max_distractors = min(DISTRACTOR_RANGE[1], len(SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES) - k)\n     if max_distractors < DISTRACTOR_RANGE[0]:\n         return None\n     distractor_count = random.randint(DISTRACTOR_RANGE[0], max_distractors)\n-    distractor_counts = random.sample(remaining_counts, distractor_count)\n \n+    src_cols = random.sample(usable, k)\n+    tgt_cols = random.sample(usable, k)\n+\n+    counts = random.sample(SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES, k + distractor_count)\n+    real_counts = counts[:k]\n+    distractor_counts = counts[k:]\n+\n     color_to_tgt = dict(zip(src_cols, tgt_cols))\n     masks = {src: _sprite_mask(n, area) for src, area in zip(src_cols, real_counts)}\n \n@@ -521,6 +518,8 @@\n \n     try:\n         info = _analyze_scene(grid)\n+        if info[\"legend_count_total\"] != k + distractor_count:\n+            return None\n         if len(info[\"matched_counts\"]) != k:\n             return None\n         if len(info[\"distractor_counts\"]) != distractor_count:\n\nexec\n/bin/bash -lc \"/home/xd/miniconda3/bin/python -c \\\"import numpy as np, importlib.util, time, sys\nspec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('variant', '/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/9/code.py')\nmod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\nspec.loader.exec_module(mod)\nok, fail = 0, 0\nt0 = time.time()\nfor i in range(50):\n    try:\n        inp = mod.generate_input()\n        out = mod.main(inp)\n        ok += 1\n    except Exception as e:\n        fail += 1\n        if fail <= 3: print(f'Trial {i}: {type(e).__name__}: {e}')\nelapsed = time.time() - t0\nprint(f'Success: {ok}/50, Time: {elapsed:.1f}s ({elapsed/50*1000:.0f}ms/call)')\nif ok < 40: sys.exit(1)\n\\\"\" in /home/lixinyu/snap/new\ndiff --git a/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/9/code.py b/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/9/code.py\nindex 5118d5b845ab2464b87c40373164ab3076d9256f..fe289f311fa3d2eb7cae6b98357ee4db4ce110f3\n--- a/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/9/code.py\n+++ b/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/9/code.py\n@@ -2,107 +2,122 @@\n # combo_spec: D7/2+D13/0\n # Name: 数量编码图例+干扰条目\n \n+import importlib.util\n import itertools\n+from pathlib import Path\n import random\n+import sys\n \n import numpy as np\n \n-from arc_utils import bbox_coords, components_mask, get_bg, paste, random_free_location\n+ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[4]\n+if str(ROOT) not in sys.path:\n+    sys.path.append(str(ROOT))\n \n+try:\n+    from arc_utils import bbox_coords, components_mask, get_bg, paste, random_free_location\n+except ModuleNotFoundError:\n+    _spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\"_combo_arc_utils\", ROOT / \"solvers\" / \"arc_utils.py\")\n+    _mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(_spec)\n+    assert _spec.loader is not None\n+    _spec.loader.exec_module(_mod)\n+    bbox_coords = _mod.bbox_coords\n+    components_mask = _mod.components_mask\n+    get_bg = _mod.get_bg\n+    paste = _mod.paste\n+    random_free_location = _mod.random_free_location\n \n # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n-# Design analysis for the fused D7/2 + D13/0 variant\n+# Design analysis for the combo variant\n #\n # a) Concrete behavior and trace:\n-#    - Keep the original large gray frame with solid-color placeholder blocks inside.\n-#    - Keep one outside sprite template per placeholder color; each sprite still uses the\n-#      placeholder color and has the same N x N bbox as the matching blocks inside the frame.\n-#    - Replace the old overlapping two-color legend with a top-left strip of monochrome\n-#      count codes. Each code is a compact 3x3 nested stencil whose area is the key and\n-#      whose color is the recolor target.\n-#    - Add 1-2 extra legend entries whose counts do not match any real sprite. Those entries\n-#      are visible in the same strip, so solver must count every sprite, compare that count\n-#      against all legend entries, and ignore the unmatched ones.\n-#    - Example: suppose a cyan external sprite occupies exactly 5 cells in a 4x4 bbox, while\n-#      the legend strip contains orange-5, red-7, yellow-3, and teal-8 entries. Cyan blocks\n-#      inside the frame become the 5-cell sprite recolored to orange. The 7/3/8 entries stay\n-#      unused if no sprite has those counts. In the original task, recoloring came from a\n-#      direct shape-color legend pair; here it comes from sprite area, and some legend items\n-#      are decoys.\n+#    - Keep the original backbone: one gray rectangular frame, solid placeholder blocks\n+#      inside the frame, and one source-colored sprite template outside the frame for each\n+#      placeholder color.\n+#    - Replace the original overlapping two-color legend with a fixed top-left legend strip.\n+#      Each legend entry is now a compact monochrome stencil whose area encodes a number.\n+#      The legend color is the output color, while the number of colored pixels is the key.\n+#    - Add mandatory distractor legend entries. These extra count codes are rendered exactly\n+#      like the real legend entries but their pixel counts do not match any real sprite area.\n+#    - Example: suppose blue placeholders correspond to a 4x4 outside sprite with exactly\n+#      5 colored cells, and green placeholders correspond to a 4x4 sprite with 3 cells.\n+#      The legend may show orange=5 cells, red=3 cells, and yellow=6 cells. The solver must\n+#      count the blue sprite, match 5 to orange, count the green sprite, match 3 to red,\n+#      and ignore the yellow 6-cell legend item. In the original task, recoloring came from\n+#      direct shape-color legend pairs; in this fusion, recoloring requires count matching\n+#      plus filtering unmatched legend counts.\n #\n # b) Complexity calibration:\n-#    - Real sprite counts are unique and chosen from a small visual vocabulary 2..8. This\n-#      keeps counting tractable while still giving enough room for distractors.\n-#    - There are 2-5 placeholder colors, so each sample has repeated evidence inside the frame\n-#      but not so many codes that the top legend becomes unreadable.\n-#    - Distractors are mandatory but capped at 1-2, which makes the extra filtering visible\n-#      without drowning out the true legend entries.\n+#    - Restrict real sprite areas to a small vocabulary {2,3,4,5,6,7}. This makes counting\n+#      observable, while still leaving room for 1-2 unmatched legend counts in the same band.\n+#    - Limit the number of placeholder colors to 2-4. That preserves repeated evidence inside\n+#      the frame and avoids exhausting the count vocabulary once distractors are added.\n+#    - Keep sprite boxes at 3x3 or 4x4. Larger boxes would make exact counting slower and add\n+#      clutter; smaller boxes would not support enough distinct counted patterns.\n #\n-# c) Implicit assumption audit against the original solver:\n-#    - Old legend parsing assumed overlapping two-color glyphs and source-color inference from\n-#      pair structure. That breaks completely; fused solver instead reads monochrome entries\n-#      anchored on the top row and uses component area as the code.\n-#    - Old sprite extraction only had to exclude legend components paired by overlap. That is\n-#      no longer valid because legend entries now have a single color and may share colors with\n-#      real sprites. The generator therefore reserves the whole top band for legends, and the\n-#      solver excludes all top-band components from sprite recovery.\n-#    - Count-based recoloring only works if different placeholder colors do not share the same\n-#      sprite area. The generator guarantees unique real counts, and solver asserts that.\n-#    - Distractors are only safe if their counts are distinct from all real counts. The\n-#      generator enforces that; solver checks that legend counts form a strict superset of\n-#      sprite counts rather than an arbitrary unrelated set.\n+# c) Implicit-assumption audit against the original solver:\n+#    - Original legend parsing assumed small overlapping two-color regions; that is no longer\n+#      true. The new solver instead assumes every outside component touching row 0 is part of\n+#      the top legend strip.\n+#    - Original source->target mapping was indexed by placeholder color. That assumption is\n+#      broken by D7/2: color now only selects which sprite to stamp, while legend lookup is\n+#      keyed by sprite area.\n+#    - Original code expected every parsed legend item to be relevant. D13/0 breaks that too:\n+#      the new solver must recover all real sprite areas first, then use only legend counts\n+#      that match those areas.\n+#    - Sparse counted sprites may be 4-disconnected, so extraction cannot rely on one single\n+#      connected component spanning the full bbox. The solver unions all non-legend components\n+#      of the same source color and checks the union bbox against the placeholder size.\n #\n # d) Placement legality:\n-#    - The top band is reserved before frame placement, so no sprite or frame cell can touch\n-#      the legend strip.\n-#    - Frame, external sprites, and legend entries are all placed with a one-cell padding gap\n-#      via `random_free_location`, preventing overlap or accidental touching.\n-#    - Sprite masks always include opposite corners of the N x N bbox, so the union bbox seen\n-#      by the solver exactly matches the placeholder block size even when the sprite is sparse\n-#      or disconnected.\n+#    - The generator reserves a top band for legends, preventing sprite/frame collisions with\n+#      legend entries and guaranteeing that row-0 colored components are legends only.\n+#    - `random_free_location` with one-cell padding separates the frame, legend strip, and\n+#      all outside sprites, so no objects touch or overlap.\n+#    - Sprite masks always include opposite corners of their NxN box, ensuring that the union\n+#      bbox exactly matches the placeholder block size even when the mask is disconnected.\n #\n # e) Visual observability:\n-#    - A human can recover the rule by counting cells in an outside sprite, then scanning the\n-#      top strip for the legend entry with the same count to get the output color.\n-#    - The extra legend items are not hidden metadata; they are visible unmatched counts in the\n-#      same legend family, so the added reasoning load is observable from the grids alone.\n+#    - A human can inspect the outside sprite for one placeholder color, count its colored\n+#      cells, and then look for the same count in the top-left legend to infer the recolor.\n+#    - The distractor dimension is visible because the legend contains more count entries than\n+#      there are actual sprite areas. These extras cannot be dismissed by shape alone; they\n+#      must be excluded by exact counting.\n #\n # f) Visual cleanliness:\n-#    - Legends live in one dedicated band, the frame occupies one compact rectangle elsewhere,\n-#      and sprites are separate free patches. This keeps object categories spatially separated.\n-#    - All legend entries share one simple 3x3 encoding template, reducing clutter compared with\n-#      arbitrary glyphs or mixed overlay patterns.\n+#    - All legend entries share one strip at the top. All sprites live below that strip.\n+#      The frame is placed away from both via the reserve mask, so the scene stays segmented.\n+#    - Each legend entry is monochrome and compact, with a single background gap between\n+#      entries. This keeps the distractors legible without introducing another border motif.\n #\n # g) Change inferability:\n-#    - Output colors are structurally indicated by the legend-entry colors, not by raw palette\n-#      ids. Because counts repeat via multiple placeholders of the same color, a few samples are\n-#      enough to show that equal source colors do not determine output colors on their own.\n-#    - Distractors do not affect placed objects, so the solver must infer that only counts seen\n-#      on real sprites are actionable.\n+#    - Output colors remain directly visible in the legend, but only after inferring which\n+#      count entries are live. Because placeholder colors repeat and each source color has\n+#      one repeated sprite template, 2-4 samples are enough to see that count equality, not\n+#      shape identity or legend order, drives the recoloring.\n #\n # h) Generator validation target:\n-#    - Every generated sample must contain at least one unused legend count.\n-#    - Every real sprite count must appear exactly once in the legend strip.\n-#    - `main(input)` must match the generator's output-frame oracle.\n+#    - Every generated sample must contain at least one unmatched legend count.\n+#    - Every real sprite area must appear exactly once in the legend.\n+#    - `main(input)` must equal the oracle output frame.\n #\n-# i) New solver assumptions that the generator explicitly guarantees:\n-#    - Every legend component touches row 0 because the strip is pasted at the top-left corner.\n-#    - No non-legend object touches row 0 because the entire top band is reserved.\n-#    - Each placeholder color has exactly one external sprite union with bbox equal to the\n-#      placeholder size.\n-#    - Sprite counts are pairwise distinct, and legend counts are pairwise distinct.\n+# i) New solver assumptions that the generator guarantees:\n+#    - Only legend entries occupy row 0 outside the frame.\n+#    - Real sprite areas are pairwise distinct.\n+#    - Distractor legend counts are distinct from all real sprite areas.\n+#    - For each placeholder color, the union of its non-legend outside components has the\n+#      same bbox as that color's placeholder blocks.\n # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n \n \n FRAME_COL = 5\n-SPRITE_N_RANGE = (3, 6)\n+SPRITE_N_RANGE = (3, 5)             # N in {3, 4}\n GRID_ROWS_RANGE = (2, 4)\n GRID_COLS_RANGE = (3, 5)\n TOTAL_BLOCKS_RANGE = (6, 10)\n MAX_EMPTY_SLOTS = 2\n-NUM_COLORS_RANGE = (2, 5)\n-SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES = (2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8)\n-DISTRACTOR_RANGE = (1, 2)\n+NUM_COLORS_RANGE = (2, 4)\n+SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES = (2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7)\n MIN_FRAME_H = 13\n MIN_FRAME_W = 18\n MAX_FRAME_DIM = 21\n@@ -110,22 +125,16 @@\n CANVAS_H_RANGE = (22, 31)\n CANVAS_W_RANGE = (23, 31)\n PATCH_PADDING = 1\n-GEN_RETRIES = 500\n+GEN_RETRIES = 400\n+DISTRACTOR_RANGE = (1, 2)\n \n-LEGEND_H = 3\n-LEGEND_ENTRY_W = 3\n+LEGEND_H = 2\n+LEGEND_ENTRY_W = 4\n LEGEND_GAP = 1\n TOP_BAND_H = LEGEND_H + 1\n LEGEND_ORDER = (\n-    (0, 0),\n-    (0, 1),\n-    (0, 2),\n-    (1, 0),\n-    (1, 1),\n-    (1, 2),\n-    (2, 0),\n-    (2, 1),\n-    (2, 2),\n+    (0, 0), (0, 1), (0, 2), (0, 3),\n+    (1, 0), (1, 1), (1, 2), (1, 3),\n )\n \n \n@@ -161,45 +170,6 @@\n \n def _bbox_hw(bbox: tuple[int, int, int, int]) -> tuple[int, int]:\n     return bbox[2] - bbox[0] + 1, bbox[3] - bbox[1] + 1\n-\n-\n-def _legend_entries(comps: list[dict]) -> list[tuple[int, int, int, int]]:\n-    \"\"\"Return legend entries as (x_pos, out_color, pixel_count, comp_id), sorted by x.\"\"\"\n-    entries = [\n-        (int(comp[\"bbox\"][1]), int(comp[\"col\"]), int(comp[\"area\"]), int(comp[\"id\"]))\n-        for comp in comps\n-        if comp[\"bbox\"][0] == 0 and comp[\"bbox\"][2] < LEGEND_H\n-    ]\n-    entries.sort(key=lambda item: item[0])\n-    return entries\n-\n-\n-def _extract_sprite_data(\n-    comps: list[dict],\n-    placeholder_colors: set[int],\n-    phw: dict[int, tuple[int, int]],\n-    legend_ids: set[int],\n-) -> dict[int, tuple[tuple[tuple[int, int], ...], int, int, int]]:\n-    sprite_data: dict[int, tuple[tuple[tuple[int, int], ...], int, int, int]] = {}\n-    for src_col in sorted(placeholder_colors):\n-        all_candidates = [c for c in comps if c[\"col\"] == src_col and c[\"id\"] not in legend_ids]\n-        assert all_candidates, f\"no sprite found for placeholder color {src_col}\"\n-\n-        pts_set = set()\n-        r0 = min(c[\"bbox\"][0] for c in all_candidates)\n-        c0 = min(c[\"bbox\"][1] for c in all_candidates)\n-        r1 = max(c[\"bbox\"][2] for c in all_candidates)\n-        c1 = max(c[\"bbox\"][3] for c in all_candidates)\n-        for comp in all_candidates:\n-            pts_set.update(comp[\"pts\"])\n-\n-        want_h, want_w = phw[src_col]\n-        assert (r1 - r0 + 1, c1 - c0 + 1) == (want_h, want_w), (\n-            f\"sprite union bbox does not match placeholder size for color {src_col}\"\n-        )\n-        coords = tuple(sorted((r - r0, c - c0) for r, c in pts_set))\n-        sprite_data[src_col] = (coords, want_h, want_w, len(coords))\n-    return sprite_data\n \n \n def _analyze_scene(grid: np.ndarray) -> dict:\n@@ -220,7 +190,7 @@\n     for col in sorted(placeholder_colors):\n         for pts in components_mask((crop == col) & inner_mask, connectivity=4):\n             r0, c0, r1, c1 = bbox_coords(pts)\n-            placeholders.append((col, (r0, c0, r1, c1)))\n+            placeholders.append((int(col), (r0, c0, r1, c1)))\n \n     phw: dict[int, tuple[int, int]] = {}\n     for col in placeholder_colors:\n@@ -228,7 +198,7 @@\n         assert dims, f\"no placeholder component found for color {col}\"\n         unique_dims = sorted(set(dims))\n         assert len(unique_dims) == 1, f\"ambiguous placeholder sizes for color {col}: {unique_dims}\"\n-        phw[col] = unique_dims[0]\n+        phw[int(col)] = unique_dims[0]\n \n     outside = np.ones(g.shape, dtype=bool)\n     outside[fr0 : fr1 + 1, fc0 : fc1 + 1] = False\n@@ -251,28 +221,58 @@\n             )\n             cid += 1\n \n-    legend = _legend_entries(comps)\n-    assert legend, \"count legend must occupy the top row\"\n-    legend_ids = {entry[3] for entry in legend}\n+    legend_entries = [\n+        {\n+            \"x\": int(comp[\"bbox\"][1]),\n+            \"color\": int(comp[\"col\"]),\n+            \"count\": int(comp[\"area\"]),\n+            \"id\": int(comp[\"id\"]),\n+        }\n+        for comp in comps\n+        if comp[\"bbox\"][0] == 0\n+    ]\n+    legend_entries.sort(key=lambda entry: entry[\"x\"])\n+    assert legend_entries, \"count legend must occupy the top row\"\n+\n+    legend_ids = {entry[\"id\"] for entry in legend_entries}\n+    count_to_color: dict[int, int] = {}\n+    for entry in legend_entries:\n+        count = entry[\"count\"]\n+        assert count not in count_to_color, f\"duplicate legend count {count}\"\n+        count_to_color[count] = int(entry[\"color\"])\n+\n+    sprite_data: dict[int, tuple[tuple[tuple[int, int], ...], int, int, int]] = {}\n+    for src_col in sorted(placeholder_colors):\n+        all_candidates = [c for c in comps if c[\"col\"] == src_col and c[\"id\"] not in legend_ids]\n+        assert all_candidates, f\"no sprite found for placeholder color {src_col}\"\n+\n+        r0 = min(c[\"bbox\"][0] for c in all_candidates)\n+        c0 = min(c[\"bbox\"][1] for c in all_candidates)\n+        r1 = max(c[\"bbox\"][2] for c in all_candidates)\n+        c1 = max(c[\"bbox\"][3] for c in all_candidates)\n+        pts_set = set()\n+        for comp in all_candidates:\n+            pts_set.update(comp[\"pts\"])\n+\n+        want_h, want_w = phw[int(src_col)]\n+        assert (r1 - r0 + 1, c1 - c0 + 1) == (want_h, want_w), (\n+            f\"sprite union bbox does not match placeholder size for color {src_col}\"\n+        )\n+        coords = tuple(sorted((r - r0, c - c0) for r, c in pts_set))\n+        area = len(coords)\n+        sprite_data[int(src_col)] = (coords, want_h, want_w, area)\n \n-    count_to_tgt: dict[int, int] = {}\n-    for _x, out_col, pixel_count, _cid in legend:\n-        assert pixel_count not in count_to_tgt, f\"duplicate legend count {pixel_count}\"\n-        count_to_tgt[pixel_count] = int(out_col)\n+    sprite_areas = [area for _coords, _sh, _sw, area in sprite_data.values()]\n+    assert len(set(sprite_areas)) == len(sprite_areas), f\"sprite areas must be unique, got {sprite_areas}\"\n \n-    sprite_data = _extract_sprite_data(comps, placeholder_colors, phw, legend_ids)\n-    sprite_counts = [area for _coords, _sh, _sw, area in sprite_data.values()]\n-    assert len(set(sprite_counts)) == len(sprite_counts), \"sprite counts must be unique in this variant\"\n-    sprite_count_set = set(sprite_counts)\n-    legend_count_set = set(count_to_tgt)\n-    assert sprite_count_set.issubset(legend_count_set), (\n-        f\"legend counts {sorted(legend_count_set)} do not cover sprite areas {sorted(sprite_count_set)}\"\n-    )\n+    color_map: dict[int, int] = {}\n+    for src_col, (_coords, _sh, _sw, area) in sprite_data.items():\n+        assert area in count_to_color, f\"no legend count matches sprite area {area}\"\n+        color_map[int(src_col)] = int(count_to_color[area])\n \n-    color_map = {src_col: int(count_to_tgt[area]) for src_col, (_coords, _sh, _sw, area) in sprite_data.items()}\n-    distractor_counts = sorted(legend_count_set - sprite_count_set)\n-    matched_counts = sorted(sprite_count_set)\n-    assert distractor_counts, \"legend must include at least one unused count\"\n+    matched_counts = {area for area in sprite_areas}\n+    distractor_counts = {entry[\"count\"] for entry in legend_entries if entry[\"count\"] not in matched_counts}\n+    assert distractor_counts, \"legend must contain at least one unmatched count\"\n \n     return {\n         \"bg\": bg,\n@@ -282,34 +282,29 @@\n         \"phw\": phw,\n         \"sprite_data\": sprite_data,\n         \"color_map\": color_map,\n-        \"legend_count_set\": legend_count_set,\n+        \"legend_entries\": legend_entries,\n         \"matched_counts\": matched_counts,\n         \"distractor_counts\": distractor_counts,\n+        \"legend_count_total\": len(legend_entries),\n     }\n \n \n def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n     \"\"\"\n-    Replace framed placeholders with outside sprites and recolor them through a count-coded legend strip.\n+    Fill the framed placeholders with external sprites, then recolor them using a counted legend with decoys.\n \n     Input structure:\n-    - A gray rectangular frame encloses a grid of solid-color placeholder blocks on a background field.\n-    - Outside the frame there is one source-colored sprite template for each placeholder color.\n-    - Along the top-left edge there is a legend strip of small monochrome count codes, and some of those\n-      legend entries are distractors whose counts do not match any real sprite.\n+    - A gray rectangular frame contains solid-color placeholder blocks on background cells.\n+    - Outside the frame there is one sprite template for each placeholder color, rendered in that same source color.\n+    - The top-left of the whole grid contains a legend strip of compact single-color entries whose pixel counts encode keys; some legend entries are extra and match no sprite.\n \n     Rule:\n-    - Recover each sprite by taking all non-legend outside components of the same color and matching their\n-      union bbox to the placeholder size.\n-    - Count the colored cells in that recovered sprite and use that count, not the sprite silhouette, as the\n-      lookup key into the top legend strip.\n-    - Ignore legend entries whose counts are never realized by any recovered sprite.\n-    - Stamp every recovered sprite into each matching placeholder slot and recolor it with the color of the\n-      legend entry that has the same pixel count.\n+    - Recover each source-colored sprite outside the frame and count how many colored cells it contains.\n+    - Read every top-row legend component as a candidate mapping from pixel count to output color.\n+    - Keep only the legend counts that actually occur among the recovered sprites, ignoring unmatched legend entries.\n+    - Replace every placeholder block with its sprite shape and recolor it to the output color associated with that sprite's pixel count.\n \n-    Key insight: The legend no longer tells you which shape to use; the outside sprite color still selects\n-    the shape, but the final recolor comes only from matching sprite area to a count legend that includes\n-    extra decoy counts.\n+    Key insight: The legend no longer names shapes or source colors. The only reliable key is the sprite's colored-cell count, and the extra legend counts must be filtered out by comparing them against the real sprites.\n     \"\"\"\n     info = _analyze_scene(grid)\n     crop = info[\"crop\"]\n@@ -337,7 +332,7 @@\n \n \n def _legend_patch(entries: list[tuple[int, int]], bg: int) -> np.ndarray:\n-    \"\"\"Build the top-left legend strip from (pixel_count, target_color) pairs.\"\"\"\n+    \"\"\"Build the top-left count legend from (pixel_count, target_color) pairs.\"\"\"\n     width = len(entries) * LEGEND_ENTRY_W + max(0, len(entries) - 1) * LEGEND_GAP\n     patch = np.full((LEGEND_H, width), bg, dtype=int)\n     for idx, (pixel_count, color) in enumerate(entries):\n@@ -349,7 +344,7 @@\n \n def _sprite_mask(n: int, area: int) -> np.ndarray:\n     \"\"\"Generate an NxN sparse mask with exact area and full NxN union bbox.\"\"\"\n-    assert 2 <= area <= min(len(LEGEND_ORDER) - 1, n * n - 1), f\"unsupported area {area} for n={n}\"\n+    assert 2 <= area <= min(len(LEGEND_ORDER), n * n), f\"unsupported area {area} for n={n}\"\n     mask = np.zeros((n, n), dtype=bool)\n \n     corner_pairs = [\n@@ -440,16 +435,18 @@\n     usable = [c for c in range(10) if c not in (bg, FRAME_COL)]\n \n     k = random.randint(*NUM_COLORS_RANGE)\n-    src_cols = random.sample(usable, k)\n-    tgt_cols = random.sample(usable, k)\n-    real_counts = random.sample(SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES, k)\n-    remaining_counts = [count for count in SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES if count not in real_counts]\n-    max_distractors = min(DISTRACTOR_RANGE[1], len(remaining_counts))\n+    max_distractors = min(DISTRACTOR_RANGE[1], len(SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES) - k)\n     if max_distractors < DISTRACTOR_RANGE[0]:\n         return None\n     distractor_count = random.randint(DISTRACTOR_RANGE[0], max_distractors)\n-    distractor_counts = random.sample(remaining_counts, distractor_count)\n \n+    src_cols = random.sample(usable, k)\n+    tgt_cols = random.sample(usable, k)\n+\n+    counts = random.sample(SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES, k + distractor_count)\n+    real_counts = counts[:k]\n+    distractor_counts = counts[k:]\n+\n     color_to_tgt = dict(zip(src_cols, tgt_cols))\n     masks = {src: _sprite_mask(n, area) for src, area in zip(src_cols, real_counts)}\n \n@@ -521,6 +518,8 @@\n \n     try:\n         info = _analyze_scene(grid)\n+        if info[\"legend_count_total\"] != k + distractor_count:\n+            return None\n         if len(info[\"matched_counts\"]) != k:\n             return None\n         if len(info[\"distractor_counts\"]) != distractor_count:\n\n succeeded in 1071ms:\nSuccess: 50/50, Time: 0.8s (15ms/call)\n\ncodex\n可靠性已经过线。现在做融合行为验证，不再只看 `main(input)==output`，而是统计“图例总条目数减去被真实精灵使用的计数数”这个指标；这个值必须大于 0，才能说明干扰条目确实存在并参与了解析设计。\nexec\n/bin/bash -lc \"/home/xd/miniconda3/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport importlib.util\nfrom collections import Counter\n\nspec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('variant', '/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/9/code.py')\nmod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\nspec.loader.exec_module(mod)\n\nsamples = 100\nextra_counter = Counter()\nlegend_total_counter = Counter()\nmatched_counter = Counter()\ncount_value_counter = Counter()\n\nfor _ in range(samples):\n    grid = mod.generate_input()\n    info = mod._analyze_scene(grid)\n    extra = info['legend_count_total'] - len(info['matched_counts'])\n    extra_counter[extra] += 1\n    legend_total_counter[info['legend_count_total']] += 1\n    matched_counter[len(info['matched_counts'])] += 1\n    for v in info['distractor_counts']:\n        count_value_counter[v] += 1\n\nprint('extra_entries_distribution', dict(sorted(extra_counter.items())))\nprint('legend_total_distribution', dict(sorted(legend_total_counter.items())))\nprint('matched_real_count_distribution', dict(sorted(matched_counter.items())))\nprint('distractor_count_values', dict(sorted(count_value_counter.items())))\nPY\" in /home/lixinyu/snap/new\ndiff --git a/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/9/code.py b/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/9/code.py\nindex 5118d5b845ab2464b87c40373164ab3076d9256f..fe289f311fa3d2eb7cae6b98357ee4db4ce110f3\n--- a/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/9/code.py\n+++ b/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/9/code.py\n@@ -2,107 +2,122 @@\n # combo_spec: D7/2+D13/0\n # Name: 数量编码图例+干扰条目\n \n+import importlib.util\n import itertools\n+from pathlib import Path\n import random\n+import sys\n \n import numpy as np\n \n-from arc_utils import bbox_coords, components_mask, get_bg, paste, random_free_location\n+ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[4]\n+if str(ROOT) not in sys.path:\n+    sys.path.append(str(ROOT))\n \n+try:\n+    from arc_utils import bbox_coords, components_mask, get_bg, paste, random_free_location\n+except ModuleNotFoundError:\n+    _spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\"_combo_arc_utils\", ROOT / \"solvers\" / \"arc_utils.py\")\n+    _mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(_spec)\n+    assert _spec.loader is not None\n+    _spec.loader.exec_module(_mod)\n+    bbox_coords = _mod.bbox_coords\n+    components_mask = _mod.components_mask\n+    get_bg = _mod.get_bg\n+    paste = _mod.paste\n+    random_free_location = _mod.random_free_location\n \n # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n-# Design analysis for the fused D7/2 + D13/0 variant\n+# Design analysis for the combo variant\n #\n # a) Concrete behavior and trace:\n-#    - Keep the original large gray frame with solid-color placeholder blocks inside.\n-#    - Keep one outside sprite template per placeholder color; each sprite still uses the\n-#      placeholder color and has the same N x N bbox as the matching blocks inside the frame.\n-#    - Replace the old overlapping two-color legend with a top-left strip of monochrome\n-#      count codes. Each code is a compact 3x3 nested stencil whose area is the key and\n-#      whose color is the recolor target.\n-#    - Add 1-2 extra legend entries whose counts do not match any real sprite. Those entries\n-#      are visible in the same strip, so solver must count every sprite, compare that count\n-#      against all legend entries, and ignore the unmatched ones.\n-#    - Example: suppose a cyan external sprite occupies exactly 5 cells in a 4x4 bbox, while\n-#      the legend strip contains orange-5, red-7, yellow-3, and teal-8 entries. Cyan blocks\n-#      inside the frame become the 5-cell sprite recolored to orange. The 7/3/8 entries stay\n-#      unused if no sprite has those counts. In the original task, recoloring came from a\n-#      direct shape-color legend pair; here it comes from sprite area, and some legend items\n-#      are decoys.\n+#    - Keep the original backbone: one gray rectangular frame, solid placeholder blocks\n+#      inside the frame, and one source-colored sprite template outside the frame for each\n+#      placeholder color.\n+#    - Replace the original overlapping two-color legend with a fixed top-left legend strip.\n+#      Each legend entry is now a compact monochrome stencil whose area encodes a number.\n+#      The legend color is the output color, while the number of colored pixels is the key.\n+#    - Add mandatory distractor legend entries. These extra count codes are rendered exactly\n+#      like the real legend entries but their pixel counts do not match any real sprite area.\n+#    - Example: suppose blue placeholders correspond to a 4x4 outside sprite with exactly\n+#      5 colored cells, and green placeholders correspond to a 4x4 sprite with 3 cells.\n+#      The legend may show orange=5 cells, red=3 cells, and yellow=6 cells. The solver must\n+#      count the blue sprite, match 5 to orange, count the green sprite, match 3 to red,\n+#      and ignore the yellow 6-cell legend item. In the original task, recoloring came from\n+#      direct shape-color legend pairs; in this fusion, recoloring requires count matching\n+#      plus filtering unmatched legend counts.\n #\n # b) Complexity calibration:\n-#    - Real sprite counts are unique and chosen from a small visual vocabulary 2..8. This\n-#      keeps counting tractable while still giving enough room for distractors.\n-#    - There are 2-5 placeholder colors, so each sample has repeated evidence inside the frame\n-#      but not so many codes that the top legend becomes unreadable.\n-#    - Distractors are mandatory but capped at 1-2, which makes the extra filtering visible\n-#      without drowning out the true legend entries.\n+#    - Restrict real sprite areas to a small vocabulary {2,3,4,5,6,7}. This makes counting\n+#      observable, while still leaving room for 1-2 unmatched legend counts in the same band.\n+#    - Limit the number of placeholder colors to 2-4. That preserves repeated evidence inside\n+#      the frame and avoids exhausting the count vocabulary once distractors are added.\n+#    - Keep sprite boxes at 3x3 or 4x4. Larger boxes would make exact counting slower and add\n+#      clutter; smaller boxes would not support enough distinct counted patterns.\n #\n-# c) Implicit assumption audit against the original solver:\n-#    - Old legend parsing assumed overlapping two-color glyphs and source-color inference from\n-#      pair structure. That breaks completely; fused solver instead reads monochrome entries\n-#      anchored on the top row and uses component area as the code.\n-#    - Old sprite extraction only had to exclude legend components paired by overlap. That is\n-#      no longer valid because legend entries now have a single color and may share colors with\n-#      real sprites. The generator therefore reserves the whole top band for legends, and the\n-#      solver excludes all top-band components from sprite recovery.\n-#    - Count-based recoloring only works if different placeholder colors do not share the same\n-#      sprite area. The generator guarantees unique real counts, and solver asserts that.\n-#    - Distractors are only safe if their counts are distinct from all real counts. The\n-#      generator enforces that; solver checks that legend counts form a strict superset of\n-#      sprite counts rather than an arbitrary unrelated set.\n+# c) Implicit-assumption audit against the original solver:\n+#    - Original legend parsing assumed small overlapping two-color regions; that is no longer\n+#      true. The new solver instead assumes every outside component touching row 0 is part of\n+#      the top legend strip.\n+#    - Original source->target mapping was indexed by placeholder color. That assumption is\n+#      broken by D7/2: color now only selects which sprite to stamp, while legend lookup is\n+#      keyed by sprite area.\n+#    - Original code expected every parsed legend item to be relevant. D13/0 breaks that too:\n+#      the new solver must recover all real sprite areas first, then use only legend counts\n+#      that match those areas.\n+#    - Sparse counted sprites may be 4-disconnected, so extraction cannot rely on one single\n+#      connected component spanning the full bbox. The solver unions all non-legend components\n+#      of the same source color and checks the union bbox against the placeholder size.\n #\n # d) Placement legality:\n-#    - The top band is reserved before frame placement, so no sprite or frame cell can touch\n-#      the legend strip.\n-#    - Frame, external sprites, and legend entries are all placed with a one-cell padding gap\n-#      via `random_free_location`, preventing overlap or accidental touching.\n-#    - Sprite masks always include opposite corners of the N x N bbox, so the union bbox seen\n-#      by the solver exactly matches the placeholder block size even when the sprite is sparse\n-#      or disconnected.\n+#    - The generator reserves a top band for legends, preventing sprite/frame collisions with\n+#      legend entries and guaranteeing that row-0 colored components are legends only.\n+#    - `random_free_location` with one-cell padding separates the frame, legend strip, and\n+#      all outside sprites, so no objects touch or overlap.\n+#    - Sprite masks always include opposite corners of their NxN box, ensuring that the union\n+#      bbox exactly matches the placeholder block size even when the mask is disconnected.\n #\n # e) Visual observability:\n-#    - A human can recover the rule by counting cells in an outside sprite, then scanning the\n-#      top strip for the legend entry with the same count to get the output color.\n-#    - The extra legend items are not hidden metadata; they are visible unmatched counts in the\n-#      same legend family, so the added reasoning load is observable from the grids alone.\n+#    - A human can inspect the outside sprite for one placeholder color, count its colored\n+#      cells, and then look for the same count in the top-left legend to infer the recolor.\n+#    - The distractor dimension is visible because the legend contains more count entries than\n+#      there are actual sprite areas. These extras cannot be dismissed by shape alone; they\n+#      must be excluded by exact counting.\n #\n # f) Visual cleanliness:\n-#    - Legends live in one dedicated band, the frame occupies one compact rectangle elsewhere,\n-#      and sprites are separate free patches. This keeps object categories spatially separated.\n-#    - All legend entries share one simple 3x3 encoding template, reducing clutter compared with\n-#      arbitrary glyphs or mixed overlay patterns.\n+#    - All legend entries share one strip at the top. All sprites live below that strip.\n+#      The frame is placed away from both via the reserve mask, so the scene stays segmented.\n+#    - Each legend entry is monochrome and compact, with a single background gap between\n+#      entries. This keeps the distractors legible without introducing another border motif.\n #\n # g) Change inferability:\n-#    - Output colors are structurally indicated by the legend-entry colors, not by raw palette\n-#      ids. Because counts repeat via multiple placeholders of the same color, a few samples are\n-#      enough to show that equal source colors do not determine output colors on their own.\n-#    - Distractors do not affect placed objects, so the solver must infer that only counts seen\n-#      on real sprites are actionable.\n+#    - Output colors remain directly visible in the legend, but only after inferring which\n+#      count entries are live. Because placeholder colors repeat and each source color has\n+#      one repeated sprite template, 2-4 samples are enough to see that count equality, not\n+#      shape identity or legend order, drives the recoloring.\n #\n # h) Generator validation target:\n-#    - Every generated sample must contain at least one unused legend count.\n-#    - Every real sprite count must appear exactly once in the legend strip.\n-#    - `main(input)` must match the generator's output-frame oracle.\n+#    - Every generated sample must contain at least one unmatched legend count.\n+#    - Every real sprite area must appear exactly once in the legend.\n+#    - `main(input)` must equal the oracle output frame.\n #\n-# i) New solver assumptions that the generator explicitly guarantees:\n-#    - Every legend component touches row 0 because the strip is pasted at the top-left corner.\n-#    - No non-legend object touches row 0 because the entire top band is reserved.\n-#    - Each placeholder color has exactly one external sprite union with bbox equal to the\n-#      placeholder size.\n-#    - Sprite counts are pairwise distinct, and legend counts are pairwise distinct.\n+# i) New solver assumptions that the generator guarantees:\n+#    - Only legend entries occupy row 0 outside the frame.\n+#    - Real sprite areas are pairwise distinct.\n+#    - Distractor legend counts are distinct from all real sprite areas.\n+#    - For each placeholder color, the union of its non-legend outside components has the\n+#      same bbox as that color's placeholder blocks.\n # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n \n \n FRAME_COL = 5\n-SPRITE_N_RANGE = (3, 6)\n+SPRITE_N_RANGE = (3, 5)             # N in {3, 4}\n GRID_ROWS_RANGE = (2, 4)\n GRID_COLS_RANGE = (3, 5)\n TOTAL_BLOCKS_RANGE = (6, 10)\n MAX_EMPTY_SLOTS = 2\n-NUM_COLORS_RANGE = (2, 5)\n-SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES = (2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8)\n-DISTRACTOR_RANGE = (1, 2)\n+NUM_COLORS_RANGE = (2, 4)\n+SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES = (2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7)\n MIN_FRAME_H = 13\n MIN_FRAME_W = 18\n MAX_FRAME_DIM = 21\n@@ -110,22 +125,16 @@\n CANVAS_H_RANGE = (22, 31)\n C