 top-left edge there is a legend strip of small monochrome count codes, and some of those\n-      legend entries are distractors whose counts do not match any real sprite.\n+    - A gray rectangular frame contains solid-color placeholder blocks on background cells.\n+    - Outside the frame there is one sprite template for each placeholder color, rendered in that same source color.\n+    - The top-left of the whole grid contains a legend strip of compact single-color entries whose pixel counts encode keys; some legend entries are extra and match no sprite.\n \n     Rule:\n-    - Recover each sprite by taking all non-legend outside components of the same color and matching their\n-      union bbox to the placeholder size.\n-    - Count the colored cells in that recovered sprite and use that count, not the sprite silhouette, as the\n-      lookup key into the top legend strip.\n-    - Ignore legend entries whose counts are never realized by any recovered sprite.\n-    - Stamp every recovered sprite into each matching placeholder slot and recolor it with the color of the\n-      legend entry that has the same pixel count.\n+    - Recover each source-colored sprite outside the frame and count how many colored cells it contains.\n+    - Read every top-row legend component as a candidate mapping from pixel count to output color.\n+    - Keep only the legend counts that actually occur among the recovered sprites, ignoring unmatched legend entries.\n+    - Replace every placeholder block with its sprite shape and recolor it to the output color associated with that sprite's pixel count.\n \n-    Key insight: The legend no longer tells you which shape to use; the outside sprite color still selects\n-    the shape, but the final recolor comes only from matching sprite area to a count legend that includes\n-    extra decoy counts.\n+    Key insight: The legend no longer names shapes or source colors. The only reliable key is the sprite's colored-cell count, and the extra legend counts must be filtered out by comparing them against the real sprites.\n     \"\"\"\n     info = _analyze_scene(grid)\n     crop = info[\"crop\"]\n@@ -337,7 +332,7 @@\n \n \n def _legend_patch(entries: list[tuple[int, int]], bg: int) -> np.ndarray:\n-    \"\"\"Build the top-left legend strip from (pixel_count, target_color) pairs.\"\"\"\n+    \"\"\"Build the top-left count legend from (pixel_count, target_color) pairs.\"\"\"\n     width = len(entries) * LEGEND_ENTRY_W + max(0, len(entries) - 1) * LEGEND_GAP\n     patch = np.full((LEGEND_H, width), bg, dtype=int)\n     for idx, (pixel_count, color) in enumerate(entries):\n@@ -349,7 +344,7 @@\n \n def _sprite_mask(n: int, area: int) -> np.ndarray:\n     \"\"\"Generate an NxN sparse mask with exact area and full NxN union bbox.\"\"\"\n-    assert 2 <= area <= min(len(LEGEND_ORDER) - 1, n * n - 1), f\"unsupported area {area} for n={n}\"\n+    assert 2 <= area <= min(len(LEGEND_ORDER), n * n), f\"unsupported area {area} for n={n}\"\n     mask = np.zeros((n, n), dtype=bool)\n \n     corner_pairs = [\n@@ -440,16 +435,18 @@\n     usable = [c for c in range(10) if c not in (bg, FRAME_COL)]\n \n     k = random.randint(*NUM_COLORS_RANGE)\n-    src_cols = random.sample(usable, k)\n-    tgt_cols = random.sample(usable, k)\n-    real_counts = random.sample(SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES, k)\n-    remaining_counts = [count for count in SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES if count not in real_counts]\n-    max_distractors = min(DISTRACTOR_RANGE[1], len(remaining_counts))\n+    max_distractors = min(DISTRACTOR_RANGE[1], len(SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES) - k)\n     if max_distractors < DISTRACTOR_RANGE[0]:\n         return None\n     distractor_count = random.randint(DISTRACTOR_RANGE[0], max_distractors)\n-    distractor_counts = random.sample(remaining_counts, distractor_count)\n \n+    src_cols = random.sample(usable, k)\n+    tgt_cols = random.sample(usable, k)\n+\n+    counts = random.sample(SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES, k + distractor_count)\n+    real_counts = counts[:k]\n+    distractor_counts = counts[k:]\n+\n     color_to_tgt = dict(zip(src_cols, tgt_cols))\n     masks = {src: _sprite_mask(n, area) for src, area in zip(src_cols, real_counts)}\n \n@@ -521,6 +518,8 @@\n \n     try:\n         info = _analyze_scene(grid)\n+        if info[\"legend_count_total\"] != k + distractor_count:\n+            return None\n         if len(info[\"matched_counts\"]) != k:\n             return None\n         if len(info[\"distractor_counts\"]) != distractor_count:\n\n succeeded in 1451ms:\nextra_entries_distribution {1: 50, 2: 50}\nlegend_total_distribution {3: 18, 4: 33, 5: 32, 6: 17}\nmatched_real_count_distribution {2: 35, 3: 32, 4: 33}\ndistractor_count_values {2: 21, 3: 26, 4: 28, 5: 24, 6: 27, 7: 24}\n\ncodex\n我在等 100 个样本的分布统计返回。这里主要看 `extra_entries_distribution` 是否始终为正，以及是否确实出现了多个不同的干扰计数值。\ndiff --git a/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/9/code.py b/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/9/code.py\nindex 5118d5b845ab2464b87c40373164ab3076d9256f..fe289f311fa3d2eb7cae6b98357ee4db4ce110f3\n--- a/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/9/code.py\n+++ b/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/9/code.py\n@@ -2,107 +2,122 @@\n # combo_spec: D7/2+D13/0\n # Name: 数量编码图例+干扰条目\n \n+import importlib.util\n import itertools\n+from pathlib import Path\n import random\n+import sys\n \n import numpy as np\n \n-from arc_utils import bbox_coords, components_mask, get_bg, paste, random_free_location\n+ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[4]\n+if str(ROOT) not in sys.path:\n+    sys.path.append(str(ROOT))\n \n+try:\n+    from arc_utils import bbox_coords, components_mask, get_bg, paste, random_free_location\n+except ModuleNotFoundError:\n+    _spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\"_combo_arc_utils\", ROOT / \"solvers\" / \"arc_utils.py\")\n+    _mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(_spec)\n+    assert _spec.loader is not None\n+    _spec.loader.exec_module(_mod)\n+    bbox_coords = _mod.bbox_coords\n+    components_mask = _mod.components_mask\n+    get_bg = _mod.get_bg\n+    paste = _mod.paste\n+    random_free_location = _mod.random_free_location\n \n # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n-# Design analysis for the fused D7/2 + D13/0 variant\n+# Design analysis for the combo variant\n #\n # a) Concrete behavior and trace:\n-#    - Keep the original large gray frame with solid-color placeholder blocks inside.\n-#    - Keep one outside sprite template per placeholder color; each sprite still uses the\n-#      placeholder color and has the same N x N bbox as the matching blocks inside the frame.\n-#    - Replace the old overlapping two-color legend with a top-left strip of monochrome\n-#      count codes. Each code is a compact 3x3 nested stencil whose area is the key and\n-#      whose color is the recolor target.\n-#    - Add 1-2 extra legend entries whose counts do not match any real sprite. Those entries\n-#      are visible in the same strip, so solver must count every sprite, compare that count\n-#      against all legend entries, and ignore the unmatched ones.\n-#    - Example: suppose a cyan external sprite occupies exactly 5 cells in a 4x4 bbox, while\n-#      the legend strip contains orange-5, red-7, yellow-3, and teal-8 entries. Cyan blocks\n-#      inside the frame become the 5-cell sprite recolored to orange. The 7/3/8 entries stay\n-#      unused if no sprite has those counts. In the original task, recoloring came from a\n-#      direct shape-color legend pair; here it comes from sprite area, and some legend items\n-#      are decoys.\n+#    - Keep the original backbone: one gray rectangular frame, solid placeholder blocks\n+#      inside the frame, and one source-colored sprite template outside the frame for each\n+#      placeholder color.\n+#    - Replace the original overlapping two-color legend with a fixed top-left legend strip.\n+#      Each legend entry is now a compact monochrome stencil whose area encodes a number.\n+#      The legend color is the output color, while the number of colored pixels is the key.\n+#    - Add mandatory distractor legend entries. These extra count codes are rendered exactly\n+#      like the real legend entries but their pixel counts do not match any real sprite area.\n+#    - Example: suppose blue placeholders correspond to a 4x4 outside sprite with exactly\n+#      5 colored cells, and green placeholders correspond to a 4x4 sprite with 3 cells.\n+#      The legend may show orange=5 cells, red=3 cells, and yellow=6 cells. The solver must\n+#      count the blue sprite, match 5 to orange, count the green sprite, match 3 to red,\n+#      and ignore the yellow 6-cell legend item. In the original task, recoloring came from\n+#      direct shape-color legend pairs; in this fusion, recoloring requires count matching\n+#      plus filtering unmatched legend counts.\n #\n # b) Complexity calibration:\n-#    - Real sprite counts are unique and chosen from a small visual vocabulary 2..8. This\n-#      keeps counting tractable while still giving enough room for distractors.\n-#    - There are 2-5 placeholder colors, so each sample has repeated evidence inside the frame\n-#      but not so many codes that the top legend becomes unreadable.\n-#    - Distractors are mandatory but capped at 1-2, which makes the extra filtering visible\n-#      without drowning out the true legend entries.\n+#    - Restrict real sprite areas to a small vocabulary {2,3,4,5,6,7}. This makes counting\n+#      observable, while still leaving room for 1-2 unmatched legend counts in the same band.\n+#    - Limit the number of placeholder colors to 2-4. That preserves repeated evidence inside\n+#      the frame and avoids exhausting the count vocabulary once distractors are added.\n+#    - Keep sprite boxes at 3x3 or 4x4. Larger boxes would make exact counting slower and add\n+#      clutter; smaller boxes would not support enough distinct counted patterns.\n #\n-# c) Implicit assumption audit against the original solver:\n-#    - Old legend parsing assumed overlapping two-color glyphs and source-color inference from\n-#      pair structure. That breaks completely; fused solver instead reads monochrome entries\n-#      anchored on the top row and uses component area as the code.\n-#    - Old sprite extraction only had to exclude legend components paired by overlap. That is\n-#      no longer valid because legend entries now have a single color and may share colors with\n-#      real sprites. The generator therefore reserves the whole top band for legends, and the\n-#      solver excludes all top-band components from sprite recovery.\n-#    - Count-based recoloring only works if different placeholder colors do not share the same\n-#      sprite area. The generator guarantees unique real counts, and solver asserts that.\n-#    - Distractors are only safe if their counts are distinct from all real counts. The\n-#      generator enforces that; solver checks that legend counts form a strict superset of\n-#      sprite counts rather than an arbitrary unrelated set.\n+# c) Implicit-assumption audit against the original solver:\n+#    - Original legend parsing assumed small overlapping two-color regions; that is no longer\n+#      true. The new solver instead assumes every outside component touching row 0 is part of\n+#      the top legend strip.\n+#    - Original source->target mapping was indexed by placeholder color. That assumption is\n+#      broken by D7/2: color now only selects which sprite to stamp, while legend lookup is\n+#      keyed by sprite area.\n+#    - Original code expected every parsed legend item to be relevant. D13/0 breaks that too:\n+#      the new solver must recover all real sprite areas first, then use only legend counts\n+#      that match those areas.\n+#    - Sparse counted sprites may be 4-disconnected, so extraction cannot rely on one single\n+#      connected component spanning the full bbox. The solver unions all non-legend components\n+#      of the same source color and checks the union bbox against the placeholder size.\n #\n # d) Placement legality:\n-#    - The top band is reserved before frame placement, so no sprite or frame cell can touch\n-#      the legend strip.\n-#    - Frame, external sprites, and legend entries are all placed with a one-cell padding gap\n-#      via `random_free_location`, preventing overlap or accidental touching.\n-#    - Sprite masks always include opposite corners of the N x N bbox, so the union bbox seen\n-#      by the solver exactly matches the placeholder block size even when the sprite is sparse\n-#      or disconnected.\n+#    - The generator reserves a top band for legends, preventing sprite/frame collisions with\n+#      legend entries and guaranteeing that row-0 colored components are legends only.\n+#    - `random_free_location` with one-cell padding separates the frame, legend strip, and\n+#      all outside sprites, so no objects touch or overlap.\n+#    - Sprite masks always include opposite corners of their NxN box, ensuring that the union\n+#      bbox exactly matches the placeholder block size even when the mask is disconnected.\n #\n # e) Visual observability:\n-#    - A human can recover the rule by counting cells in an outside sprite, then scanning the\n-#      top strip for the legend entry with the same count to get the output color.\n-#    - The extra legend items are not hidden metadata; they are visible unmatched counts in the\n-#      same legend family, so the added reasoning load is observable from the grids alone.\n+#    - A human can inspect the outside sprite for one placeholder color, count its colored\n+#      cells, and then look for the same count in the top-left legend to infer the recolor.\n+#    - The distractor dimension is visible because the legend contains more count entries than\n+#      there are actual sprite areas. These extras cannot be dismissed by shape alone; they\n+#      must be excluded by exact counting.\n #\n # f) Visual cleanliness:\n-#    - Legends live in one dedicated band, the frame occupies one compact rectangle elsewhere,\n-#      and sprites are separate free patches. This keeps object categories spatially separated.\n-#    - All legend entries share one simple 3x3 encoding template, reducing clutter compared with\n-#      arbitrary glyphs or mixed overlay patterns.\n+#    - All legend entries share one strip at the top. All sprites live below that strip.\n+#      The frame is placed away from both via the reserve mask, so the scene stays segmented.\n+#    - Each legend entry is monochrome and compact, with a single background gap between\n+#      entries. This keeps the distractors legible without introducing another border motif.\n #\n # g) Change inferability:\n-#    - Output colors are structurally indicated by the legend-entry colors, not by raw palette\n-#      ids. Because counts repeat via multiple placeholders of the same color, a few samples are\n-#      enough to show that equal source colors do not determine output colors on their own.\n-#    - Distractors do not affect placed objects, so the solver must infer that only counts seen\n-#      on real sprites are actionable.\n+#    - Output colors remain directly visible in the legend, but only after inferring which\n+#      count entries are live. Because placeholder colors repeat and each source color has\n+#      one repeated sprite template, 2-4 samples are enough to see that count equality, not\n+#      shape identity or legend order, drives the recoloring.\n #\n # h) Generator validation target:\n-#    - Every generated sample must contain at least one unused legend count.\n-#    - Every real sprite count must appear exactly once in the legend strip.\n-#    - `main(input)` must match the generator's output-frame oracle.\n+#    - Every generated sample must contain at least one unmatched legend count.\n+#    - Every real sprite area must appear exactly once in the legend.\n+#    - `main(input)` must equal the oracle output frame.\n #\n-# i) New solver assumptions that the generator explicitly guarantees:\n-#    - Every legend component touches row 0 because the strip is pasted at the top-left corner.\n-#    - No non-legend object touches row 0 because the entire top band is reserved.\n-#    - Each placeholder color has exactly one external sprite union with bbox equal to the\n-#      placeholder size.\n-#    - Sprite counts are pairwise distinct, and legend counts are pairwise distinct.\n+# i) New solver assumptions that the generator guarantees:\n+#    - Only legend entries occupy row 0 outside the frame.\n+#    - Real sprite areas are pairwise distinct.\n+#    - Distractor legend counts are distinct from all real sprite areas.\n+#    - For each placeholder color, the union of its non-legend outside components has the\n+#      same bbox as that color's placeholder blocks.\n # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n \n \n FRAME_COL = 5\n-SPRITE_N_RANGE = (3, 6)\n+SPRITE_N_RANGE = (3, 5)             # N in {3, 4}\n GRID_ROWS_RANGE = (2, 4)\n GRID_COLS_RANGE = (3, 5)\n TOTAL_BLOCKS_RANGE = (6, 10)\n MAX_EMPTY_SLOTS = 2\n-NUM_COLORS_RANGE = (2, 5)\n-SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES = (2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8)\n-DISTRACTOR_RANGE = (1, 2)\n+NUM_COLORS_RANGE = (2, 4)\n+SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES = (2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7)\n MIN_FRAME_H = 13\n MIN_FRAME_W = 18\n MAX_FRAME_DIM = 21\n@@ -110,22 +125,16 @@\n CANVAS_H_RANGE = (22, 31)\n CANVAS_W_RANGE = (23, 31)\n PATCH_PADDING = 1\n-GEN_RETRIES = 500\n+GEN_RETRIES = 400\n+DISTRACTOR_RANGE = (1, 2)\n \n-LEGEND_H = 3\n-LEGEND_ENTRY_W = 3\n+LEGEND_H = 2\n+LEGEND_ENTRY_W = 4\n LEGEND_GAP = 1\n TOP_BAND_H = LEGEND_H + 1\n LEGEND_ORDER = (\n-    (0, 0),\n-    (0, 1),\n-    (0, 2),\n-    (1, 0),\n-    (1, 1),\n-    (1, 2),\n-    (2, 0),\n-    (2, 1),\n-    (2, 2),\n+    (0, 0), (0, 1), (0, 2), (0, 3),\n+    (1, 0), (1, 1), (1, 2), (1, 3),\n )\n \n \n@@ -161,45 +170,6 @@\n \n def _bbox_hw(bbox: tuple[int, int, int, int]) -> tuple[int, int]:\n     return bbox[2] - bbox[0] + 1, bbox[3] - bbox[1] + 1\n-\n-\n-def _legend_entries(comps: list[dict]) -> list[tuple[int, int, int, int]]:\n-    \"\"\"Return legend entries as (x_pos, out_color, pixel_count, comp_id), sorted by x.\"\"\"\n-    entries = [\n-        (int(comp[\"bbox\"][1]), int(comp[\"col\"]), int(comp[\"area\"]), int(comp[\"id\"]))\n-        for comp in comps\n-        if comp[\"bbox\"][0] == 0 and comp[\"bbox\"][2] < LEGEND_H\n-    ]\n-    entries.sort(key=lambda item: item[0])\n-    return entries\n-\n-\n-def _extract_sprite_data(\n-    comps: list[dict],\n-    placeholder_colors: set[int],\n-    phw: dict[int, tuple[int, int]],\n-    legend_ids: set[int],\n-) -> dict[int, tuple[tuple[tuple[int, int], ...], int, int, int]]:\n-    sprite_data: dict[int, tuple[tuple[tuple[int, int], ...], int, int, int]] = {}\n-    for src_col in sorted(placeholder_colors):\n-        all_candidates = [c for c in comps if c[\"col\"] == src_col and c[\"id\"] not in legend_ids]\n-        assert all_candidates, f\"no sprite found for placeholder color {src_col}\"\n-\n-        pts_set = set()\n-        r0 = min(c[\"bbox\"][0] for c in all_candidates)\n-        c0 = min(c[\"bbox\"][1] for c in all_candidates)\n-        r1 = max(c[\"bbox\"][2] for c in all_candidates)\n-        c1 = max(c[\"bbox\"][3] for c in all_candidates)\n-        for comp in all_candidates:\n-            pts_set.update(comp[\"pts\"])\n-\n-        want_h, want_w = phw[src_col]\n-        assert (r1 - r0 + 1, c1 - c0 + 1) == (want_h, want_w), (\n-            f\"sprite union bbox does not match placeholder size for color {src_col}\"\n-        )\n-        coords = tuple(sorted((r - r0, c - c0) for r, c in pts_set))\n-        sprite_data[src_col] = (coords, want_h, want_w, len(coords))\n-    return sprite_data\n \n \n def _analyze_scene(grid: np.ndarray) -> dict:\n@@ -220,7 +190,7 @@\n     for col in sorted(placeholder_colors):\n         for pts in components_mask((crop == col) & inner_mask, connectivity=4):\n             r0, c0, r1, c1 = bbox_coords(pts)\n-            placeholders.append((col, (r0, c0, r1, c1)))\n+            placeholders.append((int(col), (r0, c0, r1, c1)))\n \n     phw: dict[int, tuple[int, int]] = {}\n     for col in placeholder_colors:\n@@ -228,7 +198,7 @@\n         assert dims, f\"no placeholder component found for color {col}\"\n         unique_dims = sorted(set(dims))\n         assert len(unique_dims) == 1, f\"ambiguous placeholder sizes for color {col}: {unique_dims}\"\n-        phw[col] = unique_dims[0]\n+        phw[int(col)] = unique_dims[0]\n \n     outside = np.ones(g.shape, dtype=bool)\n     outside[fr0 : fr1 + 1, fc0 : fc1 + 1] = False\n@@ -251,28 +221,58 @@\n             )\n             cid += 1\n \n-    legend = _legend_entries(comps)\n-    assert legend, \"count legend must occupy the top row\"\n-    legend_ids = {entry[3] for entry in legend}\n+    legend_entries = [\n+        {\n+            \"x\": int(comp[\"bbox\"][1]),\n+            \"color\": int(comp[\"col\"]),\n+            \"count\": int(comp[\"area\"]),\n+            \"id\": int(comp[\"id\"]),\n+        }\n+        for comp in comps\n+        if comp[\"bbox\"][0] == 0\n+    ]\n+    legend_entries.sort(key=lambda entry: entry[\"x\"])\n+    assert legend_entries, \"count legend must occupy the top row\"\n+\n+    legend_ids = {entry[\"id\"] for entry in legend_entries}\n+    count_to_color: dict[int, int] = {}\n+    for entry in legend_entries:\n+        count = entry[\"count\"]\n+        assert count not in count_to_color, f\"duplicate legend count {count}\"\n+        count_to_color[count] = int(entry[\"color\"])\n+\n+    sprite_data: dict[int, tuple[tuple[tuple[int, int], ...], int, int, int]] = {}\n+    for src_col in sorted(placeholder_colors):\n+        all_candidates = [c for c in comps if c[\"col\"] == src_col and c[\"id\"] not in legend_ids]\n+        assert all_candidates, f\"no sprite found for placeholder color {src_col}\"\n+\n+        r0 = min(c[\"bbox\"][0] for c in all_candidates)\n+        c0 = min(c[\"bbox\"][1] for c in all_candidates)\n+        r1 = max(c[\"bbox\"][2] for c in all_candidates)\n+        c1 = max(c[\"bbox\"][3] for c in all_candidates)\n+        pts_set = set()\n+        for comp in all_candidates:\n+            pts_set.update(comp[\"pts\"])\n+\n+        want_h, want_w = phw[int(src_col)]\n+        assert (r1 - r0 + 1, c1 - c0 + 1) == (want_h, want_w), (\n+            f\"sprite union bbox does not match placeholder size for color {src_col}\"\n+        )\n+        coords = tuple(sorted((r - r0, c - c0) for r, c in pts_set))\n+        area = len(coords)\n+        sprite_data[int(src_col)] = (coords, want_h, want_w, area)\n \n-    count_to_tgt: dict[int, int] = {}\n-    for _x, out_col, pixel_count, _cid in legend:\n-        assert pixel_count not in count_to_tgt, f\"duplicate legend count {pixel_count}\"\n-        count_to_tgt[pixel_count] = int(out_col)\n+    sprite_areas = [area for _coords, _sh, _sw, area in sprite_data.values()]\n+    assert len(set(sprite_areas)) == len(sprite_areas), f\"sprite areas must be unique, got {sprite_areas}\"\n \n-    sprite_data = _extract_sprite_data(comps, placeholder_colors, phw, legend_ids)\n-    sprite_counts = [area for _coords, _sh, _sw, area in sprite_data.values()]\n-    assert len(set(sprite_counts)) == len(sprite_counts), \"sprite counts must be unique in this variant\"\n-    sprite_count_set = set(sprite_counts)\n-    legend_count_set = set(count_to_tgt)\n-    assert sprite_count_set.issubset(legend_count_set), (\n-        f\"legend counts {sorted(legend_count_set)} do not cover sprite areas {sorted(sprite_count_set)}\"\n-    )\n+    color_map: dict[int, int] = {}\n+    for src_col, (_coords, _sh, _sw, area) in sprite_data.items():\n+        assert area in count_to_color, f\"no legend count matches sprite area {area}\"\n+        color_map[int(src_col)] = int(count_to_color[area])\n \n-    color_map = {src_col: int(count_to_tgt[area]) for src_col, (_coords, _sh, _sw, area) in sprite_data.items()}\n-    distractor_counts = sorted(legend_count_set - sprite_count_set)\n-    matched_counts = sorted(sprite_count_set)\n-    assert distractor_counts, \"legend must include at least one unused count\"\n+    matched_counts = {area for area in sprite_areas}\n+    distractor_counts = {entry[\"count\"] for entry in legend_entries if entry[\"count\"] not in matched_counts}\n+    assert distractor_counts, \"legend must contain at least one unmatched count\"\n \n     return {\n         \"bg\": bg,\n@@ -282,34 +282,29 @@\n         \"phw\": phw,\n         \"sprite_data\": sprite_data,\n         \"color_map\": color_map,\n-        \"legend_count_set\": legend_count_set,\n+        \"legend_entries\": legend_entries,\n         \"matched_counts\": matched_counts,\n         \"distractor_counts\": distractor_counts,\n+        \"legend_count_total\": len(legend_entries),\n     }\n \n \n def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n     \"\"\"\n-    Replace framed placeholders with outside sprites and recolor them through a count-coded legend strip.\n+    Fill the framed placeholders with external sprites, then recolor them using a counted legend with decoys.\n \n     Input structure:\n-    - A gray rectangular frame encloses a grid of solid-color placeholder blocks on a background field.\n-    - Outside the frame there is one source-colored sprite template for each placeholder color.\n-    - Along the top-left edge there is a legend strip of small monochrome count codes, and some of those\n-      legend entries are distractors whose counts do not match any real sprite.\n+    - A gray rectangular frame contains solid-color placeholder blocks on background cells.\n+    - Outside the frame there is one sprite template for each placeholder color, rendered in that same source color.\n+    - The top-left of the whole grid contains a legend strip of compact single-color entries whose pixel counts encode keys; some legend entries are extra and match no sprite.\n \n     Rule:\n-    - Recover each sprite by taking all non-legend outside components of the same color and matching their\n-      union bbox to the placeholder size.\n-    - Count the colored cells in that recovered sprite and use that count, not the sprite silhouette, as the\n-      lookup key into the top legend strip.\n-    - Ignore legend entries whose counts are never realized by any recovered sprite.\n-    - Stamp every recovered sprite into each matching placeholder slot and recolor it with the color of the\n-      legend entry that has the same pixel count.\n+    - Recover each source-colored sprite outside the frame and count how many colored cells it contains.\n+    - Read every top-row legend component as a candidate mapping from pixel count to output color.\n+    - Keep only the legend counts that actually occur among the recovered sprites, ignoring unmatched legend entries.\n+    - Replace every placeholder block with its sprite shape and recolor it to the output color associated with that sprite's pixel count.\n \n-    Key insight: The legend no longer tells you which shape to use; the outside sprite color still selects\n-    the shape, but the final recolor comes only from matching sprite area to a count legend that includes\n-    extra decoy counts.\n+    Key insight: The legend no longer names shapes or source colors. The only reliable key is the sprite's colored-cell count, and the extra legend counts must be filtered out by comparing them against the real sprites.\n     \"\"\"\n     info = _analyze_scene(grid)\n     crop = info[\"crop\"]\n@@ -337,7 +332,7 @@\n \n \n def _legend_patch(entries: list[tuple[int, int]], bg: int) -> np.ndarray:\n-    \"\"\"Build the top-left legend strip from (pixel_count, target_color) pairs.\"\"\"\n+    \"\"\"Build the top-left count legend from (pixel_count, target_color) pairs.\"\"\"\n     width = len(entries) * LEGEND_ENTRY_W + max(0, len(entries) - 1) * LEGEND_GAP\n     patch = np.full((LEGEND_H, width), bg, dtype=int)\n     for idx, (pixel_count, color) in enumerate(entries):\n@@ -349,7 +344,7 @@\n \n def _sprite_mask(n: int, area: int) -> np.ndarray:\n     \"\"\"Generate an NxN sparse mask with exact area and full NxN union bbox.\"\"\"\n-    assert 2 <= area <= min(len(LEGEND_ORDER) - 1, n * n - 1), f\"unsupported area {area} for n={n}\"\n+    assert 2 <= area <= min(len(LEGEND_ORDER), n * n), f\"unsupported area {area} for n={n}\"\n     mask = np.zeros((n, n), dtype=bool)\n \n     corner_pairs = [\n@@ -440,16 +435,18 @@\n     usable = [c for c in range(10) if c not in (bg, FRAME_COL)]\n \n     k = random.randint(*NUM_COLORS_RANGE)\n-    src_cols = random.sample(usable, k)\n-    tgt_cols = random.sample(usable, k)\n-    real_counts = random.sample(SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES, k)\n-    remaining_counts = [count for count in SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES if count not in real_counts]\n-    max_distractors = min(DISTRACTOR_RANGE[1], len(remaining_counts))\n+    max_distractors = min(DISTRACTOR_RANGE[1], len(SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES) - k)\n     if max_distractors < DISTRACTOR_RANGE[0]:\n         return None\n     distractor_count = random.randint(DISTRACTOR_RANGE[0], max_distractors)\n-    distractor_counts = random.sample(remaining_counts, distractor_count)\n \n+    src_cols = random.sample(usable, k)\n+    tgt_cols = random.sample(usable, k)\n+\n+    counts = random.sample(SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES, k + distractor_count)\n+    real_counts = counts[:k]\n+    distractor_counts = counts[k:]\n+\n     color_to_tgt = dict(zip(src_cols, tgt_cols))\n     masks = {src: _sprite_mask(n, area) for src, area in zip(src_cols, real_counts)}\n \n@@ -521,6 +518,8 @@\n \n     try:\n         info = _analyze_scene(grid)\n+        if info[\"legend_count_total\"] != k + distractor_count:\n+            return None\n         if len(info[\"matched_counts\"]) != k:\n             return None\n         if len(info[\"distractor_counts\"]) != distractor_count:\n\ncodex\n实现和验证都稳定了。我再快速抓一下关键函数的行号，方便在结果里给你精确文件引用，并顺手确认没有遗漏的隐藏假设。\nexec\n/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/9/code.py | sed -n '1,260p'\" in /home/lixinyu/snap/new\n succeeded in 0ms:\n     1\t# Combo variant of edb79dae (index 9)\n     2\t# combo_spec: D7/2+D13/0\n     3\t# Name: 数量编码图例+干扰条目\n     4\t\n     5\timport importlib.util\n     6\timport itertools\n     7\tfrom pathlib import Path\n     8\timport random\n     9\timport sys\n    10\t\n    11\timport numpy as np\n    12\t\n    13\tROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[4]\n    14\tif str(ROOT) not in sys.path:\n    15\t    sys.path.append(str(ROOT))\n    16\t\n    17\ttry:\n    18\t    from arc_utils import bbox_coords, components_mask, get_bg, paste, random_free_location\n    19\texcept ModuleNotFoundError:\n    20\t    _spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\"_combo_arc_utils\", ROOT / \"solvers\" / \"arc_utils.py\")\n    21\t    _mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(_spec)\n    22\t    assert _spec.loader is not None\n    23\t    _spec.loader.exec_module(_mod)\n    24\t    bbox_coords = _mod.bbox_coords\n    25\t    components_mask = _mod.components_mask\n    26\t    get_bg = _mod.get_bg\n    27\t    paste = _mod.paste\n    28\t    random_free_location = _mod.random_free_location\n    29\t\n    30\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    31\t# Design analysis for the combo variant\n    32\t#\n    33\t# a) Concrete behavior and trace:\n    34\t#    - Keep the original backbone: one gray rectangular frame, solid placeholder blocks\n    35\t#      inside the frame, and one source-colored sprite template outside the frame for each\n    36\t#      placeholder color.\n    37\t#    - Replace the original overlapping two-color legend with a fixed top-left legend strip.\n    38\t#      Each legend entry is now a compact monochrome stencil whose area encodes a number.\n    39\t#      The legend color is the output color, while the number of colored pixels is the key.\n    40\t#    - Add mandatory distractor legend entries. These extra count codes are rendered exactly\n    41\t#      like the real legend entries but their pixel counts do not match any real sprite area.\n    42\t#    - Example: suppose blue placeholders correspond to a 4x4 outside sprite with exactly\n    43\t#      5 colored cells, and green placeholders correspond to a 4x4 sprite with 3 cells.\n    44\t#      The legend may show orange=5 cells, red=3 cells, and yellow=6 cells. The solver must\n    45\t#      count the blue sprite, match 5 to orange, count the green sprite, match 3 to red,\n    46\t#      and ignore the yellow 6-cell legend item. In the original task, recoloring came from\n    47\t#      direct shape-color legend pairs; in this fusion, recoloring requires count matching\n    48\t#      plus filtering unmatched legend counts.\n    49\t#\n    50\t# b) Complexity calibration:\n    51\t#    - Restrict real sprite areas to a small vocabulary {2,3,4,5,6,7}. This makes counting\n    52\t#      observable, while still leaving room for 1-2 unmatched legend counts in the same band.\n    53\t#    - Limit the number of placeholder colors to 2-4. That preserves repeated evidence inside\n    54\t#      the frame and avoids exhausting the count vocabulary once distractors are added.\n    55\t#    - Keep sprite boxes at 3x3 or 4x4. Larger boxes would make exact counting slower and add\n    56\t#      clutter; smaller boxes would not support enough distinct counted patterns.\n    57\t#\n    58\t# c) Implicit-assumption audit against the original solver:\n    59\t#    - Original legend parsing assumed small overlapping two-color regions; that is no longer\n    60\t#      true. The new solver instead assumes every outside component touching row 0 is part of\n    61\t#      the top legend strip.\n    62\t#    - Original source->target mapping was indexed by placeholder color. That assumption is\n    63\t#      broken by D7/2: color now only selects which sprite to stamp, while legend lookup is\n    64\t#      keyed by sprite area.\n    65\t#    - Original code expected every parsed legend item to be relevant. D13/0 breaks that too:\n    66\t#      the new solver must recover all real sprite areas first, then use only legend counts\n    67\t#      that match those areas.\n    68\t#    - Sparse counted sprites may be 4-disconnected, so extraction cannot rely on one single\n    69\t#      connected component spanning the full bbox. The solver unions all non-legend components\n    70\t#      of the same source color and checks the union bbox against the placeholder size.\n    71\t#\n    72\t# d) Placement legality:\n    73\t#    - The generator reserves a top band for legends, preventing sprite/frame collisions with\n    74\t#      legend entries and guaranteeing that row-0 colored components are legends only.\n    75\t#    - `random_free_location` with one-cell padding separates the frame, legend strip, and\n    76\t#      all outside sprites, so no objects touch or overlap.\n    77\t#    - Sprite masks always include opposite corners of their NxN box, ensuring that the union\n    78\t#      bbox exactly matches the placeholder block size even when the mask is disconnected.\n    79\t#\n    80\t# e) Visual observability:\n    81\t#    - A human can inspect the outside sprite for one placeholder color, count its colored\n    82\t#      cells, and then look for the same count in the top-left legend to infer the recolor.\n    83\t#    - The distractor dimension is visible because the legend contains more count entries than\n    84\t#      there are actual sprite areas. These extras cannot be dismissed by shape alone; they\n    85\t#      must be excluded by exact counting.\n    86\t#\n    87\t# f) Visual cleanliness:\n    88\t#    - All legend entries share one strip at the top. All sprites live below that strip.\n    89\t#      The frame is placed away from both via the reserve mask, so the scene stays segmented.\n    90\t#    - Each legend entry is monochrome and compact, with a single background gap between\n    91\t#      entries. This keeps the distractors legible without introducing another border motif.\n    92\t#\n    93\t# g) Change inferability:\n    94\t#    - Output colors remain directly visible in the legend, but only after inferring which\n    95\t#      count entries are live. Because placeholder colors repeat and each source color has\n    96\t#      one repeated sprite template, 2-4 samples are enough to see that count equality, not\n    97\t#      shape identity or legend order, drives the recoloring.\n    98\t#\n    99\t# h) Generator validation target:\n   100\t#    - Every generated sample must contain at least one unmatched legend count.\n   101\t#    - Every real sprite area must appear exactly once in the legend.\n   102\t#    - `main(input)` must equal the oracle output frame.\n   103\t#\n   104\t# i) New solver assumptions that the generator guarantees:\n   105\t#    - Only legend entries occupy row 0 outside the frame.\n   106\t#    - Real sprite areas are pairwise distinct.\n   107\t#    - Distractor legend counts are distinct from all real sprite areas.\n   108\t#    - For each placeholder color, the union of its non-legend outside components has the\n   109\t#      same bbox as that color's placeholder blocks.\n   110\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   111\t\n   112\t\n   113\tFRAME_COL = 5\n   114\tSPRITE_N_RANGE = (3, 5)             # N in {3, 4}\n   115\tGRID_ROWS_RANGE = (2, 4)\n   116\tGRID_COLS_RANGE = (3, 5)\n   117\tTOTAL_BLOCKS_RANGE = (6, 10)\n   118\tMAX_EMPTY_SLOTS = 2\n   119\tNUM_COLORS_RANGE = (2, 4)\n   120\tSPRITE_AREA_CHOICES = (2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7)\n   121\tMIN_FRAME_H = 13\n   122\tMIN_FRAME_W = 18\n   123\tMAX_FRAME_DIM = 21\n   124\tFRAME_MARGIN_SLACK = 4\n   125\tCANVAS_H_RANGE = (22, 31)\n   126\tCANVAS_W_RANGE = (23, 31)\n   127\tPATCH_PADDING = 1\n   128\tGEN_RETRIES = 400\n   129\tDISTRACTOR_RANGE = (1, 2)\n   130\t\n   131\tLEGEND_H = 2\n   132\tLEGEND_ENTRY_W = 4\n   133\tLEGEND_GAP = 1\n   134\tTOP_BAND_H = LEGEND_H + 1\n   135\tLEGEND_ORDER = (\n   136\t    (0, 0), (0, 1), (0, 2), (0, 3),\n   137\t    (1, 0), (1, 1), (1, 2), (1, 3),\n   138\t)\n   139\t\n   140\t\n   141\tdef _find_frame(g: np.ndarray, bg: int) -> tuple[int, tuple[int, int, int, int]]:\n   142\t    \"\"\"\n   143\t    Find a rectangular border component:\n   144\t      - all bbox-border cells are this color,\n   145\t      - bbox-interior is not entirely this color.\n   146\t    Return (frame_color, (r0,c0,r1,c1)).\n   147\t    \"\"\"\n   148\t    candidates = []\n   149\t    colors = [int(c) for c in np.unique(g) if int(c) != bg]\n   150\t    for col in colors:\n   151\t        for pts in components_mask(g == col, connectivity=4):\n   152\t            r0, c0, r1, c1 = bbox_coords(pts)\n   153\t            if r1 - r0 < 2 or c1 - c0 < 2:\n   154\t                continue\n   155\t            sub = g[r0 : r1 + 1, c0 : c1 + 1]\n   156\t            border = np.zeros(sub.shape, dtype=bool)\n   157\t            border[0, :] = True\n   158\t            border[-1, :] = True\n   159\t            border[:, 0] = True\n   160\t            border[:, -1] = True\n   161\t            if not np.all(sub[border] == col):\n   162\t                continue\n   163\t            if np.all(sub[~border] == col):\n   164\t                continue\n   165\t            candidates.append((col, (r0, c0, r1, c1)))\n   166\t    assert len(candidates) == 1, f\"expected exactly one rectangular frame component, found {len(candidates)}\"\n   167\t    frame_col, bbox = candidates[0]\n   168\t    return int(frame_col), bbox\n   169\t\n   170\t\n   171\tdef _bbox_hw(bbox: tuple[int, int, int, int]) -> tuple[int, int]:\n   172\t    return bbox[2] - bbox[0] + 1, bbox[3] - bbox[1] + 1\n   173\t\n   174\t\n   175\tdef _analyze_scene(grid: np.ndarray) -> dict:\n   176\t    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\n   177\t    bg = get_bg(g)\n   178\t    frame_col, (fr0, fc0, fr1, fc1) = _find_frame(g, bg)\n   179\t\n   180\t    crop = g[fr0 : fr1 + 1, fc0 : fc1 + 1]\n   181\t    h, w = crop.shape\n   182\t    assert h >= 3 and w >= 3, f\"frame too small for interior: {(h, w)}\"\n   183\t\n   184\t    inner_mask = np.zeros((h, w), dtype=bool)\n   185\t    inner_mask[1:-1, 1:-1] = True\n   186\t    placeholder_colors = set(map(int, np.unique(crop[inner_mask]))) - {bg, frame_col}\n   187\t    assert placeholder_colors, \"no placeholder colors found inside frame\"\n   188\t\n   189\t    placeholders: list[tuple[int, tuple[int, int, int, int]]] = []\n   190\t    for col in sorted(placeholder_colors):\n   191\t        for pts in components_mask((crop == col) & inner_mask, connectivity=4):\n   192\t            r0, c0, r1, c1 = bbox_coords(pts)\n   193\t            placeholders.append((int(col), (r0, c0, r1, c1)))\n   194\t\n   195\t    phw: dict[int, tuple[int, int]] = {}\n   196\t    for col in placeholder_colors:\n   197\t        dims = [_bbox_hw(b) for c, b in placeholders if c == col]\n   198\t        assert dims, f\"no placeholder component found for color {col}\"\n   199\t        unique_dims = sorted(set(dims))\n   200\t        assert len(unique_dims) == 1, f\"ambiguous placeholder sizes for color {col}: {unique_dims}\"\n   201\t        phw[int(col)] = unique_dims[0]\n   202\t\n   203\t    outside = np.ones(g.shape, dtype=bool)\n   204\t    outside[fr0 : fr1 + 1, fc0 : fc1 + 1] = False\n   205\t\n   206\t    comps = []\n   207\t    colors = [int(c) for c in np.unique(g) if int(c) not in (bg, frame_col)]\n   208\t    cid = 0\n   209\t    for col in colors:\n   210\t        for pts in components_mask((g == col) & outside, connectivity=4):\n   211\t            r0, c0, r1, c1 = bbox_coords(pts)\n   212\t            pts_tuples = [(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in pts]\n   213\t            comps.append(\n   214\t                {\n   215\t                    \"id\": cid,\n   216\t                    \"col\": int(col),\n   217\t                    \"pts\": pts_tuples,\n   218\t                    \"bbox\": (r0, c0, r1, c1),\n   219\t                    \"area\": len(pts_tuples),\n   220\t                }\n   221\t            )\n   222\t            cid += 1\n   223\t\n   224\t    legend_entries = [\n   225\t        {\n   226\t            \"x\": int(comp[\"bbox\"][1]),\n   227\t            \"color\": int(comp[\"col\"]),\n   228\t            \"count\": int(comp[\"area\"]),\n   229\t            \"id\": int(comp[\"id\"]),\n   230\t        }\n   231\t        for comp in comps\n   232\t        if comp[\"bbox\"][0] == 0\n   233\t    ]\n   234\t    legend_entries.sort(key=lambda entry: entry[\"x\"])\n   235\t    assert legend_entries, \"count legend must occupy the top row\"\n   236\t\n   237\t    legend_ids = {entry[\"id\"] for entry in legend_entries}\n   238\t    count_to_color: dict[int, int] = {}\n   239\t    for entry in legend_entries:\n   240\t        count = entry[\"count\"]\n   241\t        assert count not in count_to_color, f\"duplicate legend count {count}\"\n   242\t        count_to_color[count] = int(entry[\"color\"])\n   243\t\n   244\t    sprite_data: dict[int, tuple[tuple[tuple[int, int], ...], int, int, int]] = {}\n   245\t    for src_col in sorted(placeholder_colors):\n   246\t        all_candidates = [c for c in comps if c[\"col\"] == src_col and c[\"id\"] not in legend_ids]\n   247\t        assert all_candidates, f\"no sprite found for placeholder color {src_col}\"\n   248\t\n   249\t        r0 = min(c[\"bbox\"][0] for c in all_candidates)\n   250\t        c0 = min(c[\"bbox\"][1] for c in all_candidates)\n   251\t        r1 = max(c[\"bbox\"][2] for c in all_candidates)\n   252\t        c1 = max(c[\"bbox\"][3] for c in all_candidates)\n   253\t        pts_set = set()\n   254\t        for comp in all_candidates:\n   255\t            pts_set.update(comp[\"pts\"])\n   256\t\n   257\t        want_h, want_w = phw[int(src_col)]\n   258\t        assert (r1 - r0 + 1, c1 - c0 + 1) == (want_h, want_w), (\n   259\t            f\"sprite union bbox does not match placeholder size for color {src_col}\"\n   260\t        )\n\nexec\n/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/9/code.py | sed -n '260,520p'\" in /home/lixinyu/snap/new\n succeeded in 0ms:\n   260\t        )\n   261\t        coords = tuple(sorted((r - r0, c - c0) for r, c in pts_set))\n   262\t        area = len(coords)\n   263\t        sprite_data[int(src_col)] = (coords, want_h, want_w, area)\n   264\t\n   265\t    sprite_areas = [area for _coords, _sh, _sw, area in sprite_data.values()]\n   266\t    assert len(set(sprite_areas)) == len(sprite_areas), f\"sprite areas must be unique, got {sprite_areas}\"\n   267\t\n   268\t    color_map: dict[int, int] = {}\n   269\t    for src_col, (_coords, _sh, _sw, area) in sprite_data.items():\n   270\t        assert area in count_to_color, f\"no legend count matches sprite area {area}\"\n   271\t        color_map[int(src_col)] = int(count_to_color[area])\n   272\t\n   273\t    matched_counts = {area for area in sprite_areas}\n   274\t    distractor_counts = {entry[\"count\"] for entry in legend_entries if entry[\"count\"] not in matched_counts}\n   275\t    assert distractor_counts, \"legend must contain at least one unmatched count\"\n   276\t\n   277\t    return {\n   278\t        \"bg\": bg,\n   279\t        \"frame_col\": frame_col,\n   280\t        \"crop\": crop,\n   281\t        \"placeholders\": placeholders,\n   282\t        \"phw\": phw,\n   283\t        \"sprite_data\": sprite_data,\n   284\t        \"color_map\": color_map,\n   285\t        \"legend_entries\": legend_entries,\n   286\t        \"matched_counts\": matched_counts,\n   287\t        \"distractor_counts\": distractor_counts,\n   288\t        \"legend_count_total\": len(legend_entries),\n   289\t    }\n   290\t\n   291\t\n   292\tdef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n   293\t    \"\"\"\n   294\t    Fill the framed placeholders with external sprites, then recolor them using a counted legend with decoys.\n   295\t\n   296\t    Input structure:\n   297\t    - A gray rectangular frame contains solid-color placeholder blocks on background cells.\n   298\t    - Outside the frame there is one sprite template for each placeholder color, rendered in that same source color.\n   299\t    - The top-left of the whole grid contains a legend strip of compact single-color entries whose pixel counts encode keys; some legend entries are extra and match no sprite.\n   300\t\n   301\t    Rule:\n   302\t    - Recover each source-colored sprite outside the frame and count how many colored cells it contains.\n   303\t    - Read every top-row legend component as a candidate mapping from pixel count to output color.\n   304\t    - Keep only the legend counts that actually occur among the recovered sprites, ignoring unmatched legend entries.\n   305\t    - Replace every placeholder block with its sprite shape and recolor it to the output color associated with that sprite's pixel count.\n   306\t\n   307\t    Key insight: The legend no longer names shapes or source colors. The only reliable key is the sprite's colored-cell count, and the extra legend counts must be filtered out by comparing them against the real sprites.\n   308\t    \"\"\"\n   309\t    info = _analyze_scene(grid)\n   310\t    crop = info[\"crop\"]\n   311\t    bg = info[\"bg\"]\n   312\t    placeholders = info[\"placeholders\"]\n   313\t    sprite_data = info[\"sprite_data\"]\n   314\t    color_map = info[\"color_map\"]\n   315\t\n   316\t    out = crop.copy()\n   317\t    out[1:-1, 1:-1] = bg\n   318\t\n   319\t    for src_col, (pr0, pc0, pr1, pc1) in placeholders:\n   320\t        assert src_col in sprite_data and src_col in color_map, (\n   321\t            f\"placeholder color {src_col} missing sprite or legend mapping\"\n   322\t        )\n   323\t        coords, sh, sw, _area = sprite_data[src_col]\n   324\t        tgt_col = int(color_map[src_col])\n   325\t        assert (pr1 - pr0 + 1, pc1 - pc0 + 1) == (sh, sw), (\n   326\t            f\"placeholder size does not match sprite for color {src_col}\"\n   327\t        )\n   328\t        for dr, dc in coords:\n   329\t            out[pr0 + dr, pc0 + dc] = tgt_col\n   330\t\n   331\t    return out\n   332\t\n   333\t\n   334\tdef _legend_patch(entries: list[tuple[int, int]], bg: int) -> np.ndarray:\n   335\t    \"\"\"Build the top-left count legend from (pixel_count, target_color) pairs.\"\"\"\n   336\t    width = len(entries) * LEGEND_ENTRY_W + max(0, len(entries) - 1) * LEGEND_GAP\n   337\t    patch = np.full((LEGEND_H, width), bg, dtype=int)\n   338\t    for idx, (pixel_count, color) in enumerate(entries):\n   339\t        c0 = idx * (LEGEND_ENTRY_W + LEGEND_GAP)\n   340\t        for rr, cc in LEGEND_ORDER[:pixel_count]:\n   341\t            patch[rr, c0 + cc] = int(color)\n   342\t    return patch\n   343\t\n   344\t\n   345\tdef _sprite_mask(n: int, area: int) -> np.ndarray:\n   346\t    \"\"\"Generate an NxN sparse mask with exact area and full NxN union bbox.\"\"\"\n   347\t    assert 2 <= area <= min(len(LEGEND_ORDER), n * n), f\"unsupported area {area} for n={n}\"\n   348\t    mask = np.zeros((n, n), dtype=bool)\n   349\t\n   350\t    corner_pairs = [\n   351\t        ((0, 0), (n - 1, n - 1)),\n   352\t        ((0, n - 1), (n - 1, 0)),\n   353\t    ]\n   354\t    a, b = random.choice(corner_pairs)\n   355\t    chosen = {a, b}\n   356\t    candidates = [(r, c) for r in range(n) for c in range(n) if (r, c) not in chosen]\n   357\t    random.shuffle(candidates)\n   358\t    while len(chosen) < area:\n   359\t        chosen.add(candidates.pop())\n   360\t\n   361\t    for r, c in chosen:\n   362\t        mask[r, c] = True\n   363\t    return mask\n   364\t\n   365\t\n   366\tdef _colored_sprite(mask: np.ndarray, color: int, bg: int) -> np.ndarray:\n   367\t    out = np.full(mask.shape, bg, dtype=int)\n   368\t    out[mask] = int(color)\n   369\t    return out\n   370\t\n   371\t\n   372\tdef _content_extent(n: int, grid_rows: int, grid_cols: int) -> tuple[int, int]:\n   373\t    return (grid_rows * n + grid_rows - 1, grid_cols * n + grid_cols - 1)\n   374\t\n   375\t\n   376\tdef _choose_structure() -> tuple[int, int, int, int, int] | None:\n   377\t    total = random.randint(*TOTAL_BLOCKS_RANGE)\n   378\t    options = []\n   379\t    for n in range(*SPRITE_N_RANGE):\n   380\t        for rows in range(*GRID_ROWS_RANGE):\n   381\t            for cols in range(*GRID_COLS_RANGE):\n   382\t                ch, cw = _content_extent(n, rows, cols)\n   383\t                base_fh = ch + 4\n   384\t                base_fw = cw + 4\n   385\t                slots = rows * cols\n   386\t                empty = slots - total\n   387\t                if base_fh <= MAX_FRAME_DIM and base_fw <= MAX_FRAME_DIM and 0 <= empty <= MAX_EMPTY_SLOTS:\n   388\t                    options.append((n, rows, cols, empty, total))\n   389\t    return random.choice(options) if options else None\n   390\t\n   391\t\n   392\tdef _choose_empty_slots(\n   393\t    rows: int, cols: int, empty_count: int\n   394\t) -> tuple[set[tuple[int, int]], list[tuple[int, int]]]:\n   395\t    slots = [(r, c) for r in range(rows) for c in range(cols)]\n   396\t    valid = []\n   397\t    for combo in itertools.combinations(slots, empty_count):\n   398\t        empty = set(combo)\n   399\t        filled = [s for s in slots if s not in empty]\n   400\t        if len({r for r, _ in filled}) == rows and len({c for _, c in filled}) == cols:\n   401\t            valid.append(empty)\n   402\t    empty_slots = random.choice(valid)\n   403\t    filled_slots = [s for s in slots if s not in empty_slots]\n   404\t    random.shuffle(filled_slots)\n   405\t    return empty_slots, filled_slots\n   406\t\n   407\t\n   408\tdef _make_bordered_frame(h: int, w: int, bg: int) -> np.ndarray:\n   409\t    frame = np.full((h, w), bg, dtype=int)\n   410\t    frame[0, :] = frame[-1, :] = FRAME_COL\n   411\t    frame[:, 0] = frame[:, -1] = FRAME_COL\n   412\t    return frame\n   413\t\n   414\t\n   415\tdef _place_patch(\n   416\t    grid: np.ndarray, reserve: np.ndarray, patch: np.ndarray, bg: int, *, transparent: bool\n   417\t) -> bool:\n   418\t    blocker = np.full(patch.shape, FRAME_COL, dtype=int)\n   419\t    try:\n   420\t        r, c = random_free_location(reserve, blocker, transparent=bg, padding=PATCH_PADDING)\n   421\t    except ValueError:\n   422\t        return False\n   423\t    paste(reserve, blocker, r, c)\n   424\t    paste(grid, patch, r, c, transparent=bg if transparent else None)\n   425\t    return True\n   426\t\n   427\t\n   428\tdef _gen_attempt() -> np.ndarray | None:\n   429\t    struct = _choose_structure()\n   430\t    if struct is None:\n   431\t        return None\n   432\t    n, rows, cols, empty_count, _ = struct\n   433\t\n   434\t    bg = random.choice([c for c in range(10) if c != FRAME_COL])\n   435\t    usable = [c for c in range(10) if c not in (bg, FRAME_COL)]\n   436\t\n   437\t    k = random.randint(*NUM_COLORS_RANGE)\n   438\t    max_distractors = min(DISTRACTOR_RANGE[1], len(SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES) - k)\n   439\t    if max_distractors < DISTRACTOR_RANGE[0]:\n   440\t        return None\n   441\t    distractor_count = random.randint(DISTRACTOR_RANGE[0], max_distractors)\n   442\t\n   443\t    src_cols = random.sample(usable, k)\n   444\t    tgt_cols = random.sample(usable, k)\n   445\t\n   446\t    counts = random.sample(SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES, k + distractor_count)\n   447\t    real_counts = counts[:k]\n   448\t    distractor_counts = counts[k:]\n   449\t\n   450\t    color_to_tgt = dict(zip(src_cols, tgt_cols))\n   451\t    masks = {src: _sprite_mask(n, area) for src, area in zip(src_cols, real_counts)}\n   452\t\n   453\t    legend_items = list(zip(real_counts, tgt_cols))\n   454\t    distractor_colors = [random.choice(usable) for _ in range(distractor_count)]\n   455\t    legend_items.extend(zip(distractor_counts, distractor_colors))\n   456\t    random.shuffle(legend_items)\n   457\t    legend_patch = _legend_patch(legend_items, bg)\n   458\t    legend_w = legend_patch.shape[1]\n   459\t\n   460\t    ch, cw = _content_extent(n, rows, cols)\n   461\t    min_fh = max(MIN_FRAME_H, ch + 4)\n   462\t    min_fw = max(MIN_FRAME_W, cw + 4)\n   463\t    frame_h = random.randint(min_fh, min(MAX_FRAME_DIM, max(min_fh, ch + 2 + FRAME_MARGIN_SLACK)))\n   464\t    frame_w = random.randint(min_fw, min(MAX_FRAME_DIM, max(min_fw, cw + 2 + FRAME_MARGIN_SLACK)))\n   465\t    y_margin = frame_h - 2 - ch\n   466\t    x_margin = frame_w - 2 - cw\n   467\t    top_margin = random.randint(1, y_margin - 1)\n   468\t    left_margin = random.randint(1, x_margin - 1)\n   469\t\n   470\t    _, filled_slots = _choose_empty_slots(rows, cols, empty_count)\n   471\t    cell_colors = {}\n   472\t    for slot, col in zip(filled_slots[:k], src_cols):\n   473\t        cell_colors[slot] = col\n   474\t    for slot in filled_slots[k:]:\n   475\t        cell_colors[slot] = random.choice(src_cols)\n   476\t\n   477\t    input_frame = _make_bordered_frame(frame_h, frame_w, bg)\n   478\t    output_frame = _make_bordered_frame(frame_h, frame_w, bg)\n   479\t    for (rr, cc), src in cell_colors.items():\n   480\t        r0 = 1 + top_margin + rr * (n + 1)\n   481\t        c0 = 1 + left_margin + cc * (n + 1)\n   482\t        paste(input_frame, np.full((n, n), src, dtype=int), r0, c0)\n   483\t        paste(output_frame, _colored_sprite(masks[src], color_to_tgt[src], bg), r0, c0, transparent=bg)\n   484\t\n   485\t    sprite_budget = k * (n * n + 6)\n   486\t    possible_dims = [\n   487\t        (h, w)\n   488\t        for h in range(*CANVAS_H_RANGE)\n   489\t        for w in range(*CANVAS_W_RANGE)\n   490\t        if h >= frame_h + TOP_BAND_H\n   491\t        and w >= max(frame_w, legend_w)\n   492\t        and h * w - frame_h * frame_w - TOP_BAND_H * w >= sprite_budget\n   493\t    ]\n   494\t    if not possible_dims:\n   495\t        return None\n   496\t\n   497\t    h, w = random.choice(possible_dims)\n   498\t    grid = np.full((h, w), bg, dtype=int)\n   499\t    reserve = np.full((h, w), bg, dtype=int)\n   500\t    reserve[:TOP_BAND_H, :] = FRAME_COL\n   501\t\n   502\t    paste(grid, legend_patch, 0, 0, transparent=bg)\n   503\t\n   504\t    frame_blocker = np.full((frame_h, frame_w), FRAME_COL, dtype=int)\n   505\t    try:\n   506\t        fr0, fc0 = random_free_location(reserve, frame_blocker, transparent=bg, padding=PATCH_PADDING)\n   507\t    except ValueError:\n   508\t        return None\n   509\t    paste(grid, input_frame, fr0, fc0)\n   510\t    paste(reserve, frame_blocker, fr0, fc0)\n   511\t\n   512\t    patches = [_colored_sprite(masks[src], src, bg) for src in src_cols]\n   513\t    random.shuffle(patches)\n   514\t    patches.sort(key=lambda patch: patch.size, reverse=True)\n   515\t    for patch in patches:\n   516\t        if not _place_patch(grid, reserve, patch, bg, transparent=True):\n   517\t            return None\n   518\t\n   519\t    try:\n   520\t        info = _analyze_scene(grid)\n\ndiff --git a/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/9/code.py b/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/9/code.py\nindex 5118d5b845ab2464b87c40373164ab3076d9256f..fe289f311fa3d2eb7cae6b98357ee4db4ce110f3\n--- a/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/9/code.py\n+++ b/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/9/code.py\n@@ -2,107 +2,122 @@\n # combo_spec: D7/2+D13/0\n # Name: 数量编码图例+干扰条目\n \n+import importlib.util\n import itertools\n+from pathlib import Path\n import random\n+import sys\n \n import numpy as np\n \n-from arc_utils import bbox_coords, components_mask, get_bg, paste, random_free_location\n+ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[4]\n+if str(ROOT) not in sys.path:\n+    sys.path.append(str(ROOT))\n \n+try:\n+    from arc_utils import bbox_coords, components_mask, get_bg, paste, random_free_location\n+except ModuleNotFoundError:\n+    _spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\"_combo_arc_utils\", ROOT / \"solvers\" / \"arc_utils.py\")\n+    _mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(_spec)\n+    assert _spec.loader is not None\n+    _spec.loader.exec_module(_mod)\n+    bbox_coords = _mod.bbox_coords\n+    components_mask = _mod.components_mask\n+    get_bg = _mod.get_bg\n+    paste = _mod.paste\n+    random_free_location = _mod.random_free_location\n \n # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n-# Design analysis for the fused D7/2 + D13/0 variant\n+# Design analysis for the combo variant\n #\n # a) Concrete behavior and trace:\n-#    - Keep the original large gray frame with solid-color placeholder blocks inside.\n-#    - Keep one outside sprite template per placeholder color; each sprite still uses the\n-#      placeholder color and has the same N x N bbox as the matching blocks inside the frame.\n-#    - Replace the old overlapping two-color legend with a top-left strip of monochrome\n-#      count codes. Each code is a compact 3x3 nested stencil whose area is the key and\n-#      whose color is the recolor target.\n-#    - Add 1-2 extra legend entries whose counts do not match any real sprite. Those entries\n-#      are visible in the same strip, so solver must count every sprite, compare that count\n-#      against all legend entries, and ignore the unmatched ones.\n-#    - Example: suppose a cyan external sprite occupies exactly 5 cells in a 4x4 bbox, while\n-#      the legend strip contains orange-5, red-7, yellow-3, and teal-8 entries. Cyan blocks\n-#      inside the frame become the 5-cell sprite recolored to orange. The 7/3/8 entries stay\n-#      unused if no sprite has those counts. In the original task, recoloring came from a\n-#      direct shape-color legend pair; here it comes from sprite area, and some legend items\n-#      are decoys.\n+#    - Keep the original backbone: one gray rectangular frame, solid placeholder blocks\n+#      inside the frame, and one source-colored sprite template outside the frame for each\n+#      placeholder color.\n+#    - Replace the original overlapping two-color legend with a fixed top-left legend strip.\n+#      Each legend entry is now a compact monochrome stencil whose area encodes a number.\n+#      The legend color is the output color, while the number of colored pixels is the key.\n+#    - Add mandatory distractor legend entries. These extra count codes are rendered exactly\n+#      like the real legend entries but their pixel counts do not match any real sprite area.\n+#    - Example: suppose blue placeholders correspond to a 4x4 outside sprite with exactly\n+#      5 colored cells, and green placeholders correspond to a 4x4 sprite with 3 cells.\n+#      The legend may show orange=5 cells, red=3 cells, and yellow=6 cells. The solver must\n+#      count the blue sprite, match 5 to orange, count the green sprite, match 3 to red,\n+#      and ignore the yellow 6-cell legend item. In the original task, recoloring came from\n+#      direct shape-color legend pairs; in this fusion, recoloring requires count matching\n+#      plus filtering unmatched legend counts.\n #\n # b) Complexity calibration:\n-#    - Real sprite counts are unique and chosen from a small visual vocabulary 2..8. This\n-#      keeps counting tractable while still giving enough room for distractors.\n-#    - There are 2-5 placeholder colors, so each sample has repeated evidence inside the frame\n-#      but not so many codes that the top legend becomes unreadable.\n-#    - Distractors are mandatory but capped at 1-2, which makes the extra filtering visible\n-#      without drowning out the true legend entries.\n+#    - Restrict real sprite areas to a small vocabulary {2,3,4,5,6,7}. This makes counting\n+#      observable, while still leaving room for 1-2 unmatched legend counts in the same band.\n+#    - Limit the number of placeholder colors to 2-4. That preserves repeated evidence inside\n+#      the frame and avoids exhausting the count vocabulary once distractors are added.\n+#    - Keep sprite boxes at 3x3 or 4x4. Larger boxes would make exact counting slower and add\n+#      clutter; smaller boxes would not support enough distinct counted patterns.\n #\n-# c) Implicit assumption audit against the original solver:\n-#    - Old legend parsing assumed overlapping two-color glyphs and source-color inference from\n-#      pair structure. That breaks completely; fused solver instead reads monochrome entries\n-#      anchored on the top row and uses component area as the code.\n-#    - Old sprite extraction only had to exclude legend components paired by overlap. That is\n-#      no longer valid because legend entries now have a single color and may share colors with\n-#      real sprites. The generator therefore reserves the whole top band for legends, and the\n-#      solver excludes all top-band components from sprite recovery.\n-#    - Count-based recoloring only works if different placeholder colors do not share the same\n-#      sprite area. The generator guarantees unique real counts, and solver asserts that.\n-#    - Distractors are only safe if their counts are distinct from all real counts. The\n-#      generator enforces that; solver checks that legend counts form a strict superset of\n-#      sprite counts rather than an arbitrary unrelated set.\n+# c) Implicit-assumption audit against the original solver:\n+#    - Original legend parsing assumed small overlapping two-color regions; that is no longer\n+#      true. The new solver instead assumes every outside component touching row 0 is part of\n+#      the top legend strip.\n+#    - Original source->target mapping was indexed by placeholder color. That assumption is\n+#      broken by D7/2: color now only selects which sprite to stamp, while legend lookup is\n+#      keyed by sprite area.\n+#    - Original code expected every parsed legend item to be relevant. D13/0 breaks that too:\n+#      the new solver must recover all real sprite areas first, then use only legend counts\n+#      that match those areas.\n+#    - Sparse counted sprites may be 4-disconnected, so extraction cannot rely on one single\n+#      connected component spanning the full bbox. The solver unions all non-legend components\n+#      of the same source color and checks the union bbox against the placeholder size.\n #\n # d) Placement legality:\n-#    - The top band is reserved before frame placement, so no sprite or frame cell can touch\n-#      the legend strip.\n-#    - Frame, external sprites, and legend entries are all placed with a one-cell padding gap\n-#      via `random_free_location`, preventing overlap or accidental touching.\n-#    - Sprite masks always include opposite corners of the N x N bbox, so the union bbox seen\n-#      by the solver exactly matches the placeholder block size even when the sprite is sparse\n-#      or disconnected.\n+#    - The generator reserves a top band for legends, preventing sprite/frame collisions with\n+#      legend entries and guaranteeing that row-0 colored components are legends only.\n+#    - `random_free_location` with one-cell padding separates the frame, legend strip, and\n+#      all outside sprites, so no objects touch or overlap.\n+#    - Sprite masks always include opposite corners of their NxN box, ensuring that the union\n+#      bbox exactly matches the placeholder block size even when the mask is disconnected.\n #\n # e) Visual observability:\n-#    - A human can recover the rule by counting cells in an outside sprite, then scanning the\n-#      top strip for the legend entry with the same count to get the output color.\n-#    - The extra legend items are not hidden metadata; they are visible unmatched counts in the\n-#      same legend family, so the added reasoning load is observable from the grids alone.\n+#    - A human can inspect the outside sprite for one placeholder color, count its colored\n+#      cells, and then look for the same count in the top-left legend to infer the recolor.\n+#    - The distractor dimension is visible because the legend contains more count entries than\n+#      there are actual sprite areas. These extras cannot be dismissed by shape alone; they\n+#      must be excluded by exact counting.\n #\n # f) Visual cleanliness:\n-#    - Legends live in one dedicated band, the frame occupies one compact rectangle elsewhere,\n-#      and sprites are separate free patches. This keeps object categories spatially separated.\n-#    - All legend entries share one simple 3x3 encoding template, reducing clutter compared with\n-#      arbitrary glyphs or mixed overlay patterns.\n+#    - All legend entries share one strip at the top. All sprites live below that strip.\n+#      The frame is placed away from both via the reserve mask, so the scene stays segmented.\n+#    - Each legend entry is monochrome and compact, with a single background gap between\n+#      entries. This keeps the distractors legible without introducing another border motif.\n #\n # g) Change inferability:\n-#    - Output colors are structurally indicated by the legend-entry colors, not by raw palette\n-#      ids. Because counts repeat via multiple placeholders of the same color, a few samples are\n-#      enough to show that equal source colors do not determine output colors on their own.\n-#    - Distractors do not affect placed objects, so the solver must infer that only counts seen\n-#      on real sprites are actionable.\n+#    - Output colors remain directly visible in the legend, but only after inferring which\n+#      count entries are live. Because placeholder colors repeat and each source color has\n+#      one repeated sprite template, 2-4 samples are enough to see that count equality, not\n+#      shape identity or legend order, drives the recoloring.\n #\n # h) Generator validation target:\n-#    - Every generated sample must contain at least one unused legend count.\n-#    - Every real sprite count must appear exactly once in the legend strip.\n-#    - `main(input)` must match the generator's output-frame oracle.\n+#    - Every generated sample must contain at least one unmatched legend count.\n+#    - Every real sprite area must appear exactly once in the legend.\n+#    - `main(input)` must equal the oracle output frame.\n #\n-# i) New solver assumptions that the generator explicitly guarantees:\n-#    - Every legend component touches row 0 because the strip is pasted at the top-left corner.\n-#    - No non-legend object touches row 0 because the entire top band is reserved.\n-#    - Each placeholder color has exactly one external sprite union with bbox equal to the\n-#      placeholder size.\n-#    - Sprite counts are pairwise distinct, and legend counts are pairwise distinct.\n+# i) New solver assumptions that the generator guarantees:\n+#    - Only legend entries occupy row 0 outside the frame.\n+#    - Real sprite areas are pairwise distinct.\n+#    - Distractor legend counts are distinct from all real sprite areas.\n+#    - For each placeholder color, the union of its non-legend outside components has the\n+#      same bbox as that color's placeholder blocks.\n # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n \n \n FRAME_COL = 5\n-SPRITE_N_RANGE = (3, 6)\n+SPRITE_N_RANGE = (3, 5)             # N in {3, 4}\n GRID_ROWS_RANGE = (2, 4)\n GRID_COLS_RANGE = (3, 5)\n TOTAL_BLOCKS_RANGE = (6, 10)\n MAX_EMPTY_SLOTS = 2\n-NUM_COLORS_RANGE = (2, 5)\n-SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES = (2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8)\n-DISTRACTOR_RANGE = (1, 2)\n+NUM_COLORS_RANGE = (2, 4)\n+SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES = (2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7)\n MIN_FRAME_H = 13\n MIN_FRAME_W = 18\n MAX_FRAME_DIM = 21\n@@ -110,22 +125,16 @@\n CANVAS_H_RANGE = (22, 31)\n CANVAS_W_RANGE = (23, 31)\n PATCH_PADDING = 1\n-GEN_RETRIES = 500\n+GEN_RETRIES = 400\n+DISTRACTOR_RANGE = (1, 2)\n \n-LEGEND_H = 3\n-LEGEND_ENTRY_W = 3\n+LEGEND_H = 2\n+LEGEND_ENTRY_W = 4\n LEGEND_GAP = 1\n TOP_BAND_H = LEGEND_H + 1\n LEGEND_ORDER = (\n-    (0, 0),\n-    (0, 1),\n-    (0, 2),\n-    (1, 0),\n-    (1, 1),\n-    (1, 2),\n-    (2, 0),\n-    (2, 1),\n-    (2, 2),\n+    (0, 0), (0, 1), (0, 2), (0, 3),\n+    (1, 0), (1, 1), (1, 2), (1, 3),\n )\n \n \n@@ -161,45 +170,6 @@\n \n def _bbox_hw(bbox: tuple[int, int, int, int]) -> tuple[int, int]:\n     return bbox[2] - bbox[0] + 1, bbox[3] - bbox[1] + 1\n-\n-\n-def _legend_entries(comps: list[dict]) -> list[tuple[int, int, int, int]]:\n-    \"\"\"Return legend entries as (x_pos, out_color, pixel_count, comp_id), sorted by x.\"\"\"\n-    entries = [\n-        (int(comp[\"bbox\"][1]), int(comp[\"col\"]), int(comp[\"area\"]), int(comp[\"id\"]))\n-        for comp in comps\n-        if comp[\"bbox\"][0] == 0 and comp[\"bbox\"][2] < LEGEND_H\n-    ]\n-    entries.sort(key=lambda item: item[0])\n-    return entries\n-\n-\n-def _extract_sprite_data(\n-    comps: list[dict],\n-    placeholder_colors: set[int],\n-    phw: dict[int, tuple[int, int]],\n-    legend_ids: set[int],\n-) -> dict[int, tuple[tuple[tuple[int, int], ...], int, int, int]]:\n-    sprite_data: dict[int, tuple[tuple[tuple[int, int], ...], int, int, int]] = {}\n-    for src_col in sorted(placeholder_colors):\n-        all_candidates = [c for c in comps if c[\"col\"] == src_col and c[\"id\"] not in legend_ids]\n-        assert all_candidates, f\"no sprite found for placeholder color {src_col}\"\n-\n-        pts_set = set()\n-        r0 = min(c[\"bbox\"][0] for c in all_candidates)\n-        c0 = min(c[\"bbox\"][1] for c in all_candidates)\n-        r1 = max(c[\"bbox\"][2] for c in all_candidates)\n-        c1 = max(c[\"bbox\"][3] for c in all_candidates)\n-        for comp in all_candidates:\n-            pts_set.update(comp[\"pts\"])\n-\n-        want_h, want_w = phw[src_col]\n-        assert (r1 - r0 + 1, c1 - c0 + 1) == (want_h, want_w), (\n-            f\"sprite union bbox does not match placeholder size for color {src_col}\"\n-        )\n-        coords = tuple(sorted((r - r0, c - c0) for r, c in pts_set))\n-        sprite_data[src_col] = (coords, want_h, want_w, len(coords))\n-    return sprite_data\n \n \n def _analyze_scene(grid: np.ndarray) -> dict:\n@@ -220,7 +190,7 @@\n     for col in sorted(placeholder_colors):\n         for pts in components_mask((crop == col) & inner_mask, connectivity=4):\n             r0, c0, r1, c1 = bbox_coords(pts)\n-            placeholders.append((col, (r0, c0, r1, c1)))\n+            placeholders.append((int(col), (r0, c0, r1, c1)))\n \n     phw: dict[int, tuple[int, int]] = {}\n     for col in placeholder_colors:\n@@ -228,7 +198,7 @@\n         assert dims, f\"no placeholder component found for color {col}\"\n         unique_dims = sorted(set(dims))\n         assert len(unique_dims) == 1, f\"ambiguous placeholder sizes for color {col}: {unique_dims}\"\n-        phw[col] = unique_dims[0]\n+        phw[int(col)] = unique_dims[0]\n \n     outside = np.ones(g.shape, dtype=bool)\n     outside[fr0 : fr1 + 1, fc0 : fc1 + 1] = False\n@@ -251,28 +221,58 @@\n             )\n             cid += 1\n \n-    legend = _legend_entries(comps)\n-    assert legend, \"count legend must occupy the top row\"\n-    legend_ids = {entry[3] for entry in legend}\n+    legend_entries = [\n+        {\n+            \"x\": int(comp[\"bbox\"][1]),\n+            \"color\": int(comp[\"col\"]),\n+            \"count\": int(comp[\"area\"]),\n+            \"id\": int(comp[\"id\"]),\n+        }\n+        for comp in comps\n+        if comp[\"bbox\"][0] == 0\n+    ]\n+    legend_entries.sort(key=lambda entry: entry[\"x\"])\n+    assert legend_entries, \"count legend must occupy the top row\"\n+\n+    legend_ids = {entry[\"id\"] for entry in legend_entries}\n+    count_to_color: dict[int, int] = {}\n+    for entry in legend_entries:\n+        count = entry[\"count\"]\n+        assert count not in count_to_color, f\"duplicate legend count {count}\"\n+        count_to_color[count] = int(entry[\"color\"])\n+\n+    sprite_data: dict[int, tuple[tuple[tuple[int, int], ...], int, int, int]] = {}\n+    for src_col in sorted(placeholder_colors):\n+        all_candidates = [c for c in comps if c[\"col\"] == src_col and c[\"id\"] not in legend_ids]\n+        assert all_candidates, f\"no sprite found for placeholder color {src_col}\"\n+\n+        r0 = min(c[\"bbox\"][0] for c in all_candidates)\n+        c0 = min(c[\"bbox\"][1] for c in all_candidates)\n+        r1 = max(c[\"bbox\"][2] for c in all_candidates)\n+        c1 = max(c[\"bbox\"][3] for c in all_candidates)\n+        pts_set = set()\n+        for comp in all_candidates:\n+            pts_set.update(comp[\"pts\"])\n+\n+        want_h, want_w = phw[int(src_col)]\n+        assert (r1 - r0 + 1, c1 - c0 + 1) == (want_h, want_w), (\n+            f\"sprite union bbox does not match placeholder size for color {src_col}\"\n+        )\n+        coords = tuple(sorted((r - r0, c - c0) for r, c in pts_set))\n+        area = len(coords)\n+        sprite_data[int(src_col)] = (coords, want_h, want_w, area)\n \n-    count_to_tgt: dict[int, int] = {}\n-    for _x, out_col, pixel_count, _cid in legend:\n-        assert pixel_count not in count_to_tgt, f\"duplicate legend count {pixel_count}\"\n-        count_to_tgt[pixel_count] = int(out_col)\n+    sprite_areas = [area for _coords, _sh, _sw, area in sprite_data.values()]\n+    assert len(set(sprite_areas)) == len(sprite_areas), f\"sprite areas must be unique, got {sprite_areas}\"\n \n-    sprite_data = _extract_sprite_data(comps, placeholder_colors, phw, legend_ids)\n-    sprite_counts = [area for _coords, _sh, _sw, area in sprite_data.values()]\n-    assert len(set(sprite_counts)) == len(sprite_counts), \"sprite counts must be unique in this variant\"\n-    sprite_count_set = set(sprite_counts)\n-    legend_count_set = set(count_to_tgt)\n-    assert sprite_count_set.issubset(legend_count_set), (\n-        f\"legend counts {sorted(legend_count_set)} do not cover sprite areas {sorted(sprite_count_set)}\"\n-    )\n+    color_map: dict[int, int] = {}\n+    for src_col, (_coords, _sh, _sw, area) in sprite_data.items():\n+        assert area in count_to_color, f\"no legend count matches sprite area {area}\"\n+        color_map[int(src_col)] = int(count_to_color[area])\n \n-    color_map = {src_col: int(count_to_tgt[area]) for src_col, (_coords, _sh, _sw, area) in sprite_data.items()}\n-    distractor_counts = sorted(legend_count_set - sprite_count_set)\n-    matched_counts = sorted(sprite_count_set)\n-    assert distractor_counts, \"legend must include at least one unused count\"\n+    matched_counts = {area for area in sprite_areas}\n+    distractor_counts = {entry[\"count\"] for entry in legend_entries if entry[\"count\"] not in matched_counts}\n+    assert distractor_counts, \"legend must contain at least one unmatched count\"\n \n     return {\n         \"bg\": bg,\n@@ -282,34 +282,29 @@\n         \"phw\": phw,\n         \"sprite_data\": sprite_data,\n         \"color_map\": color_map,\n-        \"legend_count_set\": legend_count_set,\n+        \"legend_entries\": legend_entries,\n         \"matched_counts\": matched_counts,\n         \"distractor_counts\": distractor_counts,\n+        \"legend_count_total\": len(legend_entries),\n     }\n \n \n def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n     \"\"\"\n-    Replace framed placeholders with outside sprites and recolor them through a count-coded legend strip.\n+    Fill the framed placeholders with external sprites, then recolor them using a counted legend with decoys.\n \n     Input structure:\n-    - A gray rectangular frame encloses a grid of solid-color placeholder blocks on a background field.\n-    - Outside the frame there is one source-colored sprite template for each placeholder color.\n-    - Along the top-left edge there is a legend strip of small monochrome count codes, and some of those\n-      legend entries are distractors whose counts do not match any real sprite.\n+    - A gray rectangular frame contains solid-color placeholder blocks on background cells.\n+    - Outside the frame there is one sprite template for each placeholder color, rendered in that same source color.\n+    - The top-left of the whole grid contains a legend strip of compact single-color entries whose pixel counts encode keys; some legend entries are extra and match no sprite.\n \n     Rule:\n-    - Recover each sprite by taking all non-legend outside components of the same color and matching their\n-      union bbox to the placeholder size.\n-    - Count the colored cells in that recovered sprite and use that count, not the sprite silhouette, as the\n-      lookup key into the top legend strip.\n-    - Ignore legend entries whose counts are never realized by any recovered sprite.\n-    - Stamp every recovered sprite into each matching placeholder slot and recolor it with the color of the\n-      legend entry that has the same pixel count.\n+    - Recover each source-colored sprite outside the frame and count how many colored cells it contains.\n+    - Read every top-row legend component as a candidate mapping from pixel count to output color.\n+    - Keep only the legend counts that actually occur among the recovered sprites, ignoring unmatched legend entries.\n+    - Replace every placeholder block with its sprite shape and recolor it to the output color associated with that sprite's pixel count.\n \n-    Key insight: The legend no longer tells you which shape to use; the outside sprite color still selects\n-    the shape, but the final recolor comes only from matching sprite area to a count legend that includes\n-    extra decoy counts.\n+    Key insight: The legend no longer names shapes or source colors. The only reliable key is the sprite's colored-cell count, and the extra legend counts must be filtered out by comparing them against the real sprites.\n     \"\"\"\n     info = _analyze_scene(grid)\n     crop = info[\"crop\"]\n@@ -337,7 +332,7 @@\n \n \n def _legend_patch(entries: list[tuple[int, int]], bg: int) -> np.ndarray:\n-    \"\"\"Build the top-left legend strip from (pixel_count, target_color) pairs.\"\"\"\n+    \"\"\"Build the top-left count legend from (pixel_count, target_color) pairs.\"\"\"\n     width = len(entries) * LEGEND_ENTRY_W + max(0, len(entries) - 1) * LEGEND_GAP\n     patch = np.full((LEGEND_H, width), bg, dtype=int)\n     for idx, (pixel_count, color) in enumerate(entries):\n@@ -349,7 +344,7 @@\n \n def _sprite_mask(n: int, area: int) -> np.ndarray:\n     \"\"\"Generate an NxN sparse mask with exact area and full NxN union bbox.\"\"\"\n-    assert 2 <= area <= min(len(LEGEND_ORDER) - 1, n * n - 1), f\"unsupported area {area} for n={n}\"\n+    assert 2 <= area <= min(len(LEGEND_ORDER), n * n), f\"unsupported area {area} for n={n}\"\n     mask = np.zeros((n, n), dtype=bool)\n \n     corner_pairs = [\n@@ -440,16 +435,18 @@\n     usable = [c for c in range(10) if c not in (bg, FRAME_COL)]\n \n     k = random.randint(*NUM_COLORS_RANGE)\n-    src_cols = random.sample(usable, k)\n-    tgt_cols = random.sample(usable, k)\n-    real_counts = random.sample(SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES, k)\n-    remaining_counts = [count for count in SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES if count not in real_counts]\n-    max_distractors = min(DISTRACTOR_RANGE[1], len(remaining_counts))\n+    max_distractors = min(DISTRACTOR_RANGE[1], len(SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES) - k)\n     if max_distractors < DISTRACTOR_RANGE[0]:\n         return None\n     distractor_count = random.randint(DISTRACTOR_RANGE[0], max_distractors)\n-    distractor_counts = random.sample(remaining_counts, distractor_count)\n \n+    src_cols = random.sample(usable, k)\n+    tgt_cols = random.sample(usable, k)\n+\n+    counts = random.sample(SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES, k + distractor_count)\n+    real_counts = counts[:k]\n+    distractor_counts = counts[k:]\n+\n     color_to_tgt = dict(zip(src_cols, tgt_cols))\n     masks = {src: _sprite_mask(n, area) for src, area in zip(src_cols, real_counts)}\n \n@@ -521,6 +518,8 @@\n \n     try:\n         info = _analyze_scene(grid)\n+        if info[\"legend_count_total\"] != k + distractor_count:\n+            return None\n         if len(info[\"matched_counts\"]) != k:\n             return None\n         if len(info[\"distractor_counts\"]) != distractor_count:\n\n  ✓ Design fused count-legend-with-distractors rules and shared scene analysis\n  ✓ Implement new combo solver/generator in ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/9/code.py\n  ✓ Run reliability and behavior-validation scripts, then refine if needed\ndiff --git a/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/9/code.py b/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/9/code.py\nindex 5118d5b845ab2464b87c40373164ab3076d9256f..fe289f311fa3d2eb7cae6b98357ee4db4ce110f3\n--- a/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/9/code.py\n+++ b/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/9/code.py\n@@ -2,107 +2,122 @@\n # combo_spec: D7/2+D13/0\n # Name: 数量编码图例+干扰条目\n \n+import importlib.util\n import itertools\n+from pathlib import Path\n import random\n+import sys\n \n import numpy as np\n \n-from arc_utils import bbox_coords, components_mask, get_bg, paste, random_free_location\n+ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[4]\n+if str(ROOT) not in sys.path:\n+    sys.path.append(str(ROOT))\n \n+try:\n+    from arc_utils import bbox_coords, components_mask, get_bg, paste, random_free_location\n+except ModuleNotFoundError:\n+    _spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\"_combo_arc_utils\", ROOT / \"solvers\" / \"arc_utils.py\")\n+    _mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(_spec)\n+    assert _spec.loader is not None\n+    _spec.loader.exec_module(_mod)\n+    bbox_coords = _mod.bbox_coords\n+    components_mask = _mod.components_mask\n+    get_bg = _mod.get_bg\n+    paste = _mod.paste\n+    random_free_location = _mod.random_free_location\n \n # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n-# Design analysis for the fused D7/2 + D13/0 variant\n+# Design analysis for the combo variant\n #\n # a) Concrete behavior and trace:\n-#    - Keep the original large gray frame with solid-color placeholder blocks inside.\n-#    - Keep one outside sprite template per placeholder color; each sprite still uses the\n-#      placeholder color and has the same N x N bbox as the matching blocks inside the frame.\n-#    - Replace the old overlapping two-color legend with a top-left strip of monochrome\n-#      count codes. Each code is a compact 3x3 nested stencil whose area is the key and\n-#      whose color is the recolor target.\n-#    - Add 1-2 extra legend entries whose counts do not match any real sprite. Those entries\n-#      are visible in the same strip, so solver must count every sprite, compare that count\n-#      against all legend entries, and ignore the unmatched ones.\n-#    - Example: suppose a cyan external sprite occupies exactly 5 cells in a 4x4 bbox, while\n-#      the legend strip contains orange-5, red-7, yellow-3, and teal-8 entries. Cyan blocks\n-#      inside the frame become the 5-cell sprite recolored to orange. The 7/3/8 entries stay\n-#      unused if no sprite has those counts. In the original task, recoloring came from a\n-#      direct shape-color legend pair; here it comes from sprite area, and some legend items\n-#      are decoys.\n+#    - Keep the original backbone: one gray rectangular frame, solid placeholder blocks\n+#      inside the frame, and one source-colored sprite template outside the frame for each\n+#      placeholder color.\n+#    - Replace the original overlapping two-color legend with a fixed top-left legend strip.\n+#      Each legend entry is now a compact monochrome stencil whose area encodes a number.\n+#      The legend color is the output color, while the number of colored pixels is the key.\n+#    - Add mandatory distractor legend entries. These extra count codes are rendered exactly\n+#      like the real legend entries but their pixel counts do not match any real sprite area.\n+#    - Example: suppose blue placeholders correspond to a 4x4 outside sprite with exactly\n+#      5 colored cells, and green placeholders correspond to a 4x4 sprite with 3 cells.\n+#      The legend may show orange=5 cells, red=3 cells, and yellow=6 cells. The solver must\n+#      count the blue sprite, match 5 to orange, count the green sprite, match 3 to red,\n+#      and ignore the yellow 6-cell legend item. In the original task, recoloring came from\n+#      direct shape-color legend pairs; in this fusion, recoloring requires count matching\n+#      plus filtering unmatched legend counts.\n #\n # b) Complexity calibration:\n-#    - Real sprite counts are unique and chosen from a small visual vocabulary 2..8. This\n-#      keeps counting tractable while still giving enough room for distractors.\n-#    - There are 2-5 placeholder colors, so each sample has repeated evidence inside the frame\n-#      but not so many codes that the top legend becomes unreadable.\n-#    - Distractors are mandatory but capped at 1-2, which makes the extra filtering visible\n-#      without drowning out the true legend entries.\n+#    - Restrict real sprite areas to a small vocabulary {2,3,4,5,6,7}. This makes counting\n+#      observable, while still leaving room for 1-2 unmatched legend counts in the same band.\n+#    - Limit the number of placeholder colors to 2-4. That preserves repeated evidence inside\n+#      the frame and avoids exhausting the count vocabulary once distractors are added.\n+#    - Keep sprite boxes at 3x3 or 4x4. Larger boxes would make exact counting slower and add\n+#      clutter; smaller boxes would not support enough distinct counted patterns.\n #\n-# c) Implicit assumption audit against the original solver:\n-#    - Old legend parsing assumed overlapping two-color glyphs and source-color inference from\n-#      pair structure. That breaks completely; fused solver instead reads monochrome entries\n-#      anchored on the top row and uses component area as the code.\n-#    - Old sprite extraction only had to exclude legend components paired by overlap. That is\n-#      no longer valid because legend entries now have a single color and may share colors with\n-#      real sprites. The generator therefore reserves the whole top band for legends, and the\n-#      solver excludes all top-band components from sprite recovery.\n-#    - Count-based recoloring only works if different placeholder colors do not share the same\n-#      sprite area. The generator guarantees unique real counts, and solver asserts that.\n-#    - Distractors are only safe if their counts are distinct from all real counts. The\n-#      generator enforces that; solver checks that legend counts form a strict superset of\n-#      sprite counts rather than an arbitrary unrelated set.\n+# c) Implicit-assumption audit against the original solver:\n+#    - Original legend parsing assumed small overlapping two-color regions; that is no longer\n+#      true. The new solver instead assumes every outside component touching row 0 is part of\n+#      the top legend strip.\n+#    - Original source->target mapping was indexed by placeholder color. That assumption is\n+#      broken by D7/2: color now only selects which sprite to stamp, while legend lookup is\n+#      keyed by sprite area.\n+#    - Original code expected every parsed legend item to be relevant. D13/0 breaks that too:\n+#      the new solver must recover all real sprite areas first, then use only legend counts\n+#      that match those areas.\n+#    - Sparse counted sprites may be 4-disconnected, so extraction cannot rely on one single\n+#      connected component spanning the full bbox. The solver unions all non-legend components\n+#      of the same source color and checks the union bbox against the placeholder size.\n #\n # d) Placement legality:\n-#    - The top band is reserved before frame placement, so no sprite or frame cell can touch\n-#      the legend strip.\n-#    - Frame, external sprites, and legend entries are all placed with a one-cell padding gap\n-#      via `random_free_location`, preventing overlap or accidental touching.\n-#    - Sprite masks always include opposite corners of the N x N bbox, so the union bbox seen\n-#      by the solver exactly matches the placeholder block size even when the sprite is sparse\n-#      or disconnected.\n+#    - The generator reserves a top band for legends, preventing sprite/frame collisions with\n+#      legend entries and guaranteeing that row-0 colored components are legends only.\n+#    - `random_free_location` with one-cell padding separates the frame, legend strip, and\n+#      all outside sprites, so no objects touch or overlap.\n+#    - Sprite masks always include opposite corners of their NxN box, ensuring that the union\n+#      bbox exactly matches the placeholder block size even when the mask is disconnected.\n #\n # e) Visual observability:\n-#    - A human can recover the rule by counting cells in an outside sprite, then scanning the\n-#      top strip for the legend entry with the same count to get the output color.\n-#    - The extra legend items are not hidden metadata; they are visible unmatched counts in the\n-#      same legend family, so the added reasoning load is observable from the grids alone.\n+#    - A human can inspect the outside sprite for one placeholder color, count its colored\n+#      cells, and then look for the same count in the top-left legend to infer the recolor.\n+#    - The distractor dimension is visible because the legend contains more count entries than\n+#      there are actual sprite areas. These extras cannot be dismissed by shape alone; they\n+#      must be excluded by exact counting.\n #\n # f) Visual cleanliness:\n-#    - Legends live in one dedicated band, the frame occupies one compact rectangle elsewhere,\n-#      and sprites are separate free patches. This keeps object categories spatially separated.\n-#    - All legend entries share one simple 3x3 encoding template, reducing clutter compared with\n-#      arbitrary glyphs or mixed overlay patterns.\n+#    - All legend entries share one strip at the top. All sprites live below that strip.\n+#      The frame is placed away from both via the reserve mask, so the scene stays segmented.\n+#    - Each legend entry is monochrome and compact, with a single background gap between\n+#      entries. This keeps the distractors legible without introducing another border motif.\n #\n # g) Change inferability:\n-#    - Output colors are structurally indicated by the legend-entry colors, not by raw palette\n-#      ids. Because counts repeat via multiple placeholders of the same color, a few samples are\n-#      enough to show that equal source colors do not determine output colors on their own.\n-#    - Distractors do not affect placed objects, so the solver must infer that only counts seen\n-#      on real sprites are actionable.\n+#    - Output colors remain directly visible in the legend, but only after inferring which\n+#      count entries are live. Because placeholder colors repeat and each source color has\n+#      one repeated sprite template, 2-4 samples are enough to see that count equality, not\n+#      shape identity or legend order, drives the recoloring.\n #\n # h) Generator validation target:\n-#    - Every generated sample must contain at least one unused legend count.\n-#    - Every real sprite count must appear exactly once in the legend strip.\n-#    - `main(input)` must match the generator's output-frame oracle.\n+#    - Every generated sample must contain at least one unmatched legend count.\n+#    - Every real sprite area must appear exactly once in the legend.\n+#    - `main(input)` must equal the oracle output frame.\n #\n-# i) New solver assumptions that the generator explicitly guarantees:\n-#    - Every legend component touches row 0 because the strip is pasted at the top-left corner.\n-#    - No non-legend object touches row 0 because the entire top band is reserved.\n-#    - Each placeholder color has exactly one external sprite union with bbox equal to the\n-#      placeholder size.\n-#    - Sprite counts are pairwise distinct, and legend counts are pairwise distinct.\n+# i) New solver assumptions that the generator guarantees:\n+#    - Only legend entries occupy row 0 outside the frame.\n+#    - Real sprite areas are pairwise distinct.\n+#    - Distractor legend counts are distinct from all real sprite areas.\n+#    - For each placeholder color, the union of its non-legend outside components has the\n+#      same bbox as that color's placeholder blocks.\n # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n \n \n FRAME_COL = 5\n-SPRITE_N_RANGE = (3, 6)\n+SPRITE_N_RANGE = (3, 5)             # N in {3, 4}\n GRID_ROWS_RANGE = (2, 4)\n GRID_COLS_RANGE = (3, 5)\n TOTAL_BLOCKS_RANGE = (6, 10)\n MAX_EMPTY_SLOTS = 2\n-NUM_COLORS_RANGE = (2, 5)\n-SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES = (2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8)\n-DISTRACTOR_RANGE = (1, 2)\n+NUM_COLORS_RANGE = (2, 4)\n+SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES = (2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7)\n MIN_FRAME_H = 13\n MIN_FRAME_W = 18\n MAX_FRAME_DIM = 21\n@@ -110,22 +125,16 @@\n CANVAS_H_RANGE = (22, 31)\n CANVAS_W_RANGE = (23, 31)\n PATCH_PADDING = 1\n-GEN_RETRIES = 500\n+GEN_RETRIES = 400\n+DISTRACTOR_RANGE = (1, 2)\n \n-LEGEND_H = 3\n-LEGEND_ENTRY_W = 3\n+LEGEND_H = 2\n+LEGEND_ENTRY_W = 4\n LEGEND_GAP = 1\n TOP_BAND_H = LEGEND_H + 1\n LEGEND_ORDER = (\n-    (0, 0),\n-    (0, 1),\n-    (0, 2),\n-    (1, 0),\n-    (1, 1),\n-    (1, 2),\n-    (2, 0),\n-    (2, 1),\n-    (2, 2),\n+    (0, 0), (0, 1), (0, 2), (0, 3),\n+    (1, 0), (1, 1), (1, 2), (1, 3),\n )\n \n \n@@ -161,45 +170,6 @@\n \n def _bbox_hw(bbox: tuple[int, int, int, int]) -> tuple[int, int]:\n     return bbox[2] - bbox[0] + 1, bbox[3] - bbox[1] + 1\n-\n-\n-def _legend_entries(comps: list[dict]) -> list[tuple[int, int, int, int]]:\n-    \"\"\"Return legend entries as (x_pos, out_color, pixel_count, comp_id), sorted by x.\"\"\"\n-    entries = [\n-        (int(comp[\"bbox\"][1]), int(comp[\"col\"]), int(comp[\"area\"]), int(comp[\"id\"]))\n-        for comp in comps\n-        if comp[\"bbox\"][0] == 0 and comp[\"bbox\"][2] < LEGEND_H\n-    ]\n-    entries.sort(key=lambda item: item[0])\n-    return entries\n-\n-\n-def _extract_sprite_data(\n-    comps: list[dict],\n-    placeholder_colors: set[int],\n-    phw: dict[int, tuple[int, int]],\n-    legend_ids: set[int],\n-) -> dict[int, tuple[tuple[tuple[int, int], ...], int, int, int]]:\n-    sprite_data: dict[int, tuple[tuple[tuple[int, int], ...], int, int, int]] = {}\n-    for src_col in sorted(placeholder_colors):\n-        all_candidates = [c for c in comps if c[\"col\"] == src_col and c[\"id\"] not in legend_ids]\n-        assert all_candidates, f\"no sprite found for placeholder color {src_col}\"\n-\n-        pts_set = set()\n-        r0 = min(c[\"bbox\"][0] for c in all_candidates)\n-        c0 = min(c[\"bbox\"][1] for c in all_candidates)\n-        r1 = max(c[\"bbox\"][2] for c in all_candidates)\n-        c1 = max(c[\"bbox\"][3] for c in all_candidates)\n-        for comp in all_candidates:\n-            pts_set.update(comp[\"pts\"])\n-\n-        want_h, want_w = phw[src_col]\n-        assert (r1 - r0 + 1, c1 - c0 + 1) == (want_h, want_w), (\n-            f\"sprite union bbox does not match placeholder size for color {src_col}\"\n-        )\n-        coords = tuple(sorted((r - r0, c - c0) for r, c in pts_set))\n-        sprite_data[src_col] = (coords, want_h, want_w, len(coords))\n-    return sprite_data\n \n \n def _analyze_scene(grid: np.ndarray) -> dict:\n@@ -220,7 +190,7 @@\n     for col in sorted(placeholder_colors):\n         for pts in components_mask((crop == col) & inner_mask, connectivity=4):\n             r0, c0, r1, c1 = bbox_coords(pts)\n-            placeholders.append((col, (r0, c0, r1, c1)))\n+            placeholders.append((int(col), (r0, c0, r1, c1)))\n \n     phw: dict[int, tuple[int, int]] = {}\n     for col in placeholder_colors:\n@@ -228,7 +198,7 @@\n         assert dims, f\"no placeholder component found for color {col}\"\n         unique_dims = sorted(set(dims))\n         assert len(unique_dims) == 1, f\"ambiguous placeholder sizes for color {col}: {unique_dims}\"\n-        phw[col] = unique_dims[0]\n+        phw[int(col)] = unique_dims[0]\n \n     outside = np.ones(g.shape, dtype=bool)\n     outside[fr0 : fr1 + 1, fc0 : fc1 + 1] = False\n@@ -251,28 +221,58 @@\n             )\n             cid += 1\n \n-    legend = _legend_entries(comps)\n-    assert legend, \"count legend must occupy the top row\"\n-    legend_ids = {entry[3] for entry in legend}\n+    legend_entries = [\n+        {\n+            \"x\": int(comp[\"bbox\"][1]),\n+            \"color\": int(comp[\"col\"]),\n+            \"count\": int(comp[\"area\"]),\n+            \"id\": int(comp[\"id\"]),\n+        }\n+        for comp in comps\n+        if comp[\"bbox\"][0] == 0\n+    ]\n+    legend_entries.sort(key=lambda entry: entry[\"x\"])\n+    assert legend_entries, \"count legend must occupy the top row\"\n+\n+    legend_ids = {entry[\"id\"] for entry in legend_entries}\n+    count_to_color: dict[int, int] = {}\n+    for entry in legend_entries:\n+        count = entry[\"count\"]\n+        assert count not in count_to_color, f\"duplicate legend count {count}\"\n+        count_to_color[count] = int(entry[\"color\"])\n+\n+    sprite_data: dict[int, tuple[tuple[tuple[int, int], ...], int, int, int]] = {}\n+    for src_col in sorted(placeholder_colors):\n+        all_candidates = [c for c in comps if c[\"col\"] == src_col and c[\"id\"] not in legend_ids]\n+        assert all_candidates, f\"no sprite found for placeholder color {src_col}\"\n+\n+        r0 = min(c[\"bbox\"][0] for c in all_candidates)\n+        c0 = min(c[\"bbox\"][1] for c in all_candidates)\n+        r1 = max(c[\"bbox\"][2] for c in all_candidates)\n+        c1 = max(c[\"bbox\"][3] for c in all_candidates)\n+        pts_set = set()\n+        for comp in all_candidates:\n+            pts_set.update(comp[\"pts\"])\n+\n+        want_h, want_w = phw[int(src_col)]\n+        assert (r1 - r0 + 1, c1 - c0 + 1) == (want_h, want_w), (\n+            f\"sprite union bbox does not match placeholder size for color {src_col}\"\n+        )\n+        coords = tuple(sorted((r - r0, c - c0) for r, c in pts_set))\n+        area = len(coords)\n+        sprite_data[int(src_col)] = (coords, want_h, want_w, area)\n \n-    count_to_tgt: dict[int, int] = {}\n-    for _x, out_col, pixel_count, _cid in legend:\n-        assert pixel_count not in count_to_tgt, f\"duplicate legend count {pixel_count}\"\n-        count_to_tgt[pixel_count] = int(out_col)\n+    sprite_areas = [area for _coords, _sh, _sw, area in sprite_data.values()]\n+    assert len(set(sprite_areas)) == len(sprite_areas), f\"sprite areas must be unique, got {sprite_areas}\"\n \n-    sprite_data = _extract_sprite_data(comps, placeholder_colors, phw, legend_ids)\n-    sprite_counts = [area for _coords, _sh, _sw, area in sprite_data.values()]\n-    assert len(set(sprite_counts)) == len(sprite_counts), \"sprite counts must be unique in this variant\"\n-    sprite_count_set = set(sprite_counts)\n-    legend_count_set = set(count_to_tgt)\n-    assert sprite_count_set.issubset(legend_count_set), (\n-        f\"legend counts {sorted(legend_count_set)} do not cover sprite areas {sorted(sprite_count_set)}\"\n-    )\n+    color_map: dict[int, int] = {}\n+    for src_col, (_coords, _sh, _sw, area) in sprite_data.items():\n+        assert area in count_to_color, f\"no legend count matches sprite area {area}\"\n+        color_map[int(src_col)] = int(count_to_color[area])\n \n-    color_map = {src_col: int(count_to_tgt[area]) for src_col, (_coords, _sh, _sw, area) in sprite_data.items()}\n-    distractor_counts = sorted(legend_count_set - sprite_count_set)\n-    matched_counts = sorted(sprite_count_set)\n-    assert distractor_counts, \"legend must include at least one unused count\"\n+    matched_counts = {area for area in sprite_areas}\n+    distractor_counts = {entry[\"count\"] for entry in legend_entries if entry[\"count\"] not in matched_counts}\n+    assert distractor_counts, \"legend must contain at least one unmatched count\"\n \n     return {\n         \"bg\": bg,\n@@ -282,34 +282,29 @@\n         \"phw\": phw,\n         \"sprite_data\": sprite_data,\n         \"color_map\": color_map,\n-        \"legend_count_set\": legend_count_set,\n+        \"legend_entries\": legend_entries,\n         \"matched_counts\": matched_counts,\n         \"distractor_counts\": distractor_counts,\n+        \"legend_count_total\": len(legend_entries),\n     }\n \n \n def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n     \"\"\"\n-    Replace framed placeholders with outside sprites and recolor them through a count-coded legend strip.\n+    Fill the framed placeholders with external sprites, then recolor them using a counted legend with decoys.\n \n     Input structure:\n-    - A gray rectangular frame encloses a grid of solid-color placeholder blocks on a background field.\n-    - Outside the frame there is one source-colored sprite template for each placeholder color.\n-    - Along the top-left edge there is a legend strip of small monochrome count codes, and some of those\n-      legend entries are distractors whose counts do not match any real sprite.\n+    - A gray rectangular frame contains solid-color placeholder blocks on background cells.\n+    - Outside the frame there is one sprite template for each placeholder color, rendered in that same source color.\n+    - The top-left of the whole grid contains a legend strip of compact single-color entries whose pixel counts encode keys; some legend entries are extra and match no sprite.\n \n     Rule:\n-    - Recover each sprite by taking all non-legend outside components of the same color and matching their\n-      union bbox to the placeholder size.\n-    - Count the colored cells in that recovered sprite and use that count, not the sprite silhouette, as the\n-      lookup key into the top legend strip.\n-    - Ignore legend entries whose counts are never realized by any recovered sprite.\n-    - Stamp every recovered sprite into each matching placeholder slot and recolor it with the color of the\n-      legend entry that has the same pixel count.\n+    - Recover each source-colored sprite outside the frame and count how many colored cells it contains.\n+    - Read every top-row legend component as a candidate mapping from pixel count to output color.\n+    - Keep only the legend counts that actually occur among the recovered sprites, ignoring unmatched legend entries.\n+    - Replace every placeholder block with its sprite shape and recolor it to the output color associated with that sprite's pixel count.\n \n-    Key insight: The legend no longer tells you which shape to use; the outside sprite color still selects\n-    the shape, but the final recolor comes only from matching sprite area to a count legend that includes\n-    extra decoy counts.\n+    Key insight: The legend no longer names shapes or source colors. The only reliable key is the sprite's colored-cell count, and the extra legend counts must be filtered out by comparing them against the real sprites.\n     \"\"\"\n     info = _analyze_scene(grid)\n     crop = info[\"crop\"]\n@@ -337,7 +332,7 @@\n \n \n def _legend_patch(entries: list[tuple[int, int]], bg: int) -> np.ndarray:\n-    \"\"\"Build the top-left legend strip from (pixel_count, target_color) pairs.\"\"\"\n+    \"\"\"Build the top-left count legend from (pixel_count, target_color) pairs.\"\"\"\n     width = len(entries) * LEGEND_ENTRY_W + max(0, len(entries) - 1) * LEGEND_GAP\n     patch = np.full((LEGEND_H, width), bg, dtype=int)\n     for idx, (pixel_count, color) in enumerate(entries):\n@@ -349,7 +344,7 @@\n \n def _sprite_mask(n: int, area: int) -> np.ndarray:\n     \"\"\"Generate an NxN sparse mask with exact area and full NxN union bbox.\"\"\"\n-    assert 2 <= area <= min(len(LEGEND_ORDER) - 1, n * n - 1), f\"unsupported area {area} for n={n}\"\n+    assert 2 <= area <= min(len(LEGEND_ORDER), n * n), f\"unsupported area {area} for n={n}\"\n     mask = np.zeros((n, n), dtype=bool)\n \n     corner_pairs = [\n@@ -440,16 +435,18 @@\n     usable = [c for c in range(10) if c not in (bg, FRAME_COL)]\n \n     k = random.randint(*NUM_COLORS_RANGE)\n-    src_cols = random.sample(usable, k)\n-    tgt_cols = random.sample(usable, k)\n-    real_counts = random.sample(SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES, k)\n-    remaining_counts = [count for count in SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES if count not in real_counts]\n-    max_distractors = min(DISTRACTOR_RANGE[1], len(remaining_counts))\n+    max_distractors = min(DISTRACTOR_RANGE[1], len(SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES) - k)\n     if max_distractors < DISTRACTOR_RANGE[0]:\n         return None\n     distractor_count = random.randint(DISTRACTOR_RANGE[0], max_distractors)\n-    distractor_counts = random.sample(remaining_counts, distractor_count)\n \n+    src_cols = random.sample(usable, k)\n+    tgt_cols = random.sample(usable, k)\n+\n+    counts = random.sample(SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES, k + distractor_count)\n+    real_counts = counts[:k]\n+    distractor_counts = counts[k:]\n+\n     color_to_tgt = dict(zip(src_cols, tgt_cols))\n     masks = {src: _sprite_mask(n, area) for src, area in zip(src_cols, real_counts)}\n \n@@ -521,6 +518,8 @@\n \n     try:\n         info = _analyze_scene(grid)\n+        if info[\"legend_count_total\"] != k + distractor_count:\n+            return None\n         if len(info[\"matched_counts\"]) != k:\n             return None\n         if len(info[\"distractor_counts\"]) != distractor_count:\n\ncodex\n已完成，代码已写入 [code.py](/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/9/code.py:1)。\n\n这版把两个维度真正融合在一起了：\n- 在 [_analyze_scene()](/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/9/code.py:175) 里先恢复框外精灵、统计每个精灵的像素数，再读取顶端数量图例，并只保留那些“计数值确实被某个真实精灵使用”的图例项。\n- 在 [main()](/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/9/code.py:292) 里，放置逻辑仍然按占位颜色选精灵，但重着色已经改成“按精灵像素数量查图例”，并显式忽略干扰条目。\n- 在 [_gen_attempt()](/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/9/code.py:428) 里，生成器固定加入 1-2 个未被任何精灵使用的额外计数图例项，同时保留顶端图例带和外部精灵的清晰分区。文件顶部也加入了按要求的设计分析注释和四段式 `main()` 文档字符串。\n\n验证结果：\n- 指定 50 次可靠性测试通过：`Success: 50/50, Time: 0.8s (15ms/call)`\n- 融合行为量化指标采用 `extra_entries = legend_count_total - len(matched_counts)`，它衡量“图例里有多少额外计数项未被真实精灵使用”。\n- 100 样本统计结果：\n  - `extra_entries_distribution = {1: 50, 2: 50}`\n  - `legend_total_distribution = {3: 18, 4: 33, 5: 32, 6: 17}`\n  - `matched_real_count_distribution = {2: 35, 3: 32, 4: 33}`\n  - `distractor_count_values = {2: 21, 3: 26, 4: 28, 5: 24, 6: 27, 7: 24}`\n\n这说明干扰条目不是偶发的，而是每个样本都存在，并且计数编码本身也在实际起作用。\ndiff --git a/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/9/code.py b/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/9/code.py\nindex 5118d5b845ab2464b87c40373164ab3076d9256f..fe289f311fa3d2eb7cae6b98357ee4db4ce110f3\n--- a/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/9/code.py\n+++ b/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/9/code.py\n@@ -2,107 +2,122 @@\n # combo_spec: D7/2+D13/0\n # Name: 数量编码图例+干扰条目\n \n+import importlib.util\n import itertools\n+from pathlib import Path\n import random\n+import sys\n \n import numpy as np\n \n-from arc_utils import bbox_coords, components_mask, get_bg, paste, random_free_location\n+ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[4]\n+if str(ROOT) not in sys.path:\n+    sys.path.append(str(ROOT))\n \n+try:\n+    from arc_utils import bbox_coords, components_mask, get_bg, paste, random_free_location\n+except ModuleNotFoundError:\n+    _spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\"_combo_arc_utils\", ROOT / \"solvers\" / \"arc_utils.py\")\n+    _mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(_spec)\n+    assert _spec.loader is not None\n+    _spec.loader.exec_module(_mod)\n+    bbox_coords = _mod.bbox_coords\n+    components_mask = _mod.components_mask\n+    get_bg = _mod.get_bg\n+    paste = _mod.paste\n+    random_free_location = _mod.random_free_location\n \n # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n-# Design analysis for the fused D7/2 + D13/0 variant\n+# Design analysis for the combo variant\n #\n # a) Concrete behavior and trace:\n-#    - Keep the original large gray frame with solid-color placeholder blocks inside.\n-#    - Keep one outside sprite template per placeholder color; each sprite still uses the\n-#      placeholder color and has the same N x N bbox as the matching blocks inside the frame.\n-#    - Replace the old overlapping two-color legend with a top-left strip of monochrome\n-#      count codes. Each code is a compact 3x3 nested stencil whose area is the key and\n-#      whose color is the recolor target.\n-#    - Add 1-2 extra legend entries whose counts do not match any real sprite. Those entries\n-#      are visible in the same strip, so solver must count every sprite, compare that count\n-#      against all legend entries, and ignore the unmatched ones.\n-#    - Example: suppose a cyan external sprite occupies exactly 5 cells in a 4x4 bbox, while\n-#      the legend strip contains orange-5, red-7, yellow-3, and teal-8 entries. Cyan blocks\n-#      inside the frame become the 5-cell sprite recolored to orange. The 7/3/8 entries stay\n-#      unused if no sprite has those counts. In the original task, recoloring came from a\n-#      direct shape-color legend pair; here it comes from sprite area, and some legend items\n-#      are decoys.\n+#    - Keep the original backbone: one gray rectangular frame, solid placeholder blocks\n+#      inside the frame, and one source-colored sprite template outside the frame for each\n+#      placeholder color.\n+#    - Replace the original overlapping two-color legend with a fixed top-left legend strip.\n+#      Each legend entry is now a compact monochrome stencil whose area encodes a number.\n+#      The legend color is the output color, while the number of colored pixels is the key.\n+#    - Add mandatory distractor legend entries. These extra count codes are rendered exactly\n+#      like the real legend entries but their pixel counts do not match any real sprite area.\n+#    - Example: suppose blue placeholders correspond to a 4x4 outside sprite with exactly\n+#      5 colored cells, and green placeholders correspond to a 4x4 sprite with 3 cells.\n+#      The legend may show orange=5 cells, red=3 cells, and yellow=6 cells. The solver must\n+#      count the blue sprite, match 5 to orange, count the green sprite, match 3 to red,\n+#      and ignore the yellow 6-cell legend item. In the original task, recoloring came from\n+#      direct shape-color legend pairs; in this fusion, recoloring requires count matching\n+#      plus filtering unmatched legend counts.\n #\n # b) Complexity calibration:\n-#    - Real sprite counts are unique and chosen from a small visual vocabulary 2..8. This\n-#      keeps counting tractable while still giving enough room for distractors.\n-#    - There are 2-5 placeholder colors, so each sample has repeated evidence inside the frame\n-#      but not so many codes that the top legend becomes unreadable.\n-#    - Distractors are mandatory but capped at 1-2, which makes the extra filtering visible\n-#      without drowning out the true legend entries.\n+#    - Restrict real sprite areas to a small vocabulary {2,3,4,5,6,7}. This makes counting\n+#      observable, while still leaving room for 1-2 unmatched legend counts in the same band.\n+#    - Limit the number of placeholder colors to 2-4. That preserves repeated evidence inside\n+#      the frame and avoids exhausting the count vocabulary once distractors are added.\n+#    - Keep sprite boxes at 3x3 or 4x4. Larger boxes would make exact counting slower and add\n+#      clutter; smaller boxes would not support enough distinct counted patterns.\n #\n-# c) Implicit assumption audit against the original solver:\n-#    - Old legend parsing assumed overlapping two-color glyphs and source-color inference from\n-#      pair structure. That breaks completely; fused solver instead reads monochrome entries\n-#      anchored on the top row and uses component area as the code.\n-#    - Old sprite extraction only had to exclude legend components paired by overlap. That is\n-#      no longer valid because legend entries now have a single color and may share colors with\n-#      real sprites. The generator therefore reserves the whole top band for legends, and the\n-#      solver excludes all top-band components from sprite recovery.\n-#    - Count-based recoloring only works if different placeholder colors do not share the same\n-#      sprite area. The generator guarantees unique real counts, and solver asserts that.\n-#    - Distractors are only safe if their counts are distinct from all real counts. The\n-#      generator enforces that; solver checks that legend counts form a strict superset of\n-#      sprite counts rather than an arbitrary unrelated set.\n+# c) Implicit-assumption audit against the original solver:\n+#    - Original legend parsing assumed small overlapping two-color regions; that is no longer\n+#      true. The new solver instead assumes every outside component touching row 0 is part of\n+#      the top legend strip.\n+#    - Original source->target mapping was indexed by placeholder color. That assumption is\n+#      broken by D7/2: color now only selects which sprite to stamp, while legend lookup is\n+#      keyed by sprite area.\n+#    - Original code expected every parsed legend item to be relevant. D13/0 breaks that too:\n+#      the new solver must recover all real sprite areas first, then use only legend counts\n+#      that match those areas.\n+#    - Sparse counted sprites may be 4-disconnected, so extraction cannot rely on one single\n+#      connected component spanning the full bbox. The solver unions all non-legend components\n+#      of the same source color and checks the union bbox against the placeholder size.\n #\n # d) Placement legality:\n-#    - The top band is reserved before frame placement, so no sprite or frame cell can touch\n-#      the legend strip.\n-#    - Frame, external sprites, and legend entries are all placed with a one-cell padding gap\n-#      via `random_free_location`, preventing overlap or accidental touching.\n-#    - Sprite masks always include opposite corners of the N x N bbox, so the union bbox seen\n-#      by the solver exactly matches the placeholder block size even when the sprite is sparse\n-#      or disconnected.\n+#    - The generator reserves a top band for legends, preventing sprite/frame collisions with\n+#      legend entries and guaranteeing that row-0 colored components are legends only.\n+#    - `random_free_location` with one-cell padding separates the frame, legend strip, and\n+#      all outside sprites, so no objects touch or overlap.\n+#    - Sprite masks always include opposite corners of their NxN box, ensuring that the union\n+#      bbox exactly matches the placeholder block size even when the mask is disconnected.\n #\n # e) Visual observability:\n-#    - A human can recover the rule by counting cells in an outside sprite, then scanning the\n-#      top strip for the legend entry with the same count to get the output color.\n-#    - The extra legend items are not hidden metadata; they are visible unmatched counts in the\n-#      same legend family, so the added reasoning load is observable from the grids alone.\n+#    - A human can inspect the outside sprite for one placeholder color, count its colored\n+#      cells, and then look for the same count in the top-left legend to infer the recolor.\n+#    - The distractor dimension is visible because the legend contains more count entries than\n+#      there are actual sprite areas. These extras cannot be dismissed by shape alone; they\n+#      must be excluded by exact counting.\n #\n # f) Visual cleanliness:\n-#    - Legends live in one dedicated band, the frame occupies one compact rectangle elsewhere,\n-#      and sprites are separate free patches. This keeps object categories spatially separated.\n-#    - All legend entries share one simple 3x3 encoding template, reducing clutter compared with\n-#      arbitrary glyphs or mixed overlay patterns.\n+#    - All legend entries share one strip at the top. All sprites live below that strip.\n+#      The frame is placed away from both via the reserve mask, so the scene stays segmented.\n+#    - Each legend entry is monochrome and compact, with a single background gap between\n+#      entries. This keeps the distractors legible without introducing another border motif.\n #\n # g) Change inferability:\n-#    - Output colors are structurally indicated by the legend-entry colors, not by raw palette\n-#      ids. Because counts repeat via multiple placeholders of the same color, a few samples are\n-#      enough to show that equal source colors do not determine output colors on their own.\n-#    - Distractors do not affect placed objects, so the solver must infer that only counts seen\n-#      on real sprites are actionable.\n+#    - Output colors remain directly visible in the legend, but only after inferring which\n+#      count entries are live. Because placeholder colors repeat and each source color has\n+#      one repeated sprite template, 2-4 samples are enough to see that count equality, not\n+#      shape identity or legend order, drives the recoloring.\n #\n # h) Generator validation target:\n-#    - Every generated sample must contain at least one unused legend count.\n-#    - Every real sprite count must appear exactly once in the legend strip.\n-#    - `main(input)` must match the generator's output-frame oracle.\n+#    - Every generated sample must contain at least one unmatched legend count.\n+#    - Every real sprite area must appear exactly once in the legend.\n+#    - `main(input)` must equal the oracle output frame.\n #\n-# i) New solver assumptions that the generator explicitly guarantees:\n-#    - Every legend component touches row 0 because the strip is pasted at the top-left corner.\n-#    - No non-legend object touches row 0 because the entire top band is reserved.\n-#    - Each placeholder color has exactly one external sprite union with bbox equal to the\n-#      placeholder size.\n-#    - Sprite counts are pairwise distinct, and legend counts are pairwise distinct.\n+# i) New solver assumptions that the generator guarantees:\n+#    - Only legend entries occupy row 0 outside the frame.\n+#    - Real sprite areas are pairwise distinct.\n+#    - Distractor legend counts are distinct from all real sprite areas.\n+#    - For each placeholder color, the union of its non-legend outside components has the\n+#      same bbox as that color's placeholder blocks.\n # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n \n \n FRAME_COL = 5\n-SPRITE_N_RANGE = (3, 6)\n+SPRITE_N_RANGE = (3, 5)             # N in {3, 4}\n GRID_ROWS_RANGE = (2, 4)\n GRID_COLS_RANGE = (3, 5)\n TOTAL_BLOCKS_RANGE = (6, 10)\n MAX_EMPTY_SLOTS = 2\n-NUM_COLORS_RANGE = (2, 5)\n-SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES = (2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8)\n-DISTRACTOR_RANGE = (1, 2)\n+NUM_COLORS_RANGE = (2, 4)\n+SPRITE_AREA_CHOICES = (2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7)\n MIN_FRAME_H = 13\n MIN_FRAME_W = 18\n MAX_FRAME_DIM = 21\n@@ -110,22 +125,16 @@\n CANVAS_H_RANGE = (22, 31)\n CANVAS_W_RANGE = (23, 31)\n PATCH_PADDING = 1\n-GEN_RETRIES = 500\n+GEN_RETRIES = 400\n+DISTRACTOR_RANGE = (1, 2)\n \n-LEGEND_H = 3\n-LEGEND_ENTRY_W = 3\n+LEGEND_H = 2\n+LEGEND_ENTRY_W = 4\n LEGEND_GAP = 1\n TOP_BAND_H = LEGEND_H + 1\n LEGEND_ORDER = (\n-    (0, 0),\n-    (0, 1),\n-    (0, 2),\n-    (1, 0),\n-    (1, 1),\n-    (1, 2),\n-    (2, 0),\n-    (2, 1),\n-    (2, 2),\n+    (0, 0), (0, 1), (0, 2), (0, 3),\n+    (1, 0), (1, 1), (1, 2), (1, 3),\n )\n \n \n@@ -161,45 +170,6 @@\n \n def _bbox_hw(bbox: tuple[int, int, int, int]) -> tuple[int, int]:\n     return bbox[2] - bbox[0] + 1, bbox[3] - bbox[1] + 1\n-\n-\n-def _legend_entries(comps: list[dict]) -> list[tuple[int, int, int, int]]:\n-    \"\"\"Return legend entries as (x_pos, out_color, pixel_count, comp_id), sorted by x.\"\"\"\n-    entries = [\n-        (int(comp[\"bbox\"][1]), int(comp[\"col\"]), int(comp[\"area\"]), int(comp[\"id\"]))\n-        for comp in comps\n-        if comp[\"bbox\"][0] == 0 and comp[\"bbox\"][2] < LEGEND_H\n-    ]\n-    entries.sort(key=lambda item: item[0])\n-    return entries\n-\n-\n-def _extract_sprite_data(\n-    comps: list[dict],\n-    placeholder_colors: set[int],\n-    phw: dict[int, tuple[int, int]],\n-    legend_ids: set[int],\n-) -> dict[int, tuple[tuple[tuple[int, int], ...], int, int, int]]:\n-    sprite_data: dict[int, tuple[tuple[tuple[int, int], ...], int, int, int]] = {}\n-    for src_col in sorted(placeholder_colors):\n-        all_candidates = [c for c in comps if c[\"col\"] == src_col and c[\"id\"] not in legend_ids]\n-        assert all_candidates, f\"no sprite found for placeholder color {src_col}\"\n-\n-        pts_set = set()\n-        r0 = min(c[\"bbox\"][0] for c in all_candidates)\n-        c0 = min(c[\"bbox\"][1] for c in all_candidates)\n-        r1 = max(c[\"bbox\"][2] for c in all_candidates)\n-        c1 = max(c[\"bbox\"][3] for c in all_candidates)\n-        for comp in all_candidates:\n-            pts_set.update(comp[\"pts\"])\n-\n-        want_h, want_w = phw[src_col]\n-        assert (r1 - r0 + 1, c1 - c0 + 1) == (want_h, want_w), (\n-            f\"sprite union bbox does not match placeholder size for color {src_col}\"\n-        )\n-        coords = tuple(sorted((r - r0, c - c0) for r, c in pts_set))\n-        sprite_data[src_col] = (coords, want_h, want_w, len(coords))\n-    return sprite_data\n \n \n def _analyze_scene(grid: np.ndarray) -> dict:\n@@ -220,7 +190,7 @@\n     for col in sorted(placeholder_colors):\n         for pts in components_mask((crop == col) & inner_mask, connectivity=4):\n             r0, c0, r1, c1 = bbox_coords(pts)\n-            placeholders.append((col, (r0, c0, r1, c1)))\n+            placeholders.append((int(col), (r0, c0, r1, c1)))\n \n     phw: dict[int, tuple[int, int]] = {}\n     for col in placeholder_colors:\n@@ -228,7 +198,7 @@\n         assert dims, f\"no placeholder component found for color {col}\"\n         unique_dims = sorted(set(dims))\n         assert len(unique_dims) == 1, f\"ambiguous placeholder sizes for color {col}: {unique_dims}\"\n-        phw[col] = unique_dims[0]\n+        phw[int(col)] = unique_dims[0]\n \n     outside = np.ones(g.shape, dtype=bool)\n     outside[fr0 : fr1 + 1, fc0 : fc1 + 1] = False\n@@ -251,28 +221,58 @@\n             )\n             cid += 1\n \n-    legend = _legend_entries(comps)\n-    assert legend, \"count legend must occupy the top row\"\n-    legend_ids = {entry[3] for entry in legend}\n+    legend_entries = [\n+        {\n+            \"x\": int(comp[\"bbox\"][1]),\n+            \"color\": int(comp[\"col\"]),\n+            \"count\": int(comp[\"area\"]),\n+            \"id\": int(comp[\"id\"]),\n+        }\n+        for comp in comps\n+        if comp[\"bbox\"][0] == 0\n+    ]\n+    legend_entries.sort(key=lambda entry: entry[\"x\"])\n+    assert legend_entries, \"count legend must occupy the top row\"\n+\n+    legend_ids = {entry[\"id\"] for entry in legend_entries}\n+    count_to_color: dict[int, int] = {}\n+    for entry in legend_entries:\n+        count = entry[\"count\"]\n+        assert count not in count_to_color, f\"duplicate legend count {count}\"\n+        count_to_color[count] = int(entry[\"color\"])\n+\n+    sprite_data: dict[int, tuple[tuple[tuple[int, int], ...], int, int, int]] = {}\n+    for src_col in sorted(placeholder_colors):\n+        all_candidates = [c for c in comps if c[\"col\"] == src_col and c[\"id\"] not in legend_ids]\n+        assert all_candidates, f\"no sprite found for placeholder color {src_col}\"\n+\n+        r0 = min(c[\"bbox\"][0] for c in all_candidates)\n+        c0 = min(c[\"bbox\"][1] for c in all_candidates)\n+        r1 = max(c[\"bbox\"][2] for c in all_candidates)\n+        c1 = max(c[\"bbox\"][3] for c in all_candidates)\n+        pts_set = set()\n+        for comp in all_candidates:\n+            pts_set.update(comp[\"pts\"])\n+\n+        want_h, want_w = phw[int(src_col)]\n+        assert (r1 - r0 + 1, c1 - c0 + 1) == (want_h, want_w), (\n+            f\"sprite union bbox does not match placeholder size for color {src_col}\"\n+        )\n+        coords = tuple(sorted((r - r0, c - c0) for r, c in pts_set))\n+        area = len(coords)\n+        sprite_data[int(src_col)] = (coords, want_h, want_w, area)\n \n-    count_to_tgt: dict[int, int] = {}\n-    for _x, out_col, pixel_count, _cid in legend:\n-        assert pixel_count not in count_to_tgt, f\"duplicate legend count {pixel_count}\"\n-        count_to_tgt[pixel_count] = int(out_col)\n+    sprite_areas = [area for _coords, _sh, _sw, area in sprite_data.values()]\n+    assert len(set(sprite_areas)) == len(sprite_areas), f\"sprite areas must be unique, got {sprite_areas}\"\n \n-    sprite_data = _extract_sprite_data(comps, placeholder_colors, phw, legend_ids)\n-    sprite_counts = [area for _coords, _sh, _sw, area in sprite_data.values()]\n-    assert len(set(sprite_counts)) == len(sprite_counts), \"sprite counts must be unique in this variant\"\n-    sprite_count_set = set(sprite_counts)\n-    legend_count_set = set(count_to_tgt)\n-    assert sprite_count_set.issubset(legend_count_set), (\n-        f\"legend counts {sorted(legend_count_set)} do not cover sprite areas {sorted(sprite_count_set)}\"\n-    )\n+    color_map: dict[int, int] = {}\n+    for src_col, (_coords, _sh, _sw, area) in sprite_data.items():\n+        assert area in count_to_color, f\"no legend count matches sprite area {area}\"\n+        color_map[int(src_col)] = int(count_to_color[area])\n \n-    color_map = {src_col: int(count_to_tgt[area]) for src_col, (_coords, _sh, _sw, area) in sprite_data.items()}\n-    distractor_counts = sorted(legend_count_set - sprite_count_set)\n-    matched_counts = sorted(sprite_count_set)\n-    assert distractor_counts, \"legend must include at least one unused count\"\n+    matched_counts = {area for area in sprite_areas}\n+    distractor_counts = {entry[\"count\"] for entry in legend_entries if entry[\"count\"] not in matched_counts}\n+    assert distractor_counts, \"legend must contain at least one unmatched count\"\n \n     return {\n         \"bg\": bg,\n@@ -282,34 +282,29 @@\n         \"phw\": phw,\n         \"sprite_data\": sprite_data,\n         \"color_map\": color_map,\n-        \"legend_count_set\": legend_count_set,\n+        \"legend_entries\": legend_entries,\n         \"matched_counts\": matched_counts,\n         \"distractor_counts\": distractor_counts,\n+        \"legend_count_total\": len(legend_entries),\n     }\n \n \n def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n     \"\"\"\n-    Replace framed placeholders with outside sprites and recolor them through a count-coded legend strip.\n+    Fill the framed placeholders with external sprites, then recolor them using a counted legend with decoys.\n \n     Input structure:\n-    - A gray rectangular frame encloses a grid of solid-color placeholder blocks on a background field.\n-    - Outside the frame there is one source-colored sprite template for each placeholder color.\n-    - Along the top-left edge there is a legend strip of small monochrome count codes, and some of those\n-      legend entries are distractors whose counts do not match any real sprite.\n+    - A gray rectangular frame contains solid-color placeholder blocks on background cells.\n+    - Outside the frame there is one sprite template for each placeholder color, rendered in that same source color.\n+    - The top-left of the whole grid contains a legend strip of compact single-color entries whose pixel counts encode keys; some legend entries are extra and match no sprite.\n \n     Rule:\n-    - Recover each sprite by taking all non-legend outside components of the same color and matching their\n-      union bbox to the placeholder size.\n-    - Count the colored cells in that recovered sprite and use that count, not the sprite silhouette, as the\n-      lookup key into the top legend strip.\n-    - Ignore legend entries whose counts are never realized by any