/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tem/codex_supervisor_logs/20260515_0848_edb79dae.log:210:{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_87","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'prompt=$(cat /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/tem3/combo_prompt_edb79dae_15.txt)\ncd /home/lixinyu/snap/new\ncodex exec --skip-git-repo-check -c model='\"'\\\"gpt-5.4\\\"' -c reasoning.effort='\\\"high\\\"' \\\"\"'$prompt\"'","aggregated_output":"Reading additional input from stdin...\nOpenAI Codex v0.130.0\n--------\nworkdir: /home/lixinyu/snap/new\nmodel: gpt-5.4\nprovider: openai\napproval: never\nsandbox: workspace-write [workdir, /tmp, /home/lixinyu/.codex/memories]\nreasoning effort: high\nreasoning summaries: none\nsession id: 019e2bb9-1093-7963-9aa6-8ce0aaac0a71\n--------\nuser\n    你要修改一个 ARC-AGI-2 任务的 solver 和 generator，实现一个**多维度融合变体**。\n\n    ## 原始任务: edb79dae\n    **摘要**: 将灰色框架外的彩色精灵按颜色匹配到框架内的同色像素位置，替换为精灵形状，最后根据左上角形状-颜色图例对所有放置的精灵进行重着色\n\n    ## 要实现的融合组合\n    - **组合名称**: 位置编码图例+图例右下角\n    - **combo_spec**: D2/3+D7/0\n\n    ### 融合描述（实现规格）\n\n    图例中的形状按空间排列，精灵根据在框架内的相对位置（所在象限或行列区域）查找对应图例条目。 图例从左上角移至右下角。 融合效果：位置编码图例中精灵的\"相对位置\"参考框架，而图例自身的位置也从左上变为右下。 解题者需要先在非惯常位置找到图例，再理解图例内部的空间排列与框架内位置的映射关系。 图例位置的改变可能影响位置编码的解读方向——例如图例在右下时，其内部从左到右的排列可能对应 框架从右到左的区域。两层空间推理相互关联。\n\n    ### 各组成项的原始变体详情\n\n    以下是 combo_spec 中每个组成项在维度分析 YAML 中的原始描述，帮助你理解每项改动的来源和细节：\n\n    - **D2/3** — 第二步匹配条件：形状-颜色图例查找 (`match_cond`)\n  - 当前值: 放置后的精灵形状与左上角图例中的形状模式匹配（s2.shape == d2.shape），确定重着色的目标颜色\n  - 改为: 位置编码图例 — 图例中的形状按特定空间排列（如从左到右、从上到下），精灵根据其在框架内的相对位置（如所在象限或行列区域）查找对应图例条目。匹配从形状属性变为空间属性。\n  - 来源: creative（参考任务: None）\n- **D7/0** — 符号编码：图例的结构与位置 (`symbol_instructions`)\n  - 当前值: 左上角图例由多个条目组成，每个条目展示一个形状模式及其对应的输出颜色，形成形状到颜色的查找表\n  - 改为: 图例位于右下角 — 取反图例位置：图例从左上角移至右下角。解题者需在非惯常位置发现图例，改变视觉搜索策略。其他逻辑不变。\n  - 来源: inversion（参考任务: None）\n\n    ## 原始 solver + generator 代码\n\n    文件: `/home/lixinyu/snap/new/arc2_solver_select/edb79dae.py`\n\n    ```python\n    import numpy as np\n\nfrom arc_utils import bbox_coords, components_mask, get_bg, paste, random_free_location\nimport random\nimport itertools\n\n\ndef _find_frame(g: np.ndarray, bg: int) -> tuple[int, tuple[int, int, int, int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Find a rectangular border component:\n      - all bbox-border cells are this color,\n      - bbox-interior is not entirely this color.\n    Return (frame_color, (r0,c0,r1,c1)).\n    \"\"\"\n    candidates = []\n    colors = [int(c) for c in np.unique(g) if int(c) != bg]\n    for col in colors:\n        for pts in components_mask(g == col, connectivity=4):\n            r0, c0, r1, c1 = bbox_coords(pts)\n            if r1 - r0 < 2 or c1 - c0 < 2:\n                continue\n            sub = g[r0 : r1 + 1, c0 : c1 + 1]\n            border = np.zeros(sub.shape, dtype=bool)\n            border[0, :] = True\n            border[-1, :] = True\n            border[:, 0] = True\n            border[:, -1] = True\n            if not np.all(sub[border] == col):\n                continue\n            if np.all(sub[~border] == col):\n                continue\n            candidates.append((col, (r0, c0, r1, c1)))\n    assert len(candidates) == 1, f\"expected exactly one rectangular frame component, found {len(candidates)}\"\n    frame_col, bbox = candidates[0]\n    return int(frame_col), bbox\n\n\ndef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"\n    Stamp recolored sprites into a framed region using placeholder positions and a color legend.\n\n    Input structure:\n    - bg background, a rectangular single-color frame, colored placeholder cells inside the frame.\n    - Outside the frame: sprite shapes (one per placeholder color) and a small legend mapping each placeholder color to an output color.\n\n    Rule:\n    - Find the frame and its interior placeholders.\n    - For each placeholder color, locate the matching-color sprite outside the frame.\n    - Stamp each sprite at the placeholder's position inside the frame.\n    - Recolor every stamped sprite to the output color defined by the legend.\n\n    Key insight: The legend pairs (overlapping two-color glyphs outside the frame) dictate the final recoloring — placeholder color selects the shape, legend maps it to the output color.\n    \"\"\"\n    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\n    bg = get_bg(g)\n\n    frame_col, (fr0, fc0, fr1, fc1) = _find_frame(g, bg)\n\n    crop = g[fr0 : fr1 + 1, fc0 : fc1 + 1]\n    H, W = crop.shape\n    assert H >= 3 and W >= 3, f\"frame too small for interior: {(H, W)}\"\n\n    # Placeholder components inside the frame interior.\n    inner_mask = np.zeros((H, W), dtype=bool)\n    inner_mask[1:-1, 1:-1] = True\n    placeholder_colors = set(map(int, np.unique(crop[inner_mask]))) - {bg, frame_col}\n    assert placeholder_colors, \"no placeholder colors found inside frame\"\n\n    placeholders: list[tuple[int, tuple[int, int, int, int]]] = []\n    for col in sorted(placeholder_colors):\n        for pts in components_mask((crop == col) & inner_mask, connectivity=4):\n            r0, c0, r1, c1 = bbox_coords(pts)\n            placeholders.append((col, (r0, c0, r1, c1)))\n    # Eval inputs use one placement bbox size per placeholder color.\n    phw: dict[int, tuple[int, int]] = {}\n    for col in placeholder_colors:\n        dims = [(b[2] - b[0] + 1, b[3] - b[1] + 1) for c, b in placeholders if c == col]\n        assert dims, f\"no placeholder component found for color {col}\"\n        unique_dims = sorted(set(dims))\n        assert len(unique_dims) == 1, f\"ambiguous placeholder sizes for color {col}: {unique_dims}\"\n        phw[col] = unique_dims[0]\n\n    # Extract outside-frame components for sprite shapes and for legend color mapping.\n    outside = np.ones(g.shape, dtype=bool)\n    outside[fr0 : fr1 + 1, fc0 : fc1 + 1] = False\n\n    # Collect all outside components (with ids) for later pairing.\n    comps = []\n    colors = [int(c) for c in np.unique(g) if int(c) not in (bg, frame_col)]\n    cid = 0\n    for col in colors:\n        for pts in components_mask((g == col) & outside, connectivity=4):\n            r0, c0, r1, c1 = bbox_coords(pts)\n            pts_tuples = [(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in pts]\n            comps.append(\n                {\n                    \"id\": cid,\n                    \"col\": int(col),\n                    \"pts\": pts_tuples,\n                    \"bbox\": (r0, c0, r1, c1),\n                    \"area\": len(pts_tuples),\n                }\n            )\n            cid += 1\n\n    def _bbox_overlap(a: tuple[int, int, int, int], b: tuple[int, int, int, int]) -> bool:\n        ar0, ac0, ar1, ac1 = a\n        br0, bc0, br1, bc1 = b\n        return not (ar1 < br0 or br1 < ar0 or ac1 < bc0 or bc1 < ac0)\n\n    # Legend mapping: detect small two-color glyph regions where two components overlap in bbox\n    # and the union bbox contains only those two colors (no background).\n    color_map: dict[int, int] = {}\n    legend_ids: set[int] = set()\n\n    for i in range(len(comps)):\n        for j in range(i + 1, len(comps)):\n            ci = comps[i]\n            cj = comps[j]\n            if ci[\"col\"] == cj[\"col\"]:\n                continue\n            if not _bbox_overlap(ci[\"bbox\"], cj[\"bbox\"]):\n                continue\n            r0 = min(ci[\"bbox\"][0], cj[\"bbox\"][0])\n            c0 = min(ci[\"bbox\"][1], cj[\"bbox\"][1])\n            r1 = max(ci[\"bbox\"][2], cj[\"bbox\"][2])\n            c1 = max(ci[\"bbox\"][3], cj[\"bbox\"][3])\n            # restrict to compact legend-like regions\n            if (r1 - r0 + 1) > 8 or (c1 - c0 + 1) > 8:\n                continue\n            sub = g[r0 : r1 + 1, c0 : c1 + 1]\n            sub_colors = set(map(int, np.unique(sub))) - {frame_col}\n            if bg in sub_colors:\n                continue\n            if len(sub_colors) != 2:\n                continue\n            cset = set(sub_colors)\n            if ci[\"col\"] not in cset or cj[\"col\"] not in cset:\n                continue\n\n            # Decide source->target.\n            # If exactly one color is used as a placeholder inside the frame, that one is source.\n            if (ci[\"col\"] in placeholder_colors) ^ (cj[\"col\"] in placeholder_colors):\n                src = ci[\"col\"] if ci[\"col\"] in placeholder_colors else cj[\"col\"]\n                tgt = cj[\"col\"] if src == ci[\"col\"] else ci[\"col\"]\n            else:\n                # Otherwise: the larger component in this pair is treated as the source.\n                assert ci[\"area\"] != cj[\"area\"], f\"ambiguous equal-area legend pair: {ci['col']} and {cj['col']}\"\n                if ci[\"area\"] > cj[\"area\"]:\n                    src, tgt = ci[\"col\"], cj[\"col\"]\n                else:\n                    src, tgt = cj[\"col\"], ci[\"col\"]\n\n            assert src in placeholder_colors, f\"legend source color {src} is not a placeholder\"\n            assert src not in color_map, f\"duplicate legend mapping for placeholder color {src}\"\n            color_map[src] = int(tgt)\n            legend_ids.add(ci[\"id\"])\n            legend_ids.add(cj[\"id\"])\n    assert set(color_map) == placeholder_colors, (\n        f\"legend mappings {sorted(color_map)} do not match placeholders {sorted(placeholder_colors)}\"\n    )\n\n    # Sprite shapes: for each placeholder color, pick the non-legend component matching placeholder size.\n    sprite_coords: dict[int, tuple[tuple[tuple[int, int], ...], int, int]] = {}\n    for src_col in sorted(placeholder_colors):\n        all_candidates = [c for c in comps if c[\"col\"] == src_col and c[\"id\"] not in legend_ids]\n        assert all_candidates, f\"no non-legend sprite found for color {src_col}\"\n        want_h, want_w = phw[src_col]\n        sized = [\n            c\n            for c in all_candidates\n            if (c[\"bbox\"][2] - c[\"bbox\"][0] + 1) == want_h and (c[\"bbox\"][3] - c[\"bbox\"][1] + 1) == want_w\n        ]\n        assert len(sized) == 1, f\"expected one size-matched sprite for color {src_col}, found {len(sized)}\"\n        base = sized[0]\n        sr0, sc0, sr1, sc1 = base[\"bbox\"]\n\n        # Some sprites can be split into multiple 4-connected components of the same color.\n        # Merge any additional (non-legend) components fully contained in the chosen sprite bbox.\n        pts_set = set(base[\"pts\"])\n        for c in all_candidates:\n            if c[\"id\"] == base[\"id\"]:\n                continue\n            r0, c0, r1, c1 = c[\"bbox\"]\n            assert sr0 <= r0 and sr1 >= r1 and sc0 <= c0 and sc1 >= c1, (\n                f\"extra sprite component for color {src_col} is outside the base bbox\"\n            )\n            pts_set.update(c[\"pts\"])\n\n        coords = tuple(sorted((r - sr0, c - sc0) for r, c in pts_set))\n        sprite_coords[src_col] = (coords, sr1 - sr0 + 1, sc1 - sc0 + 1)\n\n    # Build output crop: keep frame border, clear interior to bg, then paste recolored sprites.\n    out = crop.copy()\n    out[1:-1, 1:-1] = bg\n\n    for src_col, (pr0, pc0, pr1, pc1) in placeholders:\n        assert src_col in sprite_coords and src_col in color_map, f\"placeholder color {src_col} missing sprite or color mapping\"\n        tgt_col = int(color_map[src_col])\n        coords, sh, sw = sprite_coords[src_col]\n        assert (pr1 - pr0 + 1, pc1 - pc0 + 1) == (sh, sw), (\n            f\"placeholder size does not match sprite for color {src_col}\"\n        )\n        assert pr0 + sh <= H and pc0 + sw <= W, f\"sprite for color {src_col} does not fit at placeholder\"\n        # Align sprite's bbox top-left to placeholder bbox top-left.\n        off_r = pr0\n        off_c = pc0\n        for dr, dc in coords:\n            rr, cc = off_r + dr, off_c + dc\n            out[rr, cc] = tgt_col\n\n    return out\n\n# --------------- generator (o5x) ---------------\n\n# === CFG: tunables ===\nFRAME_COL = 5                       # frame border color (always gray)\nSPRITE_N_RANGE = (3, 6)             # NxN sprite/placeholder size, exclusive upper\nGRID_ROWS_RANGE = (2, 4)            # placeholder grid row count, exclusive upper\nGRID_COLS_RANGE = (3, 5)            # placeholder grid col count, exclusive upper\nTOTAL_BLOCKS_RANGE = (6, 10)        # total filled slots (inclusive)\nMAX_EMPTY_SLOTS = 2                 # max empty slots in the grid\nNUM_COLORS_RANGE = (2, 5)           # K = number of distinct placeholder colors (inclusive)\nSPRITE_FILL_MIN = 0.5               # min sprite fill ratio\nSPRITE_FILL_MAX = 0.9               # max sprite fill ratio (clamped to n*n-1)\nMIN_FRAME_H = 13                    # minimum frame height\nMIN_FRAME_W = 18                    # minimum frame width\nMAX_FRAME_DIM = 21                  # maximum frame height or width\nFRAME_MARGIN_SLACK = 4              # max extra padding inside frame beyond content\nCANVAS_H_RANGE = (22, 31)           # final grid height range, exclusive upper\nCANVAS_W_RANGE = (23, 31)           # final grid width range, exclusive upper\nFRAME_POS_JITTER_PROB = 0.25        # probability of non-edge frame placement per axis\nPATCH_PADDING = 1                   # min bg gap between placed patches\nGEN_RETRIES = 300                   # outer retry budget\n\n\ndef _legend(src: int, tgt: int) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Build a 3x4 legend block mapping src color to tgt color.\"\"\"\n    return np.array(\n        [[src, src, tgt, tgt],\n         [src, src, src, tgt],\n         [src, src, tgt, tgt]], dtype=int)\n\n\ndef _sprite_mask(n: int) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Generate a random NxN binary mask with fill ratio in [SPRITE_FILL_MIN, SPRITE_FILL_MAX].\"\"\"\n    lo = max((n * n + 1) // 2, int(np.ceil(SPRITE_FILL_MIN * n * n)))\n    hi = min(int(np.floor(SPRITE_FILL_MAX * n * n)), n * n - 1)\n    target = random.randint(lo, hi)\n\n    # Seed: random walk column + one full row, then random orientation\n    mask = np.zeros((n, n), dtype=bool)\n    c = random.randrange(n)\n    for r in range(n):\n        c = max(0, min(n - 1, c + random.choice([-1, 0, 1])))\n        mask[r, c] = True\n    mask[random.randrange(n), :] = True\n\n    if random.random() < 0.5:\n        mask = mask.T.copy()\n    if random.random() < 0.5:\n        mask = np.flipud(mask)\n    if random.random() < 0.5:\n        mask = np.fliplr(mask)\n\n    # Grow to target fill by adding random frontier cells\n    while int(mask.sum()) < target:\n        dilated = np.zeros_like(mask)\n        dilated[1:, :] |= mask[:-1, :]\n        dilated[:-1, :] |= mask[1:, :]\n        dilated[:, 1:] |= mask[:, :-1]\n        dilated[:, :-1] |= mask[:, 1:]\n        frontier = list(zip(*np.where(dilated & ~mask)))\n        r, c = random.choice(frontier)\n        mask[r, c] = True\n    return mask\n\n\ndef _colored_sprite(mask: np.ndarray, color: int, bg: int) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Render a binary mask as a colored sprite on bg.\"\"\"\n    out = np.full(mask.shape, bg, dtype=int)\n    out[mask] = int(color)\n    return out\n\n\ndef _content_extent(n: int, grid_rows: int, grid_cols: int) -> tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"Content area needed for grid_rows x grid_cols of NxN blocks with 1-cell gaps.\"\"\"\n    return (grid_rows * n + grid_rows - 1, grid_cols * n + grid_cols - 1)\n\n\ndef _choose_structure() -> tuple[int, int, int, int, int] | None:\n    \"\"\"Pick (n, rows, cols, empty_count, total) satisfying frame size constraints.\"\"\"\n    total = random.randint(*TOTAL_BLOCKS_RANGE)\n    options = []\n    for n in range(*SPRITE_N_RANGE):\n        for rows in range(*GRID_ROWS_RANGE):\n            for cols in range(*GRID_COLS_RANGE):\n                ch, cw = _content_extent(n, rows, cols)\n                base_fh = ch + 4  # +2 border +2 min margin\n                base_fw = cw + 4\n                slots = rows * cols\n                empty = slots - total\n                if base_fh <= MAX_FRAME_DIM and base_fw <= MAX_FRAME_DIM and 0 <= empty <= MAX_EMPTY_SLOTS:\n                    options.append((n, rows, cols, empty, total))\n    return random.choice(options) if options else None\n\n\ndef _choose_empty_slots(\n    rows: int, cols: int, empty_count: int\n) -> tuple[set[tuple[int, int]], list[tuple[int, int]]]:\n    \"\"\"Choose which grid slots are empty, ensuring every row and column has at least one filled slot.\n\n    Returns (empty_slots, shuffled filled_slots).\n    \"\"\"\n    slots = [(r, c) for r in range(rows) for c in range(cols)]\n    valid = []\n    for combo in itertools.combinations(slots, empty_count):\n        empty = set(combo)\n        filled = [s for s in slots if s not in empty]\n        if len({r for r, _ in filled}) == rows and len({c for _, c in filled}) == cols:\n            valid.append(empty)\n    empty_slots = random.choice(valid)\n    filled_slots = [s for s in slots if s not in empty_slots]\n    random.shuffle(filled_slots)\n    return empty_slots, filled_slots\n\n\ndef _make_bordered_frame(h: int, w: int, bg: int) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Create an h x w frame filled with bg and a 1-cell FRAME_COL border.\"\"\"\n    frame = np.full((h, w), bg, dtype=int)\n    frame[0, :] = frame[-1, :] = FRAME_COL\n    frame[:, 0] = frame[:, -1] = FRAME_COL\n    return frame\n\n\ndef _place_patch(\n    grid: np.ndarray, reserve: np.ndarray, patch: np.ndarray, bg: int,\n    *, transparent: bool,\n) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Find a free location for patch and paste it onto grid/reserve. Returns success.\"\"\"\n    blocker = np.full(patch.shape, FRAME_COL, dtype=int)\n    try:\n        r, c = random_free_location(reserve, blocker, transparent=bg, padding=PATCH_PADDING)\n    except ValueError:\n        return False\n    paste(reserve, blocker, r, c)\n    paste(grid, patch, r, c, transparent=bg if transparent else None)\n    return True\n\n\ndef _gen_attempt() -> np.ndarray | None:\n    # --- structure ---\n    struct = _choose_structure()\n    if struct is None:\n        return None\n    n, rows, cols, empty_count, _ = struct\n\n    bg = random.choice([c for c in range(10) if c != FRAME_COL])\n    usable = [c for c in range(10) if c not in (bg, FRAME_COL)]\n\n    # --- colors ---\n    k = random.randint(*NUM_COLORS_RANGE)\n    src_cols = random.sample(usable, k)\n    tgt_cols = [random.choice([c for c in usable if c != src]) for src in src_cols]\n    color_to_tgt = dict(zip(src_cols, tgt_cols))\n    masks = {src: _sprite_mask(n) for src in src_cols}\n\n    # --- frame dimensions & margins ---\n    ch, cw = _content_extent(n, rows, cols)\n    min_fh = max(MIN_FRAME_H, ch + 4)\n    min_fw = max(MIN_FRAME_W, cw + 4)\n    frame_h = random.randint(min_fh, min(MAX_FRAME_DIM, max(min_fh, ch + 2 + FRAME_MARGIN_SLACK)))\n    frame_w = random.randint(min_fw, min(MAX_FRAME_DIM, max(min_fw, cw + 2 + FRAME_MARGIN_SLACK)))\n    y_margin = frame_h - 2 - ch\n    x_margin = frame_w - 2 - cw\n    top_margin = random.randint(1, y_margin - 1)\n    left_margin = random.randint(1, x_margin - 1)\n\n    # --- slot assignment ---\n    _, filled_slots = _choose_empty_slots(rows, cols, empty_count)\n    cell_colors = {}\n    for slot, col in zip(filled_slots[:k], src_cols):\n        cell_colors[slot] = col\n    for slot in filled_slots[k:]:\n        cell_colors[slot] = random.choice(src_cols)\n\n    # --- build input & output frames ---\n    input_frame = _make_bordered_frame(frame_h, frame_w, bg)\n    output_frame = _make_bordered_frame(frame_h, frame_w, bg)\n    for (rr, cc), src in cell_colors.items():\n        r0 = 1 + top_margin + rr * (n + 1)\n        c0 = 1 + left_margin + cc * (n + 1)\n        paste(input_frame, np.full((n, n), src, dtype=int), r0, c0)\n        paste(output_frame, _colored_sprite(masks[src], color_to_tgt[src], bg), r0, c0, transparent=bg)\n\n    # --- canvas selection & frame placement ---\n    ext_area = k * (12 + n * n + 10)\n    possible_dims = [\n        (h, w)\n        for h in range(*CANVAS_H_RANGE)\n        for w in range(*CANVAS_W_RANGE)\n        if h >= frame_h and w >= frame_w and h * w - frame_h * frame_w >= ext_area\n    ]\n    if not possible_dims:\n        return None\n    h, w = random.choice(possible_dims)\n    grid = np.full((h, w), bg, dtype=int)\n    reserve = np.full((h, w), bg, dtype=int)\n\n    fr0 = random.choice([0, h - frame_h])\n    fc0 = random.choice([0, w - frame_w])\n    if h - frame_h > 2 and random.random() < FRAME_POS_JITTER_PROB:\n        fr0 = random.randrange(0, h - frame_h + 1)\n    if w - frame_w > 2 and random.random() < FRAME_POS_JITTER_PROB:\n        fc0 = random.randrange(0, w - frame_w + 1)\n    paste(grid, input_frame, fr0, fc0)\n    paste(reserve, np.full((frame_h, frame_w), FRAME_COL, dtype=int), fr0, fc0)\n\n    # --- place external patches (sprites + legends) ---\n    patches: list[tuple[np.ndarray, bool]] = []\n    for src, tgt in zip(src_cols, tgt_cols):\n        patches.append((_colored_sprite(masks[src], src, bg), True))\n        patches.append((_legend(src, tgt), False))\n    random.shuffle(patches)\n    patches.sort(key=lambda item: item[0].size, reverse=True)\n    for patch, transparent in patches:\n        if not _place_patch(grid, reserve, patch, bg, transparent=transparent):\n            return None\n\n    # --- oracle check ---\n    try:\n        if not np.array_equal(main(grid), output_frame):\n            return None\n    except Exception:\n        return None\n    return grid\n\n\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n    for _ in range(GEN_RETRIES):\n        out = _gen_attempt()\n        if out is not None:\n            return out\n    raise RuntimeError(\"failed to generate valid edb79dae input\")\n\n    ```\n\n    ## 原始任务规格（Spec）\n\n    以下是从原始 solver 代码和示例中提炼的完整任务规格，包含精确的数值约束和生成策略。\n    Spec 本身就是原题代码生成时的参考文件，因此：\n    - 在**设计分析**阶段，参考 spec 理解原始任务的完整设计细节（对象结构、空间关系、生成策略等），以此为基础思考融合变体的改动如何落实\n    - 在**实现**阶段，参考 spec 中的数值约束（网格尺寸、对象数量/尺寸、颜色数等），确保融合变体在物理上可实现\n\n    ```yaml\n    spec:\n  grid: 22-30 rows x 23-30 cols\n  bg: any color; frame_col: always 5 [observed]\n  frame:\n    single-color rectangular border (1-cell thick), interior filled with bg + solid placeholder blocks\n    size: 13-21 rows x 18-21 cols\n  placeholders:\n    solid NxN blocks (N=3-5) arranged in a regular grid inside frame with 1-cell bg gaps\n    grid: 2-3 rows x 3-4 cols; 0-2 cells may be empty\n    total count: 6-10 blocks using 2-5 distinct placeholder colors\n    each color appears 1+ times; all instances same NxN size\n  sprites:\n    one per placeholder color, placed outside frame, same NxN bbox as placeholders\n    fill ratio: 0.50-0.90; may be 4-disconnected within bbox\n    each sprite uses only its placeholder color + bg\n  legends:\n    one per placeholder color, fixed 3x4 pattern outside frame, no bg in the 3x4 block\n    pattern: |\n      src src tgt tgt\n      src src src tgt\n      src src tgt tgt\n    src = placeholder color (area 7), tgt = output color (area 5)\n    src determined by: if exactly one color is a placeholder, that is src; else larger-area component is src\n    tgt colors may overlap with placeholder colors or be entirely new\n  output:\n    the frame region only; interior has placeholders replaced by sprites recolored to legend-mapped tgt color\n    frame border preserved; interior bg cells stay bg\n\ngeneration_strategy:\n  approach: output-first\n  steps:\n    1. Choose bg, frame_col (5), N (3-5), grid dims R x C (2-3 x 3-4), 0-2 empty cells\n    2. Choose K = number of placeholder colors (2-5), assign distinct placeholder colors and tgt colors\n    3. Generate K random NxN sprites (fill 50-90%, connected or not, at least 1 bg cell)\n    4. Build output frame interior: place sprites (recolored to tgt) on the RxC grid with 1-bg-gap, empty cells stay bg\n    5. Build input frame interior: replace each sprite region with a solid NxN block of its placeholder color\n    6. Place frame border around the interior\n    7. Place K legend blocks (3x4 fixed pattern) outside frame with bg gaps\n    8. Place K sprite templates (original placeholder-colored NxN) outside frame, separated by bg from legends/frame\n    9. Pad to final grid size with bg; ensure all outside elements fit without overlap\n    ```\n\n额外要求：原始代码的 `main()` 已包含四段式说明注释/文档字符串（开头概述 + `Input structure:` + `Rule:` + `Key insight:`）。\n生成的新代码里也必须在 `main()` 上方保留这一结构，并根据**融合后的新规则**与**原注释提供的信息**重新编写；可以借鉴原注释的组织方式，但**不要照抄原文**，要让内容准确反映融合后的输入结构、规则和关键洞察。\n\n\n## 已有单变体参考代码\n\n以下组成项已有单变体实现，可作为融合时的参考：\n\n            ### 参考代码: D2/3\n\n            文件: `/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D2/3/code.py`\n\n            ```python\n            # Variant of edb79dae\n# Dimension: D2 — 第二步匹配条件：形状-颜色图例查找 (match_cond)\n# Change: 放置后的精灵形状与左上角图例中的形状模式匹配（s2.shape == d2.shape），确定重着色的目标颜色... → 位置编码图例\n\nimport itertools\nimport random\n\nimport numpy as np\n\nfrom arc_utils import bbox_coords, components_mask, get_bg, paste, random_free_location\n\n\n# Design analysis for the D2 variant\n# ----------------------------------\n# source_task: none\n# original_task:\n#   - A gray rectangular frame contains solid NxN placeholder blocks.\n#   - Outside the frame there is one sprite template per placeholder color.\n#   - A separate legend chooses the final recolor for each placed sprite.\n# variant_core:\n#   - Keep step 1 unchanged: placeholder color still selects which external sprite shape\n#     gets stamped into the matching block inside the frame.\n#   - Replace step 2 completely: the recolor is no longer tied to source color or shape.\n#     Instead, a fixed 2x2 legend panel sits in the top-left corner of the whole canvas.\n#     Its four entries encode colors for the four relative regions of the frame interior:\n#     top-left, top-right, bottom-left, bottom-right.\n# concrete_behavior:\n#   - The legend is a 5x5 panel:\n#       aa.bb\n#       aa.bb\n#       .....\n#       cc.dd\n#       cc.dd\n#     where \".\" means background. The four 2x2 colored squares are the four target colors.\n#   - The placeholder grid inside the frame still has 2-3 rows and 3-4 columns with 0-2\n#     empty cells. The solver reconstructs row/column ranks from placeholder bbox positions.\n#   - A placeholder belongs to the upper half if its row-rank is in the first half of the\n#     occupied rows, and to the left half if its column-rank is in the first half of the\n#     occupied columns. These two bits pick one legend entry.\n# behavior_trace:\n#   - Old recolor logic at one placement: \"this sprite came from placeholder color 3, so find\n#     the legend entry associated with color 3, then repaint it to that target color.\"\n#   - New recolor logic at the same placement: \"this sprite is being stamped into the frame's\n#     upper-right region, so use the upper-right legend square's color, regardless of which\n#     placeholder color supplied the shape.\"\n#   - Visible consequence: the same source color can appear in multiple regions and will then\n#     produce different output colors in different places.\n# complexity_calibration:\n#   - Use exactly four legend entries so the position rule is visible but not overparameterized.\n#   - Generator guarantees every quadrant has at least one filled placeholder, so each legend\n#     color is exercised in each sample.\n#   - Generator also forces at least one placeholder color to appear in two different quadrants,\n#     preventing accidental collapse back to a per-color recolor rule.\n# implicit_assumption_audit:\n#   - Original `color_map[src_col] -> tgt_col` assumed a unique legend mapping per source color.\n#     That assumption is removed; recolor now depends on placeholder position, so the solver must\n#     compute a target for each placement instance, not each source color.\n#   - Placeholder row/column recovery assumes at least one filled cell in every logical row and\n#     column. The generator enforces that.\n#   - Region lookup assumes the top-left 5x5 area is reserved for the legend and does not overlap\n#     the main frame. The generator reserves that area before placing the frame.\n# placement_legality:\n#   - The legend panel is fixed at canvas coordinate (0,0).\n#   - The main frame is placed with `random_free_location` against a reserve mask that already\n#     blocks the legend panel, so frame and legend never overlap.\n#   - External sprite templates are placed afterward using the same reserve mask, so they stay\n#     separate from both the legend and the frame.\n# visual_observability:\n#   - The four legend entries are simple 2x2 solid blocks with distinct colors, making the spatial\n#     order obvious to a human.\n#   - Output recolor differences can be seen immediately because the same source-colored placeholder\n#     may turn into different colors when repeated across different quadrants.\n\n\ndef _find_frame(g: np.ndarray, bg: int) -> tuple[int, tuple[int, int, int, int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Find a rectangular border component:\n      - all bbox-border cells are this color,\n      - bbox-interior is not entirely this color.\n    Return (frame_color, (r0,c0,r1,c1)).\n    \"\"\"\n    candidates = []\n    colors = [int(c) for c in np.unique(g) if int(c) != bg]\n    for col in colors:\n        for pts in components_mask(g == col, connectivity=4):\n            r0, c0, r1, c1 = bbox_coords(pts)\n            if r1 - r0 < 2 or c1 - c0 < 2:\n                continue\n            sub = g[r0 : r1 + 1, c0 : c1 + 1]\n            border = np.zeros(sub.shape, dtype=bool)\n            border[0, :] = True\n            border[-1, :] = True\n            border[:, 0] = True\n            border[:, -1] = True\n            if not np.all(sub[border] == col):\n                continue\n            if np.all(sub[~border] == col):\n                continue\n            candidates.append((col, (r0, c0, r1, c1)))\n    assert len(candidates) == 1, f\"expected exactly one rectangular frame component, found {len(candidates)}\"\n    frame_col, bbox = candidates[0]\n    return int(frame_col), bbox\n\n\ndef _half_index(rank: int, count: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Map an ordered row/column rank to 0 (first half) or 1 (second half).\"\"\"\n    return 0 if int(rank) * 2 < int(count) else 1\n\n\ndef _read_position_legend(g: np.ndarray, bg: int) -> dict[tuple[int, int], int]:\n    \"\"\"Read the fixed 5x5 top-left position legend.\"\"\"\n    assert g.shape[0] >= 5 and g.shape[1] >= 5, \"grid too small for top-left legend\"\n    panel = g[:5, :5]\n    cross = np.ones((5, 5), dtype=bool)\n    cross[:2, :2] = False\n    cross[:2, 3:5] = False\n    cross[3:5, :2] = False\n    cross[3:5, 3:5] = False\n    assert np.all(panel[cross] == bg), \"position legend must have a background cross\"\n\n    mapping = {\n        (0, 0): int(panel[0, 0]),\n        (0, 1): int(panel[0, 3]),\n        (1, 0): int(panel[3, 0]),\n        (1, 1): int(panel[3, 3]),\n    }\n    for (rr, cc), col in mapping.items():\n        r0 = 0 if rr == 0 else 3\n        c0 = 0 if cc == 0 else 3\n        block = panel[r0 : r0 + 2, c0 : c0 + 2]\n        assert col != bg, \"legend entry cannot use background color\"\n        assert len(set(map(int, np.unique(block)))) == 1, \"legend entries must be solid 2x2 blocks\"\n    return mapping\n\n\ndef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"\n    Stamp external sprites into the frame, then recolor them by a spatial legend.\n\n    Input structure:\n    - The canvas background contains one gray rectangular frame with solid colored placeholders inside.\n    - The top-left corner of the whole canvas contains a fixed 2x2 legend panel made of four colored 2x2 squares.\n    - Outside the frame and outside that legend panel: one sprite template per placeholder color.\n\n    Rule:\n    - Detect the frame and recover the placeholder grid from the solid blocks inside it.\n    - For each placeholder color, fetch the matching-color sprite template from outside the frame.\n    - Stamp each sprite into its placeholder box, but choose the repaint color from the legend entry\n      indexed by the placeholder's relative position within the frame (upper/lower half and left/right half).\n\n    Key insight: The external sprite color still tells you which shape to place, but the final color is no\n    longer keyed by source color; it is chosen by where that placement sits inside the framed grid.\n    \"\"\"\n    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\n    bg = get_bg(g)\n\n    frame_col, (fr0, fc0, fr1, fc1) = _find_frame(g, bg)\n    assert fr0 >= 5 or fc0 >= 5, \"main frame overlaps the reserved top-left legend area\"\n    legend_map = _read_position_legend(g, bg)\n\n    crop = g[fr0 : fr1 + 1, fc0 : fc1 + 1]\n    H, W = crop.shape\n    assert H >= 3 and W >= 3, f\"frame too small for interior: {(H, W)}\"\n\n    inner_mask = np.zeros((H, W), dtype=bool)\n    inner_mask[1:-1, 1:-1] = True\n    placeholder_colors = set(map(int, np.unique(crop[inner_mask]))) - {bg, frame_col}\n    assert placeholder_colors, \"no placeholder colors found inside frame\"\n\n    placeholders: list[tuple[int, tuple[int, int, int, int]]] = []\n    for col in sorted(placeholder_colors):\n        for pts in components_mask((crop == col) & inner_mask, connectivity=4):\n            r0, c0, r1, c1 = bbox_coords(pts)\n            placeholders.append((col, (r0, c0, r1, c1)))\n\n    phw: dict[int, tuple[int, int]] = {}\n    for col in placeholder_colors:\n        dims = [(b[2] - b[0] + 1, b[3] - b[1] + 1) for c, b in placeholders if c == col]\n        assert dims, f\"no placeholder component found for color {col}\"\n        unique_dims = sorted(set(dims))\n        assert len(unique_dims) == 1, f\"ambiguous placeholder sizes for color {col}: {unique_dims}\"\n        phw[col] = unique_dims[0]\n\n    row_origins = sorted({b[0] for _, b in placeholders})\n    col_origins = sorted({b[1] for _, b in placeholders})\n    assert len(row_origins) >= 2 and len(col_origins) >= 2, \"need at least a 2x2 placement grid\"\n    row_rank = {r0: i for i, r0 in enumerate(row_origins)}\n    col_rank = {c0: i for i, c0 in enumerate(col_origins)}\n\n    outside = np.ones(g.shape, dtype=bool)\n    outside[fr0 : fr1 + 1, fc0 : fc1 + 1] = False\n    outside[:5, :5] = False\n\n    comps = []\n    colors = [int(c) for c in np.unique(g) if int(c) not in (bg, frame_col)]\n    for col in colors:\n        for pts in components_mask((g == col) & outside, connectivity=4):\n            r0, c0, r1, c1 = bbox_coords(pts)\n            pts_tuples = [(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in pts]\n            comps.append(\n                {\n                    \"col\": int(col),\n                    \"pts\": pts_tuples,\n                    \"bbox\": (r0, c0, r1, c1),\n                }\n            )\n\n    sprite_coords: dict[int, tuple[tuple[tuple[int, int], ...], int, int]] = {}\n    for src_col in sorted(placeholder_colors):\n        all_candidates = [c for c in comps if c[\"col\"] == src_col]\n        assert all_candidates, f\"no external sprite found for color {src_col}\"\n        want_h, want_w = phw[src_col]\n        sized = [\n            c\n            for c in all_candidates\n            if (c[\"bbox\"][2] - c[\"bbox\"][0] + 1) == want_h and (c[\"bbox\"][3] - c[\"bbox\"][1] + 1) == want_w\n        ]\n        assert len(sized) == 1, f\"expected one size-matched sprite for color {src_col}, found {len(sized)}\"\n        base = sized[0]\n        sr0, sc0, sr1, sc1 = base[\"bbox\"]\n        pts_set = set(base[\"pts\"])\n        for c in all_candidates:\n            if c is base:\n                continue\n            r0, c0, r1, c1 = c[\"bbox\"]\n            assert sr0 <= r0 and sr1 >= r1 and sc0 <= c0 and sc1 >= c1, (\n                f\"extra sprite component for color {src_col} is outside the base bbox\"\n            )\n            pts_set.update(c[\"pts\"])\n        coords = tuple(sorted((r - sr0, c - sc0) for r, c in pts_set))\n        sprite_coords[src_col] = (coords, sr1 - sr0 + 1, sc1 - sc0 + 1)\n\n    out = crop.copy()\n    out[1:-1, 1:-1] = bg\n\n    for src_col, (pr0, pc0, pr1, pc1) in placeholders:\n        assert src_col in sprite_coords, f\"placeholder color {src_col} missing sprite\"\n        row_side = _half_index(row_rank[pr0], len(row_origins))\n        col_side = _half_index(col_rank[pc0], len(col_origins))\n        tgt_col = legend_map[(row_side, col_side)]\n        coords, sh, sw = sprite_coords[src_col]\n        assert (pr1 - pr0 + 1, pc1 - pc0 + 1) == (sh, sw), (\n            f\"placeholder size does not match sprite for color {src_col}\"\n        )\n        assert pr0 + sh <= H and pc0 + sw <= W, f\"sprite for color {src_col} does not fit at placeholder\"\n        for dr, dc in coords:\n            out[pr0 + dr, pc0 + dc] = tgt_col\n\n    return out\n\n\n# --------------- generator (o5x) ---------------\n\n# === CFG: tunables ===\nFRAME_COL = 5\nSPRITE_N_RANGE = (3, 6)\nGRID_ROWS_RANGE = (2, 4)\nGRID_COLS_RANGE = (3, 5)\nTOTAL_BLOCKS_RANGE = (6, 10)\nMAX_EMPTY_SLOTS = 2\nNUM_COLORS_RANGE = (2, 5)\nSPRITE_FILL_MIN = 0.5\nSPRITE_FILL_MAX = 0.9\nMIN_FRAME_H = 13\nMIN_FRAME_W = 18\nMAX_FRAME_DIM = 21\nFRAME_MARGIN_SLACK = 4\nCANVAS_H_RANGE = (22, 31)\nCANVAS_W_RANGE = (23, 31)\nPATCH_PADDING = 1\nGEN_RETRIES = 300\nLEGEND_SIZE = 5\nLEGEND_BLOCK = 2\n\n\ndef _slot_region(slot: tuple[int, int], rows: int, cols: int) -> tuple[int, int]:\n    rr, cc = slot\n    return (_half_index(rr, rows), _half_index(cc, cols))\n\n\ndef _position_legend(region_to_tgt: dict[tuple[int, int], int], bg: int) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Build the fixed 5x5 top-left legend panel.\"\"\"\n    panel = np.full((LEGEND_SIZE, LEGEND_SIZE), bg, dtype=int)\n    panel[:LEGEND_BLOCK, :LEGEND_BLOCK] = region_to_tgt[(0, 0)]\n    panel[:LEGEND_BLOCK, 3:5] = region_to_tgt[(0, 1)]\n    panel[3:5, :LEGEND_BLOCK] = region_to_tgt[(1, 0)]\n    panel[3:5, 3:5] = region_to_tgt[(1, 1)]\n    return panel\n\n\ndef _sprite_mask(n: int) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Generate a random NxN binary mask with fill ratio in [SPRITE_FILL_MIN, SPRITE_FILL_MAX].\"\"\"\n    lo = max((n * n + 1) // 2, int(np.ceil(SPRITE_FILL_MIN * n * n)))\n    hi = min(int(np.floor(SPRITE_FILL_MAX * n * n)), n * n - 1)\n    target = random.randint(lo, hi)\n\n    mask = np.zeros((n, n), dtype=bool)\n    c = random.randrange(n)\n    for r in range(n):\n        c = max(0, min(n - 1, c + random.choice([-1, 0, 1])))\n        mask[r, c] = True\n    mask[random.randrange(n), :] = True\n\n    if random.random() < 0.5:\n        mask = mask.T.copy()\n    if random.random() < 0.5:\n        mask = np.flipud(mask)\n    if random.random() < 0.5:\n        mask = np.fliplr(mask)\n\n    while int(mask.sum()) < target:\n        dilated = np.zeros_like(mask)\n        dilated[1:, :] |= mask[:-1, :]\n        dilated[:-1, :] |= mask[1:, :]\n        dilated[:, 1:] |= mask[:, :-1]\n        dilated[:, :-1] |= mask[:, 1:]\n        frontier = list(zip(*np.where(dilated & ~mask)))\n        r, c = random.choice(frontier)\n        mask[r, c] = True\n    return mask\n\n\ndef _colored_sprite(mask: np.ndarray, color: int, bg: int) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Render a�合描述」和「各组成项详情」，将融合规则落实到代码层面。融合描述给出了整体的 input→output 规则，各组成项详情给出了每项改动的具体含义——两者结合才是完整的实现规格。如果上面提供了原始任务规格（Spec），请将其作为设计分析的重要参考——spec 详细描述了原始任务中各对象的结构、空间关系、生成策略等，理解这些细节有助于你准确判断融合改动的影响范围和实现方式。\n\n       a) **具体化与行为追踪**: 融合后的变体在 ARC 的像素网格中具体长什么样？用一个具体小例子追踪：原始逻辑在每个被改动的环节是怎么执行的 → 融合后应该怎么执行的 → 二者的差异是什么。\n\n       b) **复杂度校准**: 检查你的设计是否过于简化。过于简化会导致两个问题：一是容易产生冲突或重复（例如不同对象变得难以区分，匹配出现歧义），二是变体的视觉效果不明显，肉眼看不出和原任务的区别。同时不要让关键自由度过多；如果规则依赖少数档位、类别或对应关系，应控制在少量取值，并让它们在每个样例中有重复支撑。\n\n       c) **隐式假设审查**: 各组成项的改动可能破坏原代码中的哪些隐式假设？多项改动叠加后是否引入新的冲突？逐行检查 main() 中与变体相关的代码段：每行代码依赖了什么前提？这个前提在融合后是否仍然成立？\n\n       d) **放置合法性**: 生成器在放置对象时，必须保证各个体之间不重叠、不越界，且放置结果符合题意。\n\n       e) **视觉可观察性**: ARC 要求人类从 2-4 个 input→output 样例中肉眼推断规则。禁止使用任何人类不可视因素参与排序等操作（例如黑色=0，禁用）。做一次思想实验：假设你是解题者，看到几组变体生成的 input→output，能否看出融合后的规则？注意不要使用颜色值等人类不可视因素。如果变体的变化规律在2-3组像素网格上无法推出（例如对大量纯色对称对象做不同变换、无法从少量例子归纳颜色对应关系、不同情况的变换涉及正逆向旋转镜像等多种不同变化等，即全部的变化逻辑或者说是变化规律无法在3个输入输出示例对中体现），就需要调整设计使差异可观察。\n\n       f) **可视化整洁度**: 即使逻辑合理，如果可视化后的输出网格看上去乱七八糟也不行。检查：同一网格区域是否存在多种元素覆盖叠加导致无法分辨哪个是哪个？不同对象、区域、标记之间在视觉上是否能清晰区分？如果融合后的网格在视觉上杂乱不堪，需要调整设计（如减少同一区域的叠加层次、增大对象间距、简化标记方式等）。\n\n       g) **变化的可推断性**: 如果融合涉及颜色映射或颜色变化，务必确保颜色种类不宜过多，且颜色变化必须有足够的结构性线索（如位置、形状、分区等伴随特征）让人类能从少量样例中推断出颜色变化规则。避免出现大量颜色变化却无任何提示的情况——如果解题者无法从样例归纳出\"什么条件导致什么颜色\"，这个融合设计就\n\n       将以上分析写在代码注释中或输出中，然后再开始写代码。\n\n    4. **修改 `main()`**: 按照融合描述和各组成项详情实现新规则。确保各项改动在推理链中有真正的协同，不是各改各的。\n    5. **修改 `generate_input()`**: 确保生成的输入能正确触发融合后的新规则。\n    6. **保证 generator 的正确性**: 沿用 output-first 模式或适当调整，但必须保证每个输入经过新 `main()` 后不崩溃、不触发 assert、输出正确。\n    7. **测试**: 运行以下测试，确保成功率 ≥ 80%:\n\n    ```bash\n    /home/xd/miniconda3/bin/python -c \"\n    import numpy as np, importlib.util, time, sys\n    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('variant', '/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/15/code.py')\n    mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n    spec.loader.exec_module(mod)\n    ok, fail = 0, 0\n    t0 = time.time()\n    for i in range(50):\n        try:\n            inp = mod.generate_input()\n            out = mod.main(inp)\n            ok += 1\n        except Exception as e:\n            fail += 1\n            if fail <= 3: print(f'Trial {i}: {e}')\n    elapsed = time.time() - t0\n    print(f'Success: {ok}/50, Time: {elapsed:.1f}s ({elapsed/50*1000:.0f}ms/call)')\n    if ok < 40: sys.exit(1)\n    \"\n    ```\n\n    如果测试失败，分析错误原因，修改代码，重新测试。反复直到通过。\n\n    8. **验证融合行为确实发生**: `main(input)==output` 只能验证求解器不报错，无法验证输入是否真正体现了融合描述中的特征行为——退化为原始行为的输入同样能通过。测试通过后，定义一个量化指标衡量融合核心行为，统计生成样本中该指标的分布。只有当关键控制变量不起作用、样本按融合逻辑执行与按原逻辑执行在相同输入上输出相同结果时，才算退化并需要修正生成器。\n    9. **审查 `main()` 的新隐式假设**: 修改 `main()` 后，它可能对输入产生原始版本中不存在的新假设（如对象间需特定空间关系、匹配特征需可区分、处理顺序依赖前一步结果等）。逐一检查 `main()` 中的每个循环、匹配和条件分支：这段逻辑对输入做了什么假设？`generate_input()` 是否通过构造保证了这些假设？\n\n    ## 参考资源\n    - `/home/lixinyu/snap/new/solvers/arc_utils.py` — 可用的工具函数\n    - `/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC-data/ARC-AGI-2/data/evaluation/edb79dae.json` — 原任务的 I/O 样例\n\n    ## 输出\n\n    将完整的融合变体代码（包含修改后的 `main()` 和 `generate_input()`）保存到:\n    `/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/edb79dae/15/code.py`\n\n    代码文件开头加一段注释说明这是什么融合变体:\n    ```python\n    # Combo variant of edb79dae (index 15)\n    # combo_spec: D2/3+D7/0